{"abstract":"The electrochemical conversion of CO2 into acetaldehyde offers a sustainable and green alternative to the Wacker process. However, current electrocatalysts cannot effectively compete with heterogeneous processes owing to their limited selectivity towards acetaldehyde, resulting in low energy efficiencies. Here we report a theory-guided synthesis of a series of Cu-cluster catalysts (~1.6 nm) immobilized on various heteroatom-doped carbonaceous supports, produced via spark ablation of Cu electrodes (2.6 μg h−1 production rate, 6 Wh energy consumption). These catalysts achieve acetaldehyde selectivity of up to 92% at only 600 mV from the equilibrium potential. In addition, the catalysts exhibit exceptional catalytic stability during a rigorous 30 h stress test involving three repeated start–stop cycles. In situ X-ray absorption spectroscopy reveals that the initial oxide clusters were completely reduced under cathodic potential and maintained their metallic nature even after exposure to air, explaining the stable performance of the catalyst. First-principles simulations further elucidate a possible mechanism of CO2 conversion to acetaldehyde. (Figure presented.)","author_count":16,"contributors":["Koolen, Cedric David","Pedersen, Jack K.","Zijlstra, Bernardus","Winzely, Maximilian","Zhang, Jie","Pfeiffer, Tobias V.","Vrijburg, Wilbert","Li, Mo","Agarwal, Ayush","Akbari, Zohreh","Kuddusi, Yasemen","Herranz, Juan","Safonova, Olga V.","Schmidt-Ott, Andreas","Luo, Wen","Zuettel, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809456"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Netherlands","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","ETH Zürich","Paul Scherrer Institute","Shanghai University","Swiss Federal Laboratories for Materials Science and Technology (Empa)","VSParticle B.V.","École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scalable synthesis of cu cluster catalysts via spark ablation for the electrochemical conversion of co sub 000000000002 sub to acetaldehyde","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-809456","identifier":[{"id":"85214125835","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3344de08-12a0-4ef1-8e2e-686c63590ad6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC291B92349EE21262B2D1BFEFFF14B9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal laboratories for materials science and technology","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Laboratories for Materials Science and Technology (Empa)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"vsparticle b v","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"VSParticle B.V.","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"paul scherrer institute","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Paul Scherrer Institute","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"ch","key":"école polytechnique fédérale de lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology