{"abstract":"The Martini model is a popular force field for coarse-grained simulations. Membranes have always been at the center of its development, with the latest version, Martini 3, showing great promise in capturing more and more realistic behavior. In this chapter we provide a step-by-step tutorial on how to construct starting configurations, run initial simulations and perform dedicated analysis for membrane-based systems of increasing complexity, including leaflet asymmetry, curvature gradients and embedding of membrane proteins.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ozturk, Tugba Nur","König, Melanie","Carpenter, Timothy S.","Pedersen, Kasper B","Wassenaar, Tsjerk A.","Ingólfsson, Helgi I.","Marrink, Siewert J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-737957"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ingólfsson, Helgi I.","Marrink, Siewert J."],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hanze University of Applied Sciences","Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory","University of Groningen"],"keyword":["Complex membranes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"building complex membranes with martini 000000000003","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85189959416","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-737957","identifier":[{"id":"39025573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85189959416","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fadd9fdd-f9fa-4fbb-b5e5-bc0ee83a2b27"],"keyword":["Asymmetrical membranes","Complex membranes","Curved membranes","Embedding proteins in membranes","Leaflet asymmetry","Martini 3","Membrane set up"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-55F875ED163F8D61E383D63F21926914"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"lawrence livermore national laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"hanze university of applied sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hanze University of Applied Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tugba Nur","key":"ozturkpau","last":"Ozturk","name":"Ozturk, Tugba Nur","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"königpau","last":"König","name":"König, Melanie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Timothy S.","key":"carpenterpau","last":"Carpenter","name":"Carpenter, Timothy S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper B.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8a1d4f37-0eee-4288-aa56-9382c368dc30","name":"Pedersen, Kasper B","name_org":"Pedersen, Kasper B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tsjerk A.","key":"wassenaarpau","last":"Wassenaar","name":"Wassenaar, Tsjerk A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helgi I.","key":"ingólfssonpau","last":"Ingólfsson","name":"Ingólfsson, Helgi I.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Siewert J.","key":"marrinkpau","last":"Marrink","name":"Marrink, Siewert J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Markus","key":"desernopedh","last":"Deserno","name":"Deserno, Markus","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"baumgartpedh","last":"Baumgart","name":"Baumgart, Tobias","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pmid":["39025573"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/bs.mie.2024.03.010","isbn":["9780443295669"],"issn":["00766879"],"pages":"237-285","publisher":"Academic Press","series":"Methods in Enzymology","status":"p","subtitle":"Part B: Theory and Simulations","title":"Biophysical Approaches for the Study of Membrane Structure","volume":"701"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189959416"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fadd9fdd-f9fa-4fbb-b5e5-bc0ee83a2b27"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Building complex membranes with Martini 3","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-737957","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Barley, a vital cereal crop worldwide, is hindered by hordeins, gluten proteins triggering adverse reactions in those with celiac disease (CeD) and non-celiac gluten sensitivity (NCGS). Recent barley breeding advancements focus on creating varieties with reduced hordein content. Researchers have developed ultra-low gluten barley mutants via targeted genetic modifications, showing significantly decreased hordein levels, potentially safe for CeD and NCGS individuals. However, some mutants carry undesirable traits, which are addressed through further breeding and new genomic techniques. These innovative methods offer promising ways to eliminate unwanted traits and transfer the ultra-low gluten characteristic to diverse barley cultivars, expanding dietary choices and potentially transforming the food and beverage industry with gluten-free barley-based products. This review addresses hordeins' impact and ultra-low gluten barley development and proposes using new genomic techniques for safe barley lines.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hanak, Tobias","Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","Hebelstrup, Kim","Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-762996"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hanak, Tobias"],"keyword":["Barley","Breeding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"barley s gluten challenge a path to hordein free food and malt","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.plaphy.2024.109174","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-762996","identifier":[{"id":"39362126","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85205385118","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-476e9e43-60a8-49a9-a76c-98bede11492b"],"keyword":["Barley","Breeding","Hordeins","New genomic techniques (NGT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-39A480E39F1DDFF81702F6755864DBF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/419926575/1-s2.0-S0981942824008428-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.plaphy.2024.109174","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"hanakpau","last":"Hanak","locid":"d1eec89c-eeb2-4337-adcc-79cf10e2d519","name":"Hanak, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-2913-9893","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olga A.","key":"andrzejczakpau","last":"Andrzejczak","locid":"591d74a1-7fcc-477e-a5e1-5edefd34ade0","name":"Andrzejczak, Olga Agata","name_org":"Andrzejczak, Olga A.","orcid":"0000-0002-5178-5229","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"hebelstruppau","last":"Hebelstrup","locid":"e20721de-154d-42bf-b85a-114d8097fbbf","name":"Hebelstrup, Kim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"brinchpedersenpau","last":"Brinch-Pedersen","locid":"b99acfd4-b212-450a-86a8-0d91eb9c1a15","name":"Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9773-8903","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39362126"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.plaphy.2024.109174","issn":["09819428","18732690"],"issn_org":["09819428"],"journal":"Plant Physiology and Biochemistry","paperid":"109174","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Plant Physiology and Biochemistry","volume":"216"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205385118"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-476e9e43-60a8-49a9-a76c-98bede11492b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Barley's gluten challenge : A path to hordein-free food and malt","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-762996","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Bioethanol is a sustainable energy alternative and can contribute to global greenhouse-gas emission reductions by over 60%. Its industrial production faces various bottlenecks, including sub-optimal efficiency resulting from bacteria. Broad-spectrum removal of these contaminants results in negligible gains, suggesting that the process is shaped by ecological interactions within the microbial community. Here, we survey the microbiome across all process steps at two biorefineries, over three timepoints in a production season. Leveraging shotgun metagenomics and cultivation-based approaches, we identify beneficial bacteria and find improved outcome when yeast-to-bacteria ratios increase during fermentation. We provide a microbial gene catalogue which reveals bacteria-specific pathways associated with performance. We also show that Limosilactobacillus fermentum overgrowth lowers production, with one strain reducing yield by ~5% in laboratory fermentations, potentially due to its metabolite profile. Temperature is found to be a major driver for strain-level dynamics. Improved microbial management strategies could unlock environmental and economic gains in this US $ 60 billion industry enabling its wider adoption.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Senne de Oliveira Lino, Felipe","Garg, Shilpa","Li, Simone S.","Misiakou, Maria-Anna","Kang, Kang","Vale da Costa, Bruno Labate","Beyer-Pedersen, Tobias Svend Aage","Giacon, Thamiris Guerra","Basso, Thiago Olitta","Panagiotou, Gianni","Sommer, Morten Otto Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-775121"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Sommer, Morten Otto Alexander"],"country":["Australia","Brazil","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Institute for Natural Product Research and Infection Biology - Hans Knöll Institute","Leibniz-Institute for Natural Product Research and Infection Biology","Universidade Estadual de Campinas","Universidade de São Paulo","University of Queensland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"strain dynamics of contaminating bacteria modulate the yield of ethanol biorefineries","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49683-2","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to acknowledge Marcos Vin\\u00EDcius, Thais Gran\\u00E7o and Rafael Alves for their support on acquiring industrial samples and metadata, and Prof. Dr. Adriano Azzoni and Prof. Dr. Ren\\u00E9 Schneider for providing access to laboratory equipment for processing industrial samples. We acknowledge the support of Georges Neto on the processing of samples from the first sampling time point batch. The authors would also like to thank Oleksandr M. Maistrenko for constructive discussions. The research was supported by funding from The Novo Nordisk Foundation under NFF grant number: NNF10CC1016517 (F.S.O.L., M.O.A.S.). S.S.L. acknowledges support by the European Molecular Biology Organisation (ALTF 137-2018) and National Health and Medical Research Council of Australia (APP1166180). T.O.B. acknowledges funding from S\\u00E3o Paulo Research Foundation (FAPESP), grants #2015/50684-9 and #2018/17172-2, and \\u201CINCT Yeasts: Biodiversity, preservation, and biotechnological innovation\\u201D, funded by Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Cient\\u00EDfico e Tecnol\\u00F3gico (CNPq), grant #406564/2022-1."],"id":"S01-000.00-775121","identifier":[{"id":"38909053","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85196651256","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11193817","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-28e2fb67-a8b0-453e-96e3-b1028df63a43"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-821C4DB344D4675E3E96666C1FF57AAD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/379775660/s41467-024-49683-2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49683-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Biosustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for natural product research and infection biology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz-Institute for Natural Product Research and Infection Biology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"br","key":"universidade estadual de campinas","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Estadual de Campinas","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"br","key":"universidade de são paulo","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade de São Paulo","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for natural product research and infection biology hans knöll institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Natural Product Research and Infection Biology - Hans Knöll Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Felipe Senne","key":"deoliveiralinopau","last":"de Oliveira Lino","locid":"16c20ecf-4be6-40fa-8b9b-2f0abfa156d8","name":"Senne de Oliveira Lino, Felipe","name_org":"de Oliveira Lino, Felipe Senne","orcid":"0000-0001-5645-9142","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shilpa","key":"gargpau","last":"Garg","locid":"4c0968e3-7694-46fa-9b8d-10aa98e5c2a4","name":"Garg, Shilpa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simone S.","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"ef9e08b4-faf9-432b-9912-731c8a61ad3e","name":"Li, Simone S.","orcid":"0000-0002-0073-3656","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maria Anna","key":"misiakoupau","last":"Misiakou","locid":"88b2ca83-9b8c-4475-9012-21240c3ec05d","name":"Misiakou, Maria-Anna","name_org":"Misiakou, Maria Anna","orcid":"0000-0002-9965-4164","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kang","key":"kangpau","last":"Kang","name":"Kang, Kang","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Bruno Labate","key":"valedacostapau","last":"Vale da Costa","name":"Vale da Costa, Bruno Labate","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Svend Aage","key":"beyerpedersenpau","last":"Beyer-Pedersen","locid":"396f3a7a-6d34-415b-b1a6-1af9008f3d04","name":"Beyer-Pedersen, Tobias Svend Aage","orcid":"0009-0002-2769-5570","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thamiris Guerra","key":"giaconpau","last":"Giacon","name":"Giacon, Thamiris Guerra","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Thiago Olitta","key":"bassopau","last":"Basso","name":"Basso, Thiago Olitta","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianni","key":"panagiotoupau","last":"Panagiotou","name":"Panagiotou, Gianni","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Otto Alexander","key":"sommerpau","last":"Sommer","locid":"923149b6-ae3b-461c-9c11-c65100ec1c82","name":"Sommer, Morten Otto Alexander","orcid":"0000-0003-4005-5674","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38909053"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-49683-2","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"5323","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196651256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-28e2fb67-a8b0-453e-96e3-b1028df63a43"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Strain dynamics of contaminating bacteria modulate the yield of ethanol biorefineries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-775121","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The MarineBasis Nuuk Monitoring Programme has performed monthly sampling of hydrography, water chemistry and phytoplankton in Nuup Kangerlua for over 15 years, which may not capture changes in phytoplankton communities occurring at shorter time windows. Likewise, the sampling location is limited to a single station which may not cover the patchy phytoplankton distribution. Here, we investigate the performance of Sentinel-3 (S3) chlorophyll-a (Chl-a) estimates (2016-2022) in relation to in situ data collected in Nuup Kangerlua with the aim to use S3 data to increase both spatial and temporal coverage. Overall, the S3 estimates were significantly correlated with the in situ measurements, with a few exceptions: during spring, when in situ measurements report the highest Chl-a values that are underestimated by S3; and during late-summer and autumn, when Chl-a values are low but with an overestimation by S3, likely due to the presence of glacier flour (silt) in the water.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gonçalves-Araujo, Rafael","Stedmon, Colin","Vonnahme, Tobias R.","López-Blanco, Efrén","Juul-Pedersen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-729961"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-25","place":"Lyngby, dk","start":"2024-01-23","title":"22. Danske Havforskermøde","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"monitoring phytoplankton dynamics in nuup kangerlua with ocean color remote","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://havforsker2024.dtu.dk/abstract-book","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-729961","ids":["dtu-c27e4a53-22e3-4987-9f60-2ad9b66b63b6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A01F5FD07C2E56BCA074220BAB48A53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://havforsker2024.dtu.dk/abstract-book","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Oceans and Arctic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rafael","key":"gonçalvesaraujopau","last":"Gonçalves-Araujo","locid":"374df3b0-b1fc-4832-aacc-dfdbc8315445","name":"Gonçalves-Araujo, Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-8344-8326","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Colin","key":"stedmonpau","last":"Stedmon","locid":"b85e3ce9-7777-4d9e-807d-aba8f30607e1","name":"Stedmon, Colin","orcid":"0000-0001-6642-9692","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias R.","key":"vonnahmepau","last":"Vonnahme","name":"Vonnahme, Tobias R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Efrén","key":"lópezblancopau","last":"López-Blanco","name":"López-Blanco, Efrén","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"juulpedersenpau","last":"Juul-Pedersen","name":"Juul-Pedersen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"6-6","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","title":"22. Danske Havforskermøde Abstract book"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c27e4a53-22e3-4987-9f60-2ad9b66b63b6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Monitoring phytoplankton dynamics in Nuup Kangerlua with ocean color remote","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-729961","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Conventional bulk protein structure determination methods are not suitable for understanding the distinct and diverse interactions of proteins with interfaces. Notably, interfacial activation is a feature common to many lipases involving movement of a helical \"lid\" region upon contact with a hydrophobic surface to expose the catalytic site. Here we use the surface specificity of vibrational sum frequency generation spectroscopy (VSFG) spectroscopy to directly probe the conformation of Thermomyces lanuginosus lipase (TLL) at hydrophobic interfaces. The TLL-catalyzed reaction at the air/water interface is monitored by VSFG spectroscopy, showing loss of ester carbonyl modes and appearance of carboxylate stretching modes of the fatty acid products. Furthermore, comparison of experimental and calculated VSFG spectra of the amide I band of TLL allows us to discern the subtle structural changes involved with lid-opening at a hydrophobic surface. Finally, we report a likely orientation of this lid-open state, which interacts with the surface through a loop region away from the lid and active site. This experimental framework for probing protein structure and function at interfaces addresses a significant problem in protein science that is not only impeding the design of better enzymes for biotechnology applications but also drug discovery targeting membrane associated proteins.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Saeed, Khezar H","Strunge, Kris","Pedersen, Kasper B","Truelsen, Sigurd F","Christensen, Sune M","Olsen, Lars","Schiøtt, Birgit","Weidner, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-758188"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Weidner, Tobias"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigating lipase stain interactions determining interfacial protein conformation with surface spectroscopy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85201697678","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-758188","identifier":[{"id":"39158521","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85201697678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-889a662e-9d05-4cb7-86ab-a75f5edf2db1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8E48C8E221D765D00746FA8D0D430AB8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novonesis","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOSI","l3nn":"Novonesis","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novonesis","namevar":["Novonesis A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Khezar H","key":"saeedpau","last":"Saeed","locid":"3d8392ab-a46b-4f6b-80ef-802ed5c12fe9","name":"Saeed, Khezar H","orcid":"0000-0001-7207-9836","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kris","key":"strungepau","last":"Strunge","locid":"e6d48eb1-e1c1-4958-b196-90a0cfdd2556","name":"Strunge, Kris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper B","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8a1d4f37-0eee-4288-aa56-9382c368dc30","name":"Pedersen, Kasper B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sigurd F","key":"truelsenpau","last":"Truelsen","name":"Truelsen, Sigurd F","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sune M","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Sune M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"schiøttpau","last":"Schiøtt","locid":"27c1af35-c8f3-471f-a448-02fd2fbd18bf","name":"Schiøtt, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0001-9937-1562","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"weidnerpau","last":"Weidner","locid":"7a001432-fe35-4c21-b32c-40a65e060b03","name":"Weidner, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-7083-7004","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39158521"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jpcb.4c03173","issn":["15205207","15206106"],"issn_org":["15206106"],"issue":"34","journal":"Journal of Physical Chemistry Part B: Condensed Matter, Materials, Surfaces, Interfaces & Biophysical","pages":"8162-8169","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Physical Chemistry Part B: Condensed Matter, Materials, Surfaces, Interfaces & Biophysical","title_org":"The journal of physical chemistry. B","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201697678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-889a662e-9d05-4cb7-86ab-a75f5edf2db1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Investigating Lipase/Stain Interactions : Determining Interfacial Protein Conformation with Surface Spectroscopy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-758188","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Speech intelligibility decreases at high presentation levels – so-called rollover – have been observed for both normal-hearing (NH) and hearing-impaired (HI) individuals. In this project, rollover was assessed with speech intelligibility and psychoacoustic measurements at three moderate-to-high levels. For the speech intelligibility measurements, sentences from the Dagmar, Asta, Tine (DAT) corpus were presented against either stationary speech-shaped noise (SSN) or the International Speech Test Signal (ISTS). For the psychoacoustic measurements, the Audible Contrast Threshold (ACT) test was used. Both NH and HI participants were tested (N = 18). For both participant groups, a tendency for rollover in the speech intelligibility measurements was observed. For the HI group, the performance decrease was significant with the ISTS masker. No rollover was found in the ACT measurements. The NH group outperformed the HI group in terms of both speech intelligibility and ACT scores. The NH group also performed better with the ISTS masker than with the SSN masker, whereas the HI group did not. This could indicate that gap listening abilities were not preserved in the HI participants. A larger study sample is needed to test for the presence of rollover (or lack thereof) in the ACT measurements.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Emma Søndergaard","Rasmussen, Josephine Bach","Jürgensen, Lukas","Fereczkowski, Michal","Neher, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783405"],"event":{"end":"2024-11-12","place":"Stouby, dk","start":"2024-11-11","title":"Annual meeting of the Danish Technical Audiological Society","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Emma Søndergaard","Rasmussen, Josephine Bach"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rollover in normal hearing and hearing impaired individuals speech intelligibility and act measurements","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-783405","ids":["sdu-8b84e60d-74f6-4bbb-9a28-a11bf73b029b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7D879ECE0710E1EF24E17B823BB86DEF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Søndergaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5fcb52e2-1283-4263-8f2a-a4262c46e2ee","name":"Pedersen, Emma Søndergaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Josephine Bach","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3f432b0c-45a6-4b88-bfab-927d869a7195","name":"Rasmussen, Josephine Bach","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lukas","key":"jürgensenoth","last":"Jürgensen","locid":"4f0251ff-3279-4c9d-a5de-3a22583badaa","name":"Jürgensen, Lukas","orcid":"0009-0009-3747-9549","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michal","key":"fereczkowskioth","last":"Fereczkowski","locid":"15d94435-488e-4abe-9cdb-16a8aab5a93c","name":"Fereczkowski, Michal","orcid":"0000-0002-7960-1188","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"neheroth","last":"Neher","locid":"64d1ab37-25d0-4a4b-94d9-59d868d830db","name":"Neher, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1107-9274","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8b84e60d-74f6-4bbb-9a28-a11bf73b029b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Rollover in normal-hearing and hearing-impaired individuals: Speech intelligibility and ACT measurements","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783405","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Animal studies indicate that noise exposure may lead to cochlear synaptopathy, primarily affecting low-spontaneous-rate fibers in the auditory nerve. Consequently, it can be hypothesized that in humans, the effects of cochlear synaptopathy will be more pronounced for high-intensity stimuli compared to low-intensity ones. For instance, cochlear synaptopathy may result in a reduced strength of the middle-ear muscle reflex (MEMR), or poorer speech intelligibility (SI) at high presentation levels compared to low levels. Recently, Shehorn et al. (2020) (DOI: 10.1016/j.heares.2020.107982) has reported that lower speech recognition at very high input levels (104 dBA) were associated with reduced MEMR magnitude (measured with an advanced, research protocol), and the reduced MEMR magnitude was associated with higher estimated lifetime noise exposure. While that study focused on SI at single presentation levels, SI changes across levels can also be assessed. SI declines with increasing level, so-called rollover (RO), have been observed in individuals with normal hearing thresholds, and may also be CS-related. However, broadened auditory filters or a reduced ‘sharpness’ of the neural speech representation at higher levels could also lead to RO. Thus, RO occurrence in individuals with normal hearing thresholds does not necessarily indicate CS. Instead, ‘normal’ and ‘abnormal’ contributions to RO would need to be disentangled. Since there are currently no clinically established tools for detecting CS, this cannot be done a priori (e.g., by testing groups with and without CS and then comparing RO for the two groups). Instead, it can be hypothesized that in case of ‘abnormal’ contributions RO will be larger and correlated with other experimental measures, such as extended high-frequency audiometry, that presumably reflect CS, or MEMR strength. To test these hypotheses, we measured SI in speech-like noise presented at 65 and 80 dB SPL. in 25 young adults with normal hearing thresholds. Extended high-frequency audiometry, acoustic-reflex measurements, and structured interviews regarding noise exposure were also conducted, using clinically available protocols. The negative correlation between noise exposure history and MEMR strength was significant, and in a good agreement with Shehorn et al. Further, majority of the listeners showed some degree of RO (median RO = 9%). However, no simple relations were found between RO and other measures. We argue that the majority of the listeners were normal-hearing and thus the 9% median can be considered ‘normal’ RO. We expect to provide estimates of ‘normal’ RO magnitude and, based on the relations with the other experimental measures, to identify individuals with a high probability of abnormal RO and, thus, CS.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fereczkowski, Michal","Van Yper, Lindsey Nadine","Pedersen, Emma Søndergaard","Neher, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783583"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-27","start":"2024-09-26","title":"Auditory Science Meeting","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can rollover be used to assess cochlear synaptopathy in listeners with normal audiograms","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-783583","ids":["sdu-b0dde554-3de2-4bee-a4b3-a2ed726974a9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-408913C9AE341EE8AE5BBB7C925318D4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Oto Rhino Laryngology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michal","key":"fereczkowskipau","last":"Fereczkowski","locid":"15d94435-488e-4abe-9cdb-16a8aab5a93c","name":"Fereczkowski, Michal","orcid":"0000-0002-7960-1188","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lindsey Nadine","key":"vanyperpau","last":"Van Yper","locid":"b8c7d51a-2d18-452b-9a7b-848e25760b59","name":"Van Yper, Lindsey Nadine","orcid":"0000-0002-6062-0928","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma Søndergaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5fcb52e2-1283-4263-8f2a-a4262c46e2ee","name":"Pedersen, Emma Søndergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"neherpau","last":"Neher","locid":"64d1ab37-25d0-4a4b-94d9-59d868d830db","name":"Neher, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1107-9274","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b0dde554-3de2-4bee-a4b3-a2ed726974a9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Can rollover be used to assess cochlear synaptopathy in listeners with normal audiograms?","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783583","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"En antologi med fokus visioner for modernismens etageboliger (1930-1974). en række fagfolk, der alle har arbejdet med forholdet mellem bevaringshensyn og klimadagsorden, beskriver deres visioner for modernismens bygningskultur i en tid med øget fokus på klima og ressourcer","author_count":21,"contributors":["Høi, Arne","Jørgensen, Morten Birk","Jørgensen, Morten Birk","Høi, Arne","Braae, Ellen","Simonsen, Graves","Zeeberg, Lone","Nielsen, Pia","Andersen, Nicolai Bo","Ørsager, Morten","Bech-Nielsen, Grith","Boye, Anne Mette","Hentzer Dausgaard, Tobias","Martens Gudmand-Høyer, Sidse","Pedersen, Søren","Olesen, Christian","Fostved, Marie","Hübetz Larsen, Kasper","Festad Langdalen, Erik","Lindh, Tommi","Brogen, Thomas Waras"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-793100"],"event":{"end":"2024-04-19","place":"København, dk","start":"2024-04-19","title":"Lancering - Klimavisioner for modernismens bygningskultur","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Etageboliger","Klima"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-PR"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-RDKA","DI-PR-OTH"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"klimavisioner for modernismens bygningskultur etageboligbebyggelser 000000001930 000000001974","src":["arka","arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://realdania.dk/publikationer/faglige-publikationer/klimavisioner-for-modernismens-bygningskultur","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Realdan ia"],"id":"S02-100.00-793100","ids":["arka-75ab9972-13de-40cf-bc5a-9589af41883d","arkc-75ab9972-13de-40cf-bc5a-9589af41883d"],"keyword":["Etageboliger","Nej","klima","klimavisioner","kulturav",