{"abstract":"The Fusarium solani species complex (FSSC) is comprised of important pathogens of plants and humans. A distinctive feature of FSSC species is perithecial pigmentation. While the dark perithecial pigments of other Fusarium species are derived from fusarubins synthesized by polyketide synthase 3 (PKS3), the perithecial pigments of FSSC are derived from an unknown metabolite synthesized by PKS35. Here, we confirm in FSSC species Fusarium vanettenii that PKS35 (fsnI) is required for perithecial pigment synthesis by deletion analysis and that fsnI is closely related to phnA from Penicillium herquei, as well as duxI from Talaromyces stipentatus, which produce prephenalenone as an early intermediate in herqueinone and duclauxin synthesis respectively. The production of prephenalenone by expression of fsnI in Saccharomyces cerevisiae indicates that it is also an early intermediate in perithecial pigment synthesis. We next identified a conserved cluster of 10 genes flanking fsnI in F. vanettenii that when expressed in F. graminearum led to the production of a novel corymbiferan lactone F as a likely end product of the phenalenone biosynthetic pathway in FSSC.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Sørensen, Trine","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Westphal, Klaus Ringsborg","Fernandez de Quincoces, Lorena Diaz","Sondergaard, Teis Esben","Wimmer, Reinhard","Brown, Daren W.","Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"cuid":["S02-097.46-766538"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","United States Department of Agriculture"],"keyword":["Fusarium graminearum","Fusarium solani","Fusarium solani species complex","Gene cluster","Genetics","Heterologous expression","Natural compounds","Peritheical pigmentation","Pigments","Pigments Biological metabolism","Polyketides","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","polyketide synthase PKS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["University St. Peoria"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"final piece to the fusarium pigmentation puzzle unraveling of the phenalenone biosynthetic pathway responsible for perithecial pigmentation in the fusarium solani species complex","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fgb.2024.103912","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The research was supported by grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF15OC0016186 and NNF18OC0034952 ) and the Obel Family Foundation , Denmark. This research was also supported by the U.S. Department of Agriculture, Agricultural Research Service . Mention of trade names or commercial products in this publication is solely for the purpose of providing specific information and does not imply recommendation or endorsement by the U.S. Department of Agriculture . USDA is an equal opportunity provider and employer."],"id":"S02-097.46-766538","identifier":[{"id":"39004163","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85199022540","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1e2b086d-02fa-475f-ba8d-aa8fd162bd9c","sdu-34d0ca20-9675-44c9-b81f-66db5d3a0c08"],"keyword":["Corymbiferan lactone","Fusarium graminearum","Fusarium solani","Fusarium solani species complex","Fusarium vanettenii","Gene cluster","Heterologous expression","Natural compounds","Perithecia","Peritheical pigmentation","Pigments","Pigments, Biological/metabolism","Polyketides","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","genetics","polyketide synthase (PKS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E844562FC10BF05182483749F96C0C9D