37"],"issn_org":["10871845"],"journal":"Fungal Genetics and Biology","paperid":"103912","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Fungal Genetics and Biology","volume":"174"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199022540"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1e2b086d-02fa-475f-ba8d-aa8fd162bd9c","sdu-34d0ca20-9675-44c9-b81f-66db5d3a0c08"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Final piece to the Fusarium pigmentation puzzle – Unraveling of the phenalenone biosynthetic pathway responsible for perithecial pigmentation in the Fusarium solani species complex","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.46-766538","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to investigate whether focusing on and sharing positive listening experiences during hearing aid treatment affects speech intelligibility outcomes for experienced hearing aid users. Twenty experienced hearing aid users were randomly split into two groups, a positive focus (PF) group and a control group (N = 2 x 10). Prior to hearing aid fitting, all participants were asked to fill out the 12-item Speech Spatial & Qualities (SSQ12) questionnaire based on their listening experiences with their own hearing aids. At the first laboratory visit, they were fitted with study hearing aids, and completed speech intelligibility measurements in stationary speech-shaped noise (HINT) and competing speech (DAT). Both groups were asked to wear the study hearing aids for two weeks, and to send daily text messages reporting hours of hearing aid use to an experimenter. Additionally, the PF group was asked to focus on positive listening experiences throughout the day, and to report these in the same text messages. After the 2-week field trial, the SSQ12 questionnaire and the speech tests were repeated. The results showed that there was an improvement in HINT for the PF group but not the control group. This indicates that asking hearing aid users to focus on positive listening experiences and to share them can improve objective hearing aid outcomes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Line Louise Aaberg","Lelic, Dina","Pedersen, Anja Kofoed","Neher, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697107"],"event":{"end":"2023-10-28","place":"Stouby, dk","start":"2023-10-27","title":"Annual meeting of the Danish Technical Audiological Society (DTAS)","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Line Louise Aaberg"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of focusing on positive listening experiences on speech intelligibility in hearing aid users","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-697107","ids":["sdu-5cacd343-8443-40a8-8974-b22f5bd305b1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-426ED7D9F10DB970E15D702C6845DD4D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["WS Audiology A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Louise Aaberg","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5a8208bc-1931-418d-81ca-c8764bb5c8c4","name":"Nielsen, Line Louise Aaberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dina","key":"lelicpau","last":"Lelic","name":"Lelic, Dina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Kofoed","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anja Kofoed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"neherpau","last":"Neher","locid":"64d1ab37-25d0-4a4b-94d9-59d868d830db","name":"Neher, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1107-9274","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","ws audiology a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5cacd343-8443-40a8-8974-b22f5bd305b1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of focusing on positive listening experiences on speech intelligibility in hearing-aid users","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697107","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Fjord systems are transition zones between land and sea, resulting in complex and dynamic environments. They are of particular interest in the Arctic as they harbour ecosystems inhabited by a rich range of species and provide many societal benefits. The key drivers of change in the European Arctic (i.e., Greenland, Svalbard, and Northern Norway) fjord socio-ecological systems are reviewed here, structured into five categories: cryosphere (sea ice, glacier mass balance, and glacial and riverine discharge), physics (seawater temperature, salinity, and light), chemistry (carbonate system, nutrients), biology (primary production, biomass, and species richness), and social (governance, tourism, and fisheries). The data available for the past and present state of these drivers, as well as future model projections, are analysed in a companion paper. Changes to the two drivers at the base of most interactions within fjords, seawater temperature and glacier mass balance, will have the most significant and profound consequences on the future of European Arctic fjords. This is because even though governance may be effective at mitigating/adapting to local disruptions caused by the changing climate, there is possibly nothing that can be done to halt the melting of glaciers, the warming of fjord waters, and all of the downstream consequences that these two changes will have. This review provides the first transdisciplinary synthesis of the interactions between the drivers of change within Arctic fjord socio-ecological systems. Knowledge of what these drivers of change are, and how they interact with one another, should provide more expedient focus for future research on the needs of adapting to the changing Arctic.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Schlegel, Robert","Bartsch, Inka","Bischof, Kai","Bjørst, Lill Rastad","Dannevig, Halvor","Diehl, Nora","Duarte, Pedro","Hovelsrud, Grete K.","Juul-Pedersen, Thomas","Lebrun, Anaïs","Merillet, Laurène","Miller, Cale","Ren, Carina","Sejr, Mikael","Søreide, Janne E.","Vonnahme, Tobias R.","Gattuso, Jean-Pierre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-077977"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Greenland","Netherlands","Norway"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Institute of Marine Research","Nordland Research Institute","Norwegian Polar Institute","Sciences Po","Sorbonne Université","University Centre in Svalbard","University of Bergen","University of Bremen","Utrecht University","Western Norway Research Institute"],"keyword":["Arctic","Biology","Climate adaptation","Drivers of change","Ecosystem","Fjorde","Greenland","Humaniora","Social science"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drivers of change in arctic fjord socio ecological systems examples from the european arctic","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/cft.2023.1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-077977","identifier":[{"id":"85170370351","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-603ca776-8847-4171-bac8-5b9bc22c5b69"],"keyword":["Arctic","Biology","Climate adaptation","Drivers of change","Ecosystem","Fjorde","Greenland","humaniora","social science"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D38BD2EF4657EF949C57667FA81C74D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/547655749/div-class-title-drivers-of-change-in-arctic-fjord-socio-ecological-syste