{"abstract":"The purpose of the current study was to investigate whether focusing on positive listening experiences affects speech intelligibility outcomes in experienced hearing aid (HA) users. Twenty participants were randomly assigned to either a control group or a positive focus (PF) group (N = 2 x 10). Prior to HA fitting, all participants were asked to fill out the 12-item Speech Spatial & Qualities (SSQ12) questionnaire based on their listening experiences with their own HAs. At the first laboratory visit, they were fitted with study HAs, and speech intelligibility measurements in two noise scenarios were conducted. Both groups then wore the study HAs for two weeks and sent daily text messages reporting hours of HA use to an experimenter. During the 2-week trial period, the PF group was instructed to focus on positive listening experiences and to report them in the daily text messages. After the field trial, all participants filled out the SSQ12 questionnaire based on their experiences with the study HAs. In addition, they completed another round of speech intelligibility measurements. The analyses showed improved outcomes in terms of speech intelligibility in one noise scenario as well as average SSQ12 scores in the PF group but not in the control group. These results point to the importance of asking HA users to focus on positive listening experiences and to reflect upon them to improve both subjective and objective benefits following HA treatment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lelic, Dina","Nielsen, Line Louise Aaberg","Pedersen, Anja Kofoed","Neher, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-691338"],"event":{"end":"2023-08-25","place":"Nyborg, dk","start":"2023-08-23","title":"International Symposium on Auditory and Audiological Research","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lelic, Dina"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"focusing on positive listening experiences improves speech intelligibility in experienced hearing aid users","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-691338","ids":["sdu-c5564f84-868e-4086-b6c9-81f60a60d254"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0A563B3D677521455FBC265669296E03"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["WS Audiology A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dina","key":"lelicpau","last":"Lelic","name":"Lelic, Dina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Louise Aaberg","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"5a8208bc-1931-418d-81ca-c8764bb5c8c4","name":"Nielsen, Line Louise Aaberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Kofoed","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anja Kofoed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"neherpau","last":"Neher","locid":"64d1ab37-25d0-4a4b-94d9-59d868d830db","name":"Neher, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1107-9274","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","ws audiology a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c5564f84-868e-4086-b6c9-81f60a60d254"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Focusing On Positive Listening Experiences Improves Speech Intelligibility In Experienced Hearing Aid Users","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-691338","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The amyloid aggregation of α-synuclein (αS), related to Parkinson's disease, can be catalyzed by lipid membranes. Despite the importance of lipid surfaces, the 3D-structure and orientation of lipid-bound αS is still not known in detail. Here, we report interface-specific vibrational sum-frequency generation (VSFG) experiments that reveal how monomeric αS binds to an anionic lipid interface over a large range of αS-lipid ratios. To interpret the experimental data, we present a frame-selection method (\"ViscaSelect\") in which out-of-equilibrium molecular dynamics simulations are used to generate structural hypotheses that are compared to experimental amide-I spectra via excitonic spectral calculations. At low and physiological αS concentrations, we derive flat-lying helical structures as previously reported. However, at elevated and potentially disease-related concentrations, a transition to interface-protruding αS structures occurs. Such an upright conformation promotes lateral interactions between αS monomers and may explain how lipid membranes catalyze the formation of αS amyloids at elevated protein concentrations.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Roeters, Steven J.","Strunge, Kris","Pedersen, Kasper B","Golbek, Thaddeus W.","Bregnhøj, Mikkel","Zhang, Yuge","Wang, Yin","Dong, Mingdong","Nielsen, Janni","Otzen, Daniel E","Schiøtt, Birgit","Weidner, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694275"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Roeters, Steven J.","Weidner, Tobias"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","VU University Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Alpha synuclein","Amides","Amyloidogenic Proteins","Humans","Lipids","Parkinson Disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"elevated concentrations cause upright alpha synuclein conformation at lipid interfaces","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39843-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694275","identifier":[{"id":"37723164","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10507035","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85171548497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cb075929-4e74-4bf7-94ed-34db8b63c13a"],"keyword":["Amides","Amyloidogenic Proteins","Humans","Lipids","Parkinson Disease","alpha-Synuclein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D4252E4A76D4580A0FFC3600ED2261AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39843-1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"vu university amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"VU University Amsterdam","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven J","key":"roeterspau","last":"Roeters","locid":"c76b17db-0e9b-4988-b0e9-81012389655b","name":"Roeters, Steven J.","name_org":"Roeters, Steven J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kris","key":"strungepau","last":"Strunge","locid":"e6d48eb1-e1c1-4958-b196-90a0cfdd2556","name":"Strunge, Kris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper B","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8a1d4f37-0eee-4288-aa56-9382c368dc30","name":"Pedersen, Kasper B","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thaddeus W","key":"golbekpau","last":"Golbek","locid":"0fa79311-6553-451b-b607-7a5408d66af6","name":"Golbek, Thaddeus W.","name_org":"Golbek, Thaddeus W","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"bregnhøjpau","last":"Bregnhøj","locid":"60be394a-4fb2-4545-b2cc-42bc556a2abf","name":"Bregnhøj, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5748-6783","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuge","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"7c6513f4-1c35-4fd2-bdde-db8f6e17d42c","name":"Zhang, Yuge","orcid":"0000-0002-1956-416X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yin","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"be255a8d-609e-4fd6-b5d9-9e25b49c8ff4","name":"Wang, Yin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mingdong","key":"dongpau","last":"Dong","locid":"b54afe28-ba86-4353-9f09-6618abd83284","name":"Dong, Mingdong","orcid":"0000-0002-2025-2171","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janni","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"f8b802f3-e9d1-431f-9a1b-160e2d0254fb","name":"Nielsen, Janni","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel E","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","locid":"0ec06c22-1f74-4dd2-a894-af30b6565766","name":"Otzen, Daniel E","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birgit","key":"schiøttpau","last":"Schiøtt","locid":"27c1af35-c8f3-471f-a448-02fd2fbd18bf","name":"Schiøtt, Birgit","orcid":"0000-0001-9937-1562","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"weidnerpau","last":"Weidner","locid":"7a001432-fe35-4c21-b32c-40a65e060b03","name":"Weidner, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-7083-7004","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37723164"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-023-39843-1","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"5731","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171548497"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cb075929-4e74-4bf7-94ed-34db8b63c13a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Elevated concentrations cause upright alpha-synuclein conformation at lipid interfaces","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694275","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This review paper is the first to collect and synthesise the available knowledge, across various disciplines, on the importance of wintertime freshwater inflow from tidewater glaciers into Arctic fjords. While surface melt is limited during winter, tidewater glaciers can continue to deliver freshwater into the marine environment. This can be delivered via subglacial discharge or produced by submarine melt. Subglacial freshwater can be generated all year round through geothermal and frictional heat and delayed release of subglacially-stored freshwater. Submarine melt in Arctic fjords is caused by the presence of warm water such as Atlantic Water and its derivative coastal water masses. The dynamics of the contributing water masses are subject to varying bathymetric barriers, seasonally shifting density fronts, and external forcing such as wind or internal waves. Their impact is variable across different fjord systems. When other terrestrial water influx is limited during winter, any glacier-derived freshwater inflow into the fjords can have pronounced physical and biogeochemical consequences, even at low fluxes. These can include the generation of upwelling, but also increased stratification. The extent of the freshwater influence depends on parameters such as discharge volume flux, water depth, and depth of the glacier termini, which might in turn affect ice algae and phytoplankton production during the early spring bloom. Coupling of winter freshwater discharge from tidewater glaciers with the physical and biogeochemical conditions of the fjord is therefore a dynamic multivariable process. Rapidly changing wintertime conditions in the Arctic may already be impacting the functioning of the Arctic fjord ecosystems and necessitate efforts to understand these processes better. This review highlights the importance of wintertime freshwater by summarising the current state of knowledge about its presence and magnitude, drivers governing its inputs, as well as its potential ecological impact on fjord ecosystems. Our study uncovers knowledge gaps and proposes research directions to better understand the changing Arctic environment.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Vonnahme, Tobias Reiner","Nowak, Aga","Hopwood, Mark James","Meire, Lorenz","Søgaard, Dorte Haubjerg","Krawczyk, Diana","Kalhagen, Kjersti","Juul-Pedersen, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-699440"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Vonnahme, Tobias Reiner"],"country":["China","Greenland","Netherlands","Norway","Svalbard and Jan Mayen"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","Norwegian Polar Institute","Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","Southern University of Science and Technology","University Centre in Svalbard"],"keyword":["Fjord dynamics","Greenland","Runoff","Subglacial discharge","Svalbard","WINTER"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of winter freshwater from tidewater glaciers on fjords in svalbard and greenland a review","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pocean.2023.103144","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-699440","identifier":[{"id":"85175202756","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3ac6ec1b-a99a-4a1f-9d73-1311a3e44fa4"],"keyword":["Coastal circulation","Fjord dynamics","Greenland","Runoff","Subglacial discharge","Submarine glacier melt","Svalbard","Winter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C8642667E03C296327E487DC67E6F1E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/418452755/1-s2.0-S0079661123001878-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pocean.2023.103144","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gl","key":"greenland institute of natural resources","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Greenland Institute of Natural Resources","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sj","key":"university centre in svalbard","loc":["Svalbard and Jan Mayen","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"name":"University Centre in Svalbard","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"norwegian polar institute","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Polar Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands institute for sea research nioz","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Institute for Sea Research - NIOZ","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Aquatic Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Reiner","key":"vonnahmepau","last":"Vonnahme","name":"Vonnahme, Tobias Reiner","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Aga","key":"nowakpau","last":"Nowak","name":"Nowak, Aga","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark James","key":"hopwoodpau","last":"Hopwood","name":"Hopwood, Mark James","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorenz","key":"meirepau","last":"Meire","name":"Meire, Lorenz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte H.","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"69c49015-05f4-4626-be9e-3e4b667b7eb7","name":"Søgaard, Dorte Haubjerg","name_org":"Søgaard, Dorte H.","orcid":"0000-0002-6483-4747","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diana","key":"krawczykpau","last":"Krawczyk","name":"Krawczyk, Diana","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjersti","key":"kalhagenpau","last":"Kalhagen","name":"Kalhagen, Kjersti","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"juulpedersenpau","last":"Juul-Pedersen","name":"Juul-Pedersen, Thomas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.pocean.2023.103144","issn":["00796611","18734472"],"issn_org":["00796611"],"journal":"Progress in Oceanography","paperid":"103144","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Progress in Oceanography","volume":"219"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175202756"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3ac6ec1b-a99a-4a1f-9d73-1311a3e44fa4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Impact of winter freshwater from tidewater glaciers on fjords in Svalbard and Greenland : A review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-699440","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Den mørke nattehimmel med dens lejlighedsvise, flygtige stjerneskud kan give den velplacerede iagttager en uforlignelig oplevelse. Det er dog en oplevelse, som stigende lysforurening vanskeliggør. Det næstbedste må så være at tage teknikken til hjælp. Direkte transmission, “livestreaming” af nattehimlen, er efterhånden veludviklet, prisbillig, og kan, i tilgift til den æstetiske oplevelse, benyttes til videnskabelige målinger. Vi vil berette om computerdetektion af stjerneskud (meteorer) som et videnskabsprojekt faciliteret indenfor rammerne af et muligt fremtidig borgerdrevet “citizen science” forløb.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Holger","Hinse, Tobias Cornelius"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-723068"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Citizen science"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mikroobservatorier ser det nære univers og alle kan være med","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/240393375/kv231_PH_Mikroobs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-723068","ids":["sdu-3cf89fe2-178f-46d2-8a29-aa0fd47810d9"],"keyword":["Citizen Science","METEOR detection","global meteor network","sky monitoring"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-27D99977991391343B3BCCCED4803190"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/240393375/kv231_PH_Mikroobs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://kvant.dk/kv231-PH-Mikroobs.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Niels Bohr Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy, Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Holger","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Cornelius","key":"hinsepau","last":"Hinse","locid":"f7a3a4fc-432b-4f10-9791-f1498d07e261","name":"Hinse, Tobias Cornelius","orcid":"0000-0001-8870-3146","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09058893","22454942"],"issn_org":["09058893"],"issue":"2023","journal":"Kvant: Tidsskrift for Fysik og Astronomi","pages":"7-11","paperid":"04/2023","publisher":"Astronomisk Selskab","status":"p","title":"Kvant: Tidsskrift for Fysik og Astronomi","title_org":"KVANT","volume":"April"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3cf89fe2-178f-46d2-8a29-aa0fd47810d9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mikroobservatorier ser det nære univers – og alle kan være med!","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-723068","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present the discovery and validation of two TESS exoplanets orbiting nearby M dwarfs: TOI-2084 b, and TOI-4184b. We characterized the host stars by combining spectra from Shane/Kast and Magellan/FIRE, spectral energy distribution analysis, and stellar evolutionary models. In addition, we used Gemini-South/Zorro & -North/Alopeke high-resolution imaging, archival science images, and statistical validation packages to support the planetary interpretation. We performed a global analysis of multi-colour photometric data from TESS and ground-based facilities in order to derive the stellar and planetary physical parameters for each system. We find that TOI-2084 band TOI-4184 bare sub-Neptune-sized planets with radii of Rp = 2.47 ± 0.13R• and Rp = 2.43 ± 0.21 R• , respectively. TOI-2084 b completes an orbit around its host star every 6.08 days, has an equilibrium temperature of Teq = 527 ± 8 K and an irradiation of Sp = 12.8 ± 0.8 S• . Its host star is a dwarf of spectral M2.0 ± 0.5 at a distance of 114 pc with an effective temperature of Teff = 3550 ± 50 K, and has a wide, co-moving M8 companion at a projected separation of 1400 au. TOI-4184 b orbits around an M5.0 ± 0.5 type dwarf star (Kmag = 11.87) each 4.9 days, and has an equilibrium temperature of Teq = 412 ± 8 K and an irradiation of Sp = 4.8 ± 0.4 S• . TOI-4184 is a metal poor star ([Fe/H] = 0.27 ± 0.09 dex) at a distance of 69 pc with an effective temperature of Teff = 3225 ± 75 K. Both planets are located at the edge of the sub-Jovian desert in the radius-period plane. The combination of the small size and the large infrared brightness of their host stars make these new planets promising targets for future atmospheric exploration with JWST.","author_count":70,"contributors":["Barkaoui, K.","Timmermans, M.","Soubkiou, A.","Rackham, B. V.","Burgasser, A. J.","Chouqar, J.","Pozuelos, F. J.","Collins, K. A.","Howell, S. B.","Simcoe, R.","Melis, C.","Stassun, K. G.","Tregloan-Reed, J.","Cointepas, M.","Gillon, M.","Bonfils, X.","Furlan, E.","Gnilka, C. L.","Almenara, J. M.","Alonso, R.","Benkhaldoun, Z.","Bonavita, M.","Bouchy, F.","Burdanov, A.","Chinchilla, P.","Davoudi, F.","Delrez, L.","Demangeon, O.","Dominik, M.","Demory, B. O.","De Wit, J.","Dransfield, G.","Ducrot, E.","Fukui, A.","Hinse, Tobias Cornelius","Hooton, M. J.","Jehin, E.","Jenkins, J. M.","Jørgensen, U. G.","Latham, D. W.","Garcia, L.","Carrazco-Gaxiola, S.","Ghachoui, M.","Gómez Maqueo Chew, Y.","Günther, M. N.","McCormac, J.","Murgas, F.","Murray, C. A.","Narita, N.","Niraula, P.","Pedersen, P. P.","Queloz, D.","Rebolo-López, R.","Ricker, G.","Sabin, L.","Sajadian, S.","Schanche, N.","Schwarz, R. P.","Seager, S.","Sebastian, D.","Sefako, R.","Sohy, S.","Southworth, J.","Srdoc, G.","Thompson, S. J.","Triaud, A. H.M.J.","Vanderspek, R.","Wells, R. D.","Winn, J. N.","Zúñiga-Fernández, S."],"cuid":["S02-086.73-698260"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa","America, Central","America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Barkaoui, K."],"country":["Belgium","Chile","Croatia","France","Iran","Japan","Mexico","Morocco","Netherlands","Portugal","South Africa","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cadi Ayyad University","Center for Astrophysics","Centro de Astrofísica da Universidade do Porto","ESA-ESTEC","Georgia State University","Instituto de Astrofísica de Andalucía - CSIC","Instituto de Astrofísica de Canarias","Ipag","Isfahan University of Technology","Keele University","Kotizarovci Observatory","Massachusetts Institute of Technology","NASA Ames Research Center","NASA Astrobiology Institute","NINS Astrobiology Center","National Autonomous University of Mexico","Princeton University","RECONS Institute","South African Astronomical Observatory","The University of Tokyo","University of Atacama","University of Bern","University of Birmingham","University of California","University of Colorado","University of Edinburgh, Institute for Astronomy","University of Geneva","University of La Laguna","University of Liège","University of Maryland","University of Paris-Saclay","University of Porto","University of St Andrews","University of Warwick","Vanderbilt University"],"keyword":["Stars low mass","Techniques photometric"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Cavendish Laboratory"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toi 000000002084 b and toi 000000004184 b two new sub neptunes around m dwarf stars","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202346838","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This paper made use of data collected by the TESS mission and are publicly available from the Mikulski Archive for Space Telescopes (MAST) operated by the Space Telescope Science Institute (STScI). Funding for the TESS mission is provided by NASA’s Science Mission Directorate. We acknowledge the use of public TESS data from pipelines at the TESS Science Office and at the TESS Science Processing Operations Center. Resources supporting this work were provided by the NASA High-End Computing (HEC) Program through the NASA Advanced Supercomputing (NAS) Division at Ames Research Center for the production of the SPOC data products. Some of the observations in the paper made use of the High-Resolution Imaging instruments Alopeke and Zorro obtained under Gemini LLP Proposal Number: GN/S-2021A-LP-105. Alopeke and Zorro were funded by the NASA Exoplanet Exploration Program and built at the NASA Ames Research Center by Steve B. Howell, Nie Scott, Elliott P. Horch, and Emmett Quigley. Alopeke/Zorro was mounted on the Gemini North/South) telescope of the international Gemini Observatory, a program of NSF’s OIR Lab, which is managed by the Association of Universities for Research in Astronomy (AURA) under a cooperative agreement with the National Science Foundation, on behalf of the Gemini partnership: the National Science Foundation (United States), National Research Council (Canada), Agencia Nacional de Investigacion y Desarrollo (Chile), Mnisterio de Ciencia, Tecnologia e Innovacion (Argentina), Mnistério da Ciência, Tecnologia, Inovaçôes e Comunicaçôes (Brazil), and Korea Astronomy and Space Science Institute (Republic of Korea). The research leading to these results has received funding from the ARC grant for Concerted Research Actions, financed by the Wallonia-Brussels Federation. TRAPPIST is funded by the Belgian Fund for Scientific Research (Fond National de la Recherche Scientifique, FNRS) under the grant PDR T.0120.21. TRAPPIST-North is a project funded by the University of Liege (Belgium), in collaboration with Cadi Ayyad University of Marrakech (Morocco). M.G. is F.R.S.-FNRS Research Director and EJ. is F.R.S.-FNRS Senior Research Associate. L.D. is an F.R.S.-FNRS Postdoctoral Researcher. The postdoctoral fellowship of K.B. is funded by F.R.S.-FNRS grant T.0109.20 and by the Francqui Foundation. This publication benefits from the support of the French Community of Belgium in the context of the FRIA Doctoral Grant awarded to MT. This research is in part funded by the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation program (grants agreements n° 803193/BEBOP), and from the Science and Technology Facilities Council (STFC; grant n° ST/S00193X/1). This work is based upon observations carried out at the Observatorio Astronomico Nacional on the Sierra de San Pedro Mârtir (OAN-SPM), Baja California, Mexico. SAINT-EX observations and team were supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation (PP00P2-163967 and PP00P2-190080), the Centre for Space and Habitability (CSH) of the University of Bern, the National Centre for Competence in Research PlanetS, supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF), and UNAM PAPIIT-IG101321. J.d.W. and M.I.T. gratefully acknowledge financial support from the Heising-Simons Foundation, Dr. and Mrs. Colin Masson and Dr. Peter A. Oilman for Artemis, the first telescope of the SPECULOOS network situated in Tenerife, Spain. CM. acknowledges support from the US National Science Foundation grant SPG-1826583. Research at Lick Observatory is partially supported by a generous gift from Google. B.V.R. thanks the Heising-Simons Foundation for support. F.J.P. acknowledges financial support from the grant CEX2021-001131-S funded by MCIN/AEI/ 10.13039/501100011033. T.C.H. received funding from the Europlanet 2024 Research Infrastructure (RI) programme under grant agreement no. 871149. The Europlanet 2024 RI provides free access to the world’s largest collection of planetary simulation and analysis facilities, data services and tools, a ground-based observational network and programme of community support activities. This work is partly supported by JSPS KAKENHI Grant Number JP18H05439 and JST CREST Grant Number JPMJCR1761. This paper is based on observations made with the MuSCAT3 instrument, developed by the Astrobi-ology Center and under financial supports by JSPS KAKENHI (JP18H05439) and JST PRESTO (JPMJPR1775), at Faulkes Telescope North on Maui, HI, operated by the Las Cumbres Observatory. U.G.J. gratefully acknowledges support from the Novo Nordisk Foundation Interdisciplinary Synergy Program grant no. NNF19OC0057374 and from the European Union H2020-MSCA-ITN-2019 under grant no. 860470 (CHAMELEON). This work makes use of observations from the LCOGT network. Part of the LCOGT telescope time was granted by NOIRLab through the Mid-Scale Innovations Program (MSIP). MSIP is funded by NSF. This research has made use of the Exoplanet Follow-up Observation Program (ExoFOP; DOI: 10.26134/ExoFOP5 ) website, which is operated by the California Institute of Technology, under contract with the National Aeronautics and Space Administration under the Exoplanet Exploration Program. K.A.C. acknowledges support from the TESS mission via subaward s3449 from MIT. We are grateful to the ESO/La Silla staff for their continuous support. We acknowledge funding from the European Research Council under the ERC Grant Agreement n. 337591-ExTrA. We thank the Swiss National Science Foundation (SNSF) and the Geneva University for their continuous support to our planet search programs. This work has been carried out within the framework of the National Centre of Competence in Research PlanetS supported by the Swiss National Science Foundation under grants 51NF40_182901 and 51NF40_205606. The authors acknowledge the financial support of the SNSF. Portions of this work were conducted at Lick Observatory, which was built on the unceded territory of the Ohlone (Costanoans), Tamyen and Muwekma Ohlone tribes, whose people continue to maintain their political sovereignty and cultural traditions as vital members of central and northern California communities."],"id":"S02-086.73-698260","identifier":[{"id":"85170826751","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-82e4786e-6eaf-4993-a791-61bd1d4b0ac5","sdu-91adcbad-aa9c-4d52-a538-9acb6189408f"],"keyword":["Stars: low-mass","Techniques: photometric"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D983C40FB61E3FC41FD908C82071B766"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/241018711/aa46838_23.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/202346838","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/370489658/aa46838_23.pdf","v