,"url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-691853","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Piezoelectric III-N semiconductor nanostructures are of increasing interest to be used for sensor technologies and energy harvesting. Within this group of materials, AlN is known for the largest bulk piezoelectric constant, but piezoelectric properties of AlN nanostructures are not well studied. In the current work, AlN nanostructures are fabricated by reactive magnetron sputter deposition at normal and glancing angle orientations on Si substrates covered by a conductive TiN film. Ag nanoparticles are used to facilitate nucleation of the nanostructures, which are found to have a bud-like shape consisting of individual pillars/lamellae. These pillars exhibit a wurtzite-like hexagonal lattice and preferential growth direction along the c-axis. Piezoresponse force microscopy is used to characterize the properties of the nanostructures. Giant values of the piezoresponse coefficient are measured, reaching up to 6 times higher values compared to AlN bulk and thin films. The obtained results create a basis for optimization of the fabrication parameters enabling tuning of the AlN piezoelectric properties and further development of the technology toward the formation of large-area nanoscale matrixes for energy generation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Popok, Vladimir","Chirumamilla, Manohar","Krekeler, Tobias","Ritter, Martin","Pedersen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-673497"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hamburg University of Technology"],"keyword":["Nanostructures","Piezoelectric materials","Piezoresponse force microscopy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"magnetron sputter grown aln nanostructures with giant piezoelectric response toward energy generation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85161013820&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["V.N.P, M.C., and K.P. acknowledge the financial support from the Novo Nordisk Foundation under the grant Nanoscale Energy Generators (number NNF20OC0064735)."],"id":"S01-000.00-673497","identifier":[{"id":"85161013820","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-32c1565d-2d88-48c2-b69c-845acadc7276"],"keyword":["III-nitrides","nanostructures","piezoelectric generators","piezoelectric materials","piezoresponse force microscopy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3540817D73474A5CBF8EEE24590D8BDE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics and Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"hamburg university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hamburg University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vladimir","key":"popokpau","last":"Popok","locid":"825a665b-b8a4-4308-8c60-28ff3f224e2d","name":"Popok, Vladimir","orcid":"0000-0002-9480-3765","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Manohar","key":"chirumamillapau","last":"Chirumamilla","locid":"c2b8cbb4-b7a0-491b-81e2-324e75c6edb0","name":"Chirumamilla, Manohar","orcid":"0000-0002-6812-286X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"krekelerpau","last":"Krekeler","name":"Krekeler, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff5fc0ab-1fa1-47a2-916c-8b7556f2f938","name":"Pedersen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-6835-1566","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsanm.3c01250","issn":["25740970"],"issue":"10","journal":"ACS Applied Nano Materials","pages":"8849-8856","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Applied Nano Materials","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161013820"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-32c1565d-2d88-48c2-b69c-845acadc7276"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Magnetron Sputter Grown AlN Nanostructures with Giant Piezoelectric Response toward Energy Generation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-673497","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Recombinant plasmids are essential tools in molecular biotechnology, and reliable plasmid assembly methods have, therefore, become a prerequisite for the successful cloning and transfer of genes. Among the multitude of available plasmid assembly strategies, in vivo homologous recombinational cloning in yeast has emerged as a cost-effective and relatively simple method. Since we use this method routinely in our group for assembling large plasmids with secondary metabolite gene clusters and for direct heterologous production of polyketides in Saccharomyces cerevisiae, we developed an exercise module for undergraduate students where they would get hands-on experience with these molecular practices. The exercises target several molecular techniques, including PCR, restriction enzyme digestion, and yeast recombinational cloning. The students will learn about plasmid assembly and yeast transformation methods by performing these experiments while inherently acquiring new skills valuable for their subsequent laboratory work or projects.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bejenari, Mihaela","Nielsen, Line","Spedtsberg, Eva Mie Lang","Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-705805"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biotechnology","Cloning","Microbiology","Plasmids","Problem Based Learning","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Transformation","Yeast"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"yeast recombinational cloning for heterologous biosynthesis of polyketides a molecular microbiology laboratory module for undergraduate students","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/jmbe.00242-22","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by grants from The Danish Research Council, Technology, and Production (grant no. 7017-00167) and the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF18OC0034952 and NNF20OC0064343)."],"id":"S01-000.00-705805","identifier":[{"id":"85182154674","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38108002","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b265cf9f-768c-4ee0-891c-a9d7cb831761"],"keyword":["Biotechnology","Cloning","Microbiology","Plasmids","Problem-Based Learning","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Transformation","Yeast"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-71E0FDEF1D0C6027494848E6E285B50D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/jmbe.00242-22","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/620675761/bejenari-et-al-2023-yeast-recombinational-cloning-for-heterologous-biosynthesis-of-polyketides-a-molecular-microbiology.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Bioscience and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mihaela","key":"bejenarimihaelapau","last":"Bejenari","locid":"3d63793c-c26d-4fe2-b045-bb831383086e","name":"Bejenari, Mihaela","orcid":"0000-0001-9894-8817","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":