{"abstract":"This paper demonstrates a case of progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) in a patient with multiple myeloma (MM) treated with nine different MM therapies. This case report contributes to the already published 16 cases of PML in patients with MM. Additionally, this paper presents an analysis of cases from the United States Food and Drug Administration Adverse Event Report System database (n = 117) with a description of demographics and MM-specific therapies. Patients with MM, that developed PML, were treated with immunomodulatory drugs (97%), alkylating agents (52%), and/or proteasome inhibitors (49%). Prior to PML diagnosis, 72% of patients received two or more MM therapies. These results indicate that PML in MM is underreported and could be related to treatment with multiple immunosuppressive therapies rather than MM as a disease itself. Physicians should be aware of potential PML in the late stage of heavily treated MM patients.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jonasson, Elise","Antulov, Ronald","Trøllund Pedersen, Per","Sejbaek, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-680127"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jonasson, Elise"],"keyword":["Case report","FAERS","Immunosuppression","Multiple myeloma","PML","progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy in a patient with multiple myeloma a case report and analysis of the fda adverse event reporting system","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2023.1098930","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank the patient's spouse for consenting to this case report."],"id":"S01-000.00-680127","identifier":[{"id":"85159909769","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37213905","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10192558","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-282c02ed-19e3-453b-ae84-703b4d1d562f"],"keyword":["FAERS","PML","case report","immunosuppression","multiple myeloma","progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22EA5BD6527353160CECADC98443F7E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fneur.2023.1098930","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/231650178/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elise","key":"jonassonpau","last":"Jonasson","locid":"dad3ae65-225b-4d99-9dc4-68f51900fc99","name":"Jonasson, Elise","orcid":"0000-0003-3693-9346","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ronald","key":"antulovpau","last":"Antulov","locid":"a498244a-da25-4a82-b16e-4eae7e878515","name":"Antulov, Ronald","orcid":"0000-0002-5819-718X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"trøllundpedersenpau","last":"Trøllund Pedersen","locid":"6650d937-fe7b-47a5-9ba9-1828323a312b","name":"Trøllund Pedersen, Per","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"sejbækpau","last":"Sejbæk","locid":"fba1022d-c447-4075-a60b-b0c31e11995b","name":"Sejbaek, Tobias","name_org":"Sejbæk, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-7682-2188","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37213905"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fneur.2023.1098930","issn":["16642295"],"journal":"Frontiers in Neurology","paperid":"1098930","publisher":"Frontiers Research Foundation","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Neurology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159909769"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-282c02ed-19e3-453b-ae84-703b4d1d562f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy in a patient with multiple myeloma : a case report and analysis of the FDA adverse event reporting system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-680127","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Environments connected to Arctic fjords are changing rapidly, with consequences for society. A warmer climate is an important driver of change, but other factors also play a major role, including pressures and opportunities from fishing, tourism, shipping, and changing socio-economic conditions. This report provides a synthesis of insights from participatory scenario workshops with local stakeholders around the fjords Nuup Kangerlua, Greenland; Isfjorden, Svalbard; and Porsangerfjorden, Northern Norway. It includes narratives of potential futures intended as input to discussions about adaptive co-management options for two focus areas in the EU-funded FACE-IT project: Food provision and local livelihood and Nature-based tourism. While each social-ecological fjord system faces its unique management challenges, the workshops highlight several common concerns, including changing biodiversity, the importance of policy decisions and regulations as shapers of change, and increasing competition for space.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nilsson, Annika","Bjørst, Lill Rastad","Risvoll, Camilla","Ren, Carina","Vonnahme, Tobias R.","Juul-Pedersen, Thomas","Hovelsrud, Grete","Dannevig, Halvor","Paulsen, Majken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-698883"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the future of arctic fjord systems insights from participatory scenario workshops about nuup kangerlua greenland isfjorden svalbard and porsangerfjorden norway deliverable 000000000004 000000000002 workshop reports","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-698883","ids":["aau-b0e8a810-d11b-487e-a239-fa083a198ee6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D5AF26F0ED3256A4C9430E43861614A5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, Research in sociocultural aspects of sustainability and green transitions (Recast)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Law, AAU Arctic","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Green Societies","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","name":"Nilsson, Annika","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lill Rastad","key":"bjørstpau","last":"Bjørst","name":"Bjørst, Lill Rastad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla","key":"risvollpau","last":"Risvoll","name":"Risvoll, Camilla","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carina","key":"renpau","last":"Ren","locid":"767c86d5-3c9f-4859-adc4-6c90e5502b2c","name":"Ren, Carina","orcid":"0000-0003-4414-5917","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias R.","key":"vonnahmepau","last":"Vonnahme","name":"Vonnahme, Tobias R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"juulpedersenpau","last":"Juul-Pedersen","name":"Juul-Pedersen, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Grete","key":"hovelsrudpau","last":"Hovelsrud","name":"Hovelsrud, Grete","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Halvor","key":"dannevigpau","last":"Dannevig","name":"Dannevig, Halvor","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Majken","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","name":"Paulsen, Majken","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"142","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b0e8a810-d11b-487e-a239-fa083a198ee6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The future of Arctic fjord systems. Insights from participatory scenario workshops about Nuup Kangerlua (Greenland), Isfjorden (Svalbard) and Porsangerfjorden (Norway) : Deliverable 4.2 Workshop reports","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-698883","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Blockchain research tends to focus on technical improvements and their potential for efficiency and productivity, repeatedly at the cost of comprehending the complex reciprocal interaction between social and technical aspects. One of the technical challenges for blockchain systems is scalability. Interoperability has proven effective in addressing scalability by offloading transactions via bridges, enhancing flexibility and portability for, e.g., tokens. As a result, we investigate how interoperability is organized in blockchain systems and what implications it might bring. In this research, we develop an on-ledger analytics prototype, which facilitates the examinations of NFT bridges and theorizes about the dimensions of interoperability. Practical implications reveal that hiding a token’s track in an otherwise supposedly transparent system is possible. We provide evidence that current research may only consider a subset of a token’s history among blockchain systems. Ultimately, we claim that interoperability among blockchain systems can lead to decreased transparency.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Iversen, Hampus MIchael Wadum","Schmidt, Tobias Ærboe","Pedersen, Asger Balle","Beck, Roman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701227"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Information Systems IS Research","Information systems","Interoperability","Tokens","Transparency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to cross the bridge interoperability among blockchain systems interoperability among blockchain systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770173/icis23a-sub1171-cam-i9_13_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701227","ids":["itu-14631e3b-8d1c-42e2-aa15-1fed22e7b14d"],"keyword":["Information Systems (IS) Research","blockchain","information systems","interoperability","tokens","transparency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-46E9D755E2152288894AF6E60DEF2623"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101770173/icis23a-sub1171-cam-i9_13_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT, European Blockchain Center (EBC)","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hampus MIchael Wadum","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","name":"Iversen, Hampus MIchael Wadum","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Ærboe","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Tobias Ærboe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Balle","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"09ec1bda-4550-4a83-8480-fe742d77e882","name":"Pedersen, Asger Balle","orcid":"0000-0002-3390-2831","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Roman","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"d72cc0d6-fe4f-4392-bf88-243e5d7e36e5","name":"Beck, Roman","orcid":"0000-0002-6341-2382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000033"],"journal":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / International Conference on Information Systems (ICIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-14631e3b-8d1c-42e2-aa15-1fed22e7b14d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How to cross the bridge: Interoperability among blockchain systems : Interoperability among blockchain systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701227","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Intermetatarsal bursitis (IMB) is an inflammation of the intermetatarsal bursas. The condition causes forefoot pain with symptoms similar to those of Morton’s neuroma (MN). Some studies suggest that IMB is a contributing factor to the development of MN, while others describe the condition as a differential diagnosis. Among patients with rheumatic diseases, IMB is frequent, but the scope is yet to be understood. The aim of this paper was to investigate the diagnostic considerations of IMB and its role in metatarsalgia by a systematic review approach. We identified studies about IMB by searching the electronic databases Pubmed, Embase, Cochrane Library, and Web of Science in September 2022. Of 1362 titles, 28 met the inclusion criteria. They were subdivided according to topic: anatomical studies (n = 3), studies of patients with metatarsalgia (n = 10), and studies of patients with rheumatic diseases (n = 15). We conclude that IMB should be considered a cause of pain in patients with metatarsalgia and patients with rheumatic diseases. For patients presenting with spreading toes/V-sign, IMB should be a diagnostic consideration. Future diagnostic studies about MN should take care to apply a protocol that is able to differ IMB from MN, to achieve a better understanding of their respective role in forefoot pain.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Sif Binder","Søgaard, Stinne Byrholdt","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Torp-Pedersen, Søren Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466429"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bursitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diagnostic considerations of intermetatarsal bursitis a systematic review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics13020211","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-466429","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9857655","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85146759325","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36673020","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-79e343f3-ea91-4cc8-8620-c10d147cf758"],"keyword":["Morton’s neuroma","bursitis","forefoot bursa","forefoot pain: metatarsalgia","intermetatarsal bursitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E2BB441D52D3CC1A0CAFC1645D603AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics13020211","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/334858034/Diagnostic_Considerations.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Renal and Vascular Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sif Binder","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Sif Binder","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Stinne Byrholdt","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"bba245e9-b5c7-4b46-8a05-554f0d8380eb","name":"Søgaard, Stinne Byrholdt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6c91b654-63b7-4eeb-8a6e-ee4a2708020a","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","orcid":"0000-0002-9380-1688","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Tobias","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Søren Tobias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36673020"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/diagnostics13020211","issn":["20754418"],"issue":"2","journal":"Diagnostics","paperid":"211","status":"p","title":"Diagnostics","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146759325"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-79e343f3-ea91-4cc8-8620-c10d147cf758"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diagnostic Considerations of Intermetatarsal Bursitis : A Systematic Review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466429","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The long-term operation of refractory-metal-based metamaterials is crucial for applications such as thermophotovoltaics. The metamaterials based on refractory metals like W, Mo, Ta, Nb, and Re fail primarily by oxidation. Here, the use of the noble metal Ir is proposed, which is stable to oxidation and has optical properties comparable to gold. The thermal endurance of Ir in a 3-layer-system, consisting of HfO2/Ir/HfO2, by performing annealing experiments up to 1240 °C in a pressure range from 2 × 10−6 mbar to 1 bar, is demonstrated. The Ir layer shows no oxidation in a vacuum and inert gas atmosphere. At temperatures above 1100 °C, the Ir layer starts to agglomerate due to the degradation of the confining HfO2 layers. An in situ X-ray diffraction experimental comparison between 1D multilayered Ir/HfO2 and W/HfO2 selective emitters annealed at 1000 °C, 2 × 10−6 mbar, over 100 h, confirms oxidation stability of Ir while W multilayers gradually disappear. The results of this work show that W-based metamaterials are not long-term stable even at 1000 °C. However, the oxidation resistance of Ir can be leveraged for refractory plasmonic metamaterials, such as selective emitters in thermophotovoltaic systems with strong suppression of long wavelength radiation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Vaidhyanathan Krishnamurthy, Gnanavel","Chirumamilla, Manohar","Krekeler, Tobias","Ritter, Martin","Raudsepp, Ragle","Schieda, Mauricio","Klassen, Thomas","Pedersen, Kjeld","Petrov, Alexander Yu","Eich, Manfred","Störmer, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692366"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chirumamilla, Manohar","Vaidhyanathan Krishnamurthy, Gnanavel"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hamburg University of Technology","Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon"],"keyword":["Hafnia","Iridium","Magnetron sputtering","Selective emitters","Thermophotovoltaics","Thin films"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"iridium based selective emitters for thermophotovoltaic applications","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202305922","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge financial support from the German Research Foundation (DFG) via SFB 986 “Tailor‐Made Multi‐Scale Materials Systems: M3”, Project‐ID 192346071, and projects C1 and Z3. The authors appreciate the support from the Helmholtz‐Zentrum Hereon library."],"id":"S01-000.00-692366","identifier":[{"id":"85170076556","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-01805273-ddbb-4eff-a569-4ad99cb17d22"],"keyword":["hafnia","iridium","magnetron sputtering","selective emitters","thermophotovoltaics","thin-films"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E57BC7FD643E9C9745D9B08FBD3AE550"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/573808752/Advanced_Materials_-_2023_-_Vaidhyanathan_Krishnamurthy_-_Iridium_Based_Selective_Emitters_for_Thermophotovoltaic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/adma.202305922","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"helmholtz zentrum hereon","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics and Mechanics","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"hamburg university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hamburg University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gnanavel","key":"vaidhyanathankrishnamurthypau","last":"Vaidhyanathan Krishnamurthy","name":"Vaidhyanathan Krishnamurthy, Gnanavel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Manohar","key":"chirumamillapau","last":"Chirumamilla","locid":"c2b8cbb4-b7a0-491b-81e2-324e75c6edb0","name":"Chirumamilla, Manohar","orcid":"0000-0002-6812-286X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"krekelerpau","last":"Krekeler","name":"Krekeler, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ragle","key":"raudsepppau","last":"Raudsepp","name":"Raudsepp, Ragle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mauricio","key":"schiedapau","last":"Schieda","name":"Schieda, Mauricio","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"klassenpau","last":"Klassen","name":"Klassen, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff5fc0ab-1fa1-47a2-916c-8b7556f2f938","name":"Pedersen, Kjeld","orcid":"00