{"abstract":"Aluminum nitride (AlN) is a material of growing interest for power electronics, fabrication of sensors, micro-electromechanical systems, and piezoelectric generators. For the latter, the formation of nanowire arrays or nanostructured films is one of the emerging research directions. In the current work, nanostructured AlN films manufactured with normal and glancing angle magnetron sputter depositions have been investigated with scanning and transmission electron microscopy, X-ray diffraction, atomic force microscopy, and optical spectroscopy. Growth of the nanostructures was realized utilizing metal seed particles (Ag, Au, and Al), allowing the control of the nucleation and following growth of AlN. It was demonstrated how variations of seed particle material and size can be used to tune the parameters of nanostructures and morphology of the AlN films. Using normal angle deposition allowed the growth of bud-shaped structures, which consisted of pillars/lamellae with wurtzite-like crystalline structures. Deposition at a glancing angle of 85° led to a film of individual nanostructures located near each other and tilted at an angle of 33° relative to the surface normal. Such films maintained a high degree of wurtzite-like crystallinity but had a more open structure and higher roughness than the nanostructured films grown at normal incidence deposition. The developed production strategies and recipes for controlling parameters of nanostructured films pave the way for the formation of matrices to be used in piezoelectric applications.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Chirumamilla, Manohar","Krekeler, Tobias","Wang, Deyong","Kristensen, Peter Kjær","Ritter, Martin","Popok, Vladimir","Pedersen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-698464"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hamburg University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"magnetron sputter deposition of nanostructured aln thin films","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/applnano4040016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-698464","identifier":[{"id":"105001101987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1ea594d8-1767-4ef0-a3b7-9dec62b59352"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA1C30C098720D5B1F1BD1424F8B4033"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/575212558/2023ApplNano_4_AlN_nanostruct.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/applnano4040016","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics and Mechanics","Aalborg University, [Mission] A Sustainable Danish Energy System"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"hamburg university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hamburg University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Manohar","key":"chirumamillapau","last":"Chirumamilla","locid":"c2b8cbb4-b7a0-491b-81e2-324e75c6edb0","name":"Chirumamilla, Manohar","orcid":"0000-0002-6812-286X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"krekelerpau","last":"Krekeler","name":"Krekeler, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Deyong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"092c44d3-1081-4222-860c-03ae150e0a0f","name":"Wang, Deyong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Kjær","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"b8970f31-d480-48c5-853b-c33bb78edb49","name":"Kristensen, Peter Kjær","orcid":"0000-0001-7260-0548","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Martin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vladimir","key":"popokpau","last":"Popok","locid":"825a665b-b8a4-4308-8c60-28ff3f224e2d","name":"Popok, Vladimir","orcid":"0000-0002-9480-3765","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff5fc0ab-1fa1-47a2-916c-8b7556f2f938","name":"Pedersen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-6835-1566","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/applnano4040016","issn":["26733501"],"issue":"4","journal":"Applied Nano","pages":"280-292","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Applied Nano","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001101987"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1ea594d8-1767-4ef0-a3b7-9dec62b59352"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Magnetron Sputter Deposition of Nanostructured AlN Thin Films","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-698464","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Climate change threatens global food security, but the biggest impact will be in arid, low social-economic regions. To improve food security, new breeding technologies (NBTs) could be implemented for re-domestication of crop wild relatives (CWR). CWR harbor many beneficial traits, but it is difficult to incorporate these traits into conventional breeding programs. Thus, although genebanks hold significant collections of CWR, their potential has yet to be reached. Using barley as an example, we describe how using genebank collections, digital sequence information and NBTs, re-domesticated barley can be produced with improved characteristics, while retaining the resilience and adaptation of the original material. Lastly, we highlight some obstacles that need to be overcome for re-domesticates to be adopted.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hanak, Tobias","Janjic, Jovana","Hay, Fiona","Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-708599"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hanak, Tobias"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome editing to re domesticate and accelerate use of barley crop wild relatives","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fsufs.2023.1331577","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-708599","identifier":[{"id":"85181525139","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9652fe58-1056-495f-841e-5e13d12afd41"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B7FA15E0552179D38DE0BDC6B2233AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fsufs.2023.1331577","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/361121151/2023_Hanak_et_al._fsufs-07-1331577.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"hanakpau","last":"Hanak","locid":"d1eec89c-eeb2-4337-adcc-79cf10e2d519","name":"Hanak, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-2913-9893","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jovana","key":"janjicpau","last":"Janjic","locid":"a468f18a-a9ff-4184-9356-cb30ae1a3b22","name":"Janjic, Jovana","orcid":"0000-0001-9000-6729","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fiona","key":"haypau","last":"Hay","locid":"f096af7d-20cc-468e-91d4-6832e59b21d4","name":"Hay, Fiona","orcid":"0000-0002-3118-897X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"brinchpedersenpau","last":"Brinch-Pedersen","locid":"b99acfd4-b212-450a-86a8-0d91eb9c1a15","name":"Brinch-Pedersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9773-8903","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fsufs.2023.1331577","issn":["2571581X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Sustainable Food Systems","paperid":"1331577","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Sustainable Food Systems","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181525139"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9652fe58-1056-495f-841e-5e13d12afd41"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Genome editing to re-domesticate and accelerate use of barley crop wild relatives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-708599","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Pedersen, Tobias Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-057637"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"heterologous expression of polyketides in yeast","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-057637","ids":["aau-19e7142f-7252-4d72-8257-9bba20133369"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AE1FB982793E3CEAEF28395CE17CD39B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Functional Genomics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section for Chemical Science and Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Bruun","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc73daa2-870d-4de9-bf18-bd8a23efc501","name":"Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["24461636"],"series":"Ph.d.-serien for Det Ingeniør- og Naturvidenskabelige Fakultet, Aalborg Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-19e7142f-7252-4d72-8257-9bba20133369"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Heterologous Expression of Polyketides in Yeast","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-057637","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The biosynthetic pathways for the fungal polyketides bikaverin and bostrycoidin, from Fusarium verticillioides and Fusarium solani respectively, were reconstructed and heterologously expressed in S. cerevisiae alongside seven different phosphopantetheinyl transferases (PPTases) from a variety of origins spanning bacterial, yeast and fungal origins. In order to gauge the efficiency of the interaction between the ACP-domains of the polyketide synthases (PKS) and PPTases, each were co-expressed individually and the resulting production of target polyketides were determined after 48 h of growth. In co-expression with both biosynthetic pathways, the PPTase from Fusarium verticillioides (FvPPT1) proved most efficient at producing both bikaverin and bostrycoidin, at 1.4 mg/L and 5.9 mg/L respectively. Furthermore, the remaining PPTases showed the ability to interact with both PKS's, except for a single PKS-PPTase combination. The results indicate that it is possible to boost the production of a target polyketide, simply by utilizing a more optimal PPTase partner, instead of the commonly used PPTases; NpgA, Gsp and Sfp, from Aspergillus nidulans, Brevibacillus brevis and Bacillus subtilis respectively.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Kristensen, Sebastian Birkedal","Spedtsberg, Eva Mie Lang","Sørensen, Trine","Petersen, Celine","Muff, Jens","Sondergaard, Teis Esben","Nielsen, Kåre Lehmann","Wimmer, Reinhard","Gardiner, Donald Max","Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-060990"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Queensland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"speed dating for enzymes finding the perfect phosphopantetheinyl transferase partner for your polyketide synthase","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12934-021-01734-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-060990","identifier":[{"id":"35012550","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122758762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-25ab94d8-79d5-4ebf-8b2d-65ad9a9485ba"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63E2A41ADB78B68901B504CD81856C12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12934-021-01734-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/482618464/s12934_021_01734_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"university of queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Queensland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Bruun","key":"pedersentobiasbruunpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc73daa2-870d-4de9-bf18-bd8a23efc501","name":"Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Rank","key":"nielsenmikkelrankpau","last"