{"abstract":"In secular cultures, such as Denmark, tools to measure spiritual needs are warranted to guide existential and spiritual care. We examined the clinimetric properties of the Danish version of the Spiritual Needs Questionnaire (DA-SpNQ-20) based on a digital survey in a test–retest setup. A convenience sample was reached via social media and student platforms. A total of 325 (148 for retest) respondents were included in the analysis. The sample was randomly split into two groups (A and B) and used for exploratory (EFA) and confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) by structural equation modeling, respectively. SpNQ dimensions had an internal consistency with Cronbach’s alpha between 0.73 and 0.93. The four factors of the SpNQ were supported by both EFA and CFA as follows: religious needs, existential needs, inner peace needs, and generativity needs. The instrument showed good internal consistency, good test–retest reliability, and acceptable structural validity in the sample of relatively young and healthy persons.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Stripp, Tobias Kvist","Büssing, Arndt","Wehberg, Sonja","Andersen, Helen Støttrup","Kørup, Alex Kappel","Pedersen, Heidi Frølund","Søndergaard, Jens","Hvidt, Niels Christian"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029919"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stripp, Tobias Anker","Stripp, Tobias Kvist"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Witten/Herdecke University"],"keyword":["Clinimetrics","Denmark","Factor Analysis Statistical","Humans","Psychometrics","Reproducibility of Results","Secular society","Spiritual needs","Spirituality","Surveys and Questionnaires","Test retest","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring spiritual needs in a secular society validation and clinimetric properties of the danish 000000000020 item spiritual needs questionnaire","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85125480326","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The paper was supported by the Danish Cancer Society (R247-A14755), The Jascha Foundation (ID 3610), The Lung Foundation, AgeCare, and the University of Southern Denmark."],"id":"S02-100.00-029919","identifier":[{"id":"85125480326","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000762874300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35230599","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-edff5945-0e47-4a04-aef5-3375ecae2d99","sdu-7686f68c-d3a5-44b9-9b29-5faa65af463e"],"keyword":["Clinimetrics","Denmark","Factor Analysis, Statistical","Humans","Psychometrics","Reproducibility of Results","Secular society","Spiritual needs","Spirituality","Surveys and Questionnaires","Test–retest","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DB342EE78AC0FF7A5AA8FDA4D71E22B6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"witten herdecke university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Witten/Herdecke University","used":1},{"affn