ellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aa9f3e41-576c-4296-92c3-140001af08a4","au-837ffc81-d6a6-4c5a-ab1b-4c7574cd79f5","ku-0dd31db9-41d1-451d-9a06-e272412c39c0","sdu-2b0417db-4ca9-4e3f-9549-70e5abf9d526"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Validation of the UK myeloma research alliance risk profile, a new clinical prediction model for outcome in patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma not eligible for autologous stem cell transplantation; a population-based study from the Danish national multiple myeloma registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-008227","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The use of fugal secondary metabolites is extensive throughout several industries, and the compounds are often extracted using loads of harmful organic solvents. The issues with several different and also similar products produced by the same biosyntethic pathways are challenging the downstream separation and purification, especially when scaling up production for the industry. The main objective of this study was to investigate the separation, concentration and purification possibilities of four different valuable fungal pigments produced by Fusarium solani. We present a full membrane based filtration train to elucidate which membrane type can be useful in the separation and concentration of the compounds. This visualized the possibility if using microfiltration to concentrate bostrycoidin and also to separate fusarubin from the rest of the pigments. Also, a comparison study between three types of microfiltration membranes is presented, showing little to none difference in the investigated membranes. Lastly, a high concentration- high recovery filtration study is presented, concentrating bostrycoidin in an even higher concentration. It is shown in this paper, that it is possible to use membrane filtration to separate, concentrate and purify the fusarubins investigated.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kristensen, Sebastian Birkedal","Nikbakht Fini, Mahdi","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Sørensen, Jens Laurids","Muff, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064621"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fusarium","Mycotoxins","Pigments","Polyketides","Purification","Secondary metabolites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"membrane based separation and purification of fusarubins from i fusarium solani i","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.seppur.2021.119576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064621","identifier":[{"id":"85113536191","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-324e8645-5b16-4050-a7c3-c3056415282e"],"keyword":["Fusarium","Mycotoxins","Pigments","Polyketides","Purification","Secondary metabolites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C5BD01A40E83F06036F29D7B38344688"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/458997545/1_s2.0_S1383586621012843_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.seppur.2021.119576","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Environmental Chemical Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian Birkedal","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"628b798c-4348-46ef-99d7-a7ca00e710a7","name":"Kristensen, Sebastian Birkedal","orcid":"0000-0001-6399-9577","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mahdi","key":"nikbakhtfinipau","last":"Nikbakht Fini","locid":"f5cb913f-f13b-41c8-8f4a-2a6dfebe00fe","name":"Nikbakht Fini, Mahdi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias Bruun","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc73daa2-870d-4de9-bf18-bd8a23efc501","name":"Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Laurids","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"365188dd-0cdc-4c71-a590-2ccd261ae3df","name":"Sørensen, Jens Laurids","orcid":"0000-0002-2392-5343","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"muffpau","last":"Muff","locid":"31d59491-a0f2-44b7-aba4-6d1def771538","name":"Muff, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-1082-3409","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.seppur.2021.119576","issn":["13835866","18733794"],"issn_org":["13835866"],"journal":"Separation and Purification Technology","paperid":"119576","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Separation and Purification Technology","volume":"278"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113536191"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-324e8645-5b16-4050-a7c3-c3056415282e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Membrane based separation and purification of fusarubins from <i>Fusarium solani</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064621","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Diagnostic confirmation of SARS-CoV-2 by self-collection of specimens is a reliable method compared with healthcare worker collected samples. Citizens’ preferences for collection methods are unknown, but at-home collection could have several advantages. Methods: This study investigated the preference for guided at-home self-collection versus at-hospital specimen collection by healthcare workers. Results: Among the 3709 participants, at-home swab collection was the preferred setting for 2362 (63.7%) compared with 1347 (36.3%) reporting a preference for an at-hospital swabbing procedure. Conclusion: A high preference for guided at-home self-collection of oropharyngeal/nasal SARS-CoV-2 specimens exists and could be a future norm beyond COVID-19.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bundgaard, Johan S.","Raaschou-Pedersen, Daniel T.","Todsen, Tobias","Ringgaard, Anna","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","von Buchwald, Christian","Iversen, Kasper","Bundgaard, Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440233"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Diagnostics","Patient reported","SARS CoV 2","Self collection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danish citizens preferences for at home oropharyngeal nasal sars cov 000000000002 specimen collection","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijid.2021.06.060","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440233","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8245307","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34216732","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111197401","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4e7353a0-4d78-4555-92a4-18eea9c304ba"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Diagnostics","Oropharyngeal/nasal swab","Patient-reported","SARS-CoV-2","Self-collection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D746FFB5DDAFF4790807B16CF65E78BF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/275883931/1_s2.0_S1201971221005506_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijid.2021.06.060","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Johan S.","key":"bundgaardjohanspau","last":"Bundgaard","name":"Bundgaard, Johan S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel T.","key":"raaschoupedersendanieltpau","last":"Raaschou-Pedersen","name":"Raaschou-Pedersen, Daniel T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tobias","key":"todsentobiaspau","last":"Todsen","locid":"16d5c332-f162-4f76-aa1c-b0306b8222e2","name":"Todsen, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3267-3560","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna","key":"ringgaardannapau","last":"Ringgaard","name":"Ringgaard, Anna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenchristianpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"f71bedc6-3736-4559-b937-6a18e770616e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldchristianpau","last":"Von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","name_org":"Von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenkasperpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardhenningpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34216732"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijid.2021.06.060","issn":["12019712","18783511"],"issn_org":["12019712"],"journal":"International Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"195-198","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111197401"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4e7353a0-4d78-4555-92a4-18eea9c304ba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Danish citizens’ preferences for at-home oropharyngeal/nasal SARS-CoV-2 specimen collection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-440233","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Active, selective and stable catalysts are imperative for sustainable energy conversion, and engineering materials with such properties are highly desired. High-entropy alloys (HEAs) offer a vast compositional space for tuning such properties. Too vast, however, to traverse without the proper tools. Here, we report the use of Bayesian optimization on a model based on density functional theory (DFT) to predict the most active compositions for the electrochemical oxygen reduction reaction (ORR) with the least possible number of sampled compositions for the two HEAs Ag-Ir-Pd-Pt-Ru and Ir-Pd-Pt-Rh-Ru. The discovered optima are then scrutinized with DFT and subjected to experimental validation where optimal catalytic activities are verified for Ag–Pd, Ir–Pt, and Pd–Ru binary alloys. This study offers insight into the number of experiments needed for optimizing the vast compositional space of multimetallic alloys which has been determined to be on the order of 50 for ORR on these HEAs.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jack K.","Clausen, Christian Møgelberg","Krysiak, Olga A.","Xiao, Bin","Batchelor, Thomas A. A.","Löffler, Tobias","Mints, Vladislav A.","Banko, Lars","Arenz, Matthias","Savan, Alan","Schuhmann, Wolfgang","Ludwig, Alfred","Rossmeisl, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-519131"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bayesian optimization","Complex solid solutions","Density functional calculations","Electrochemistry","High entropy alloys"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bayesian optimization of high entropy alloy compositions for electrocatalytic oxygen reduction","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.202108116","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-519131","identifier":[{"id":"85116319790","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34506069","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8596574","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-d261a9a2-9054-43c8-b438-9112e866e2c5"],"keyword":["Density functional calculations","bayesian optimization","complex solid solutions","electrochemistry","high-entropy alloys"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52F9136CFDA8DBCA007510278C5B301B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.202108116","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/288781397/Angewandte_Chemie_Intl_Edit_2021_Pedersen_Bayesian_Optimization_of_High_u2010Entropy_Alloy_Compositions_for.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jack Kirk","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"35e9bf13-527e-4534-a69c-d714f3d7f302","name":"Pedersen, Jack K.","name_org":"Pedersen, Jack Kirk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Møgelberg","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"ce66f0be-1aa9-4da9-8e1f-1d54db74ae90","name":"Clausen, Christian Møgelberg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Olga A.","key":"krysiakpau","last":"Krysiak","name":"Krysiak, Olga A.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bin","key":"xiaopau","last":"Xiao","name":"Xiao, Bin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Thomas A. A.","key":"batchelorpau","last":"Batchelor","locid":"efb0c7e3-19b9-460b-aa55-0f0e16fe31df","name":"Batchelor, Thomas A. A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"löfflerpau","last":"Löffler","name":"Löffler, Tobias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vladislav A.","key":"mintspau","last":"Mints","name":"Mints, Vladislav A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"bankopau","last":"Banko","name":"Banko, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"arenzpau","last":"Arenz","name":"Arenz, Matthias","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alan","key":"savanpau","last":"Savan","name":"Savan, Alan","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wolfgang","key":"schuhmannpau","last":"Schuhmann","name":"Schuhmann, Wolfgang","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alfred","key":"ludwigpau","last":"Ludwig","name":"Ludwig, Alfred","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"rossmeislpau","last":"Rossmeisl","locid":"67d41da5-3458-43c8-8ea7-d2b1a80f1f8d","name":"Rossmeisl, Jan","orcid":"0000-0001-7749-6567","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34506069"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.202108116","issn":["00448249","15213757"],"issn_org":["15213773"],"issue":"45","journal":"Angewandte Chemie","pages":"24144-24152","paperid":"9","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie","title_org":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","volume":"60"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116319790"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d261a9a2-9054-43c8-b438-9112e866e2c5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bayesian Optimization of High-Entropy Alloy Compositions for Electrocatalytic Oxygen Reduction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-519131","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background and aims: Meals-on-wheels in nursing homes are sensory diminished because of the packaging and reheating of the food, which creates less appetite stimulation and an impaired meal experience for nursing home residents. This background is crucial since nursing home residents are a frail and often malnourished group that is physiologically affected by sensory, physical and mental alterations. The study aimed to increase health-related quality of life in nursing home residents receiving meals-on-wheels using an intervention menu with favourite meals that added a culinary twist and were sensory improved by chefs.  Methods: A double-blinded cluster-randomized controlled trial with two arms, one group receives an intervention menu, and the other group receives a non-optimized menu. The intervention menu included popular meals-on-wheels (a main meal for dinner and a starter/dessert before or after dinner with culinary improvements). The participants received the same meals without culinary improvements in the control group. Health-related quality of life (EQ5D3L) was the primary outcome of the study. Secondary outcomes were mental and nutritional status and muscle strength. The measurements were assessed at a baseline and end visit (12 weeks after baseline visit).  Results: Fifty-two nursing home residents were included in the study (There are 20 in the intervention group and 32 in the control group). Following the principle of intention-to-treat, a significant decreasing effect (p-value 0.026) was found between the groups on health-related quality of life. The treated group experienced the largest decrease from the baseline to the end visit. The intervention group had a significant decrease in the second item on Satisfaction With Food-related Life (SWFL2) (I am very pleased with my food). No changes were found either within or between the groups, on the rest of the measured parameters. Conclusions: Nursing home residents are a target group experiencing natural aggravation, why the health-related quality of life might be difficult to improve using a culinary meal intervention. The decreasing effect of Satisfaction With Food-related Life found in the intervention group could be related to these older adults being too unfamiliar with the culinary twist added to the intervention menu.  The study was registered on ClinTrials.gov (Identifier NCT03133364).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Okkels, Signe Loftager","Dybdal, Ditte Rokkjær","Pedersen, Rie Johanne","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","Olsen, Annemarie","Beck, Anne Marie","Bügel, Susanne Gjedsted"],"cuid":["S02-095.19-039547"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Compliance","Culinary improvement","Meals on wheels","Quality of Life","Rehabilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a culinary twist of a two course meals on wheels menu in a cluster randomized controlled trial influencing health related quality of life in nursing home residents","src":["kp","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85102451944&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.19-039547","identifier":[{"id":"85102451944","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34024505","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["kp-e692e116-7f2b-466c-a43a-9663bf3c0992","ku-da4d70de-65f2-402c-817b-27375884bf5f"],"keyword":["Compliance","Culinary improvement","Meals-on-wheels","Quality of life","Rehabilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8B1F559AF34964E6A2C62AA1A7BDA878"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Unilabs A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Ernærings- og Sundhedsuddannelsen 1"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Signe Loftager","key":"okkelspau","last":"Okkels","locid":"52622947-3b99-46c4-bc07-e4eeb441c190","name":"Okkels, Signe Loftager","orcid":"0000-0002-2547-2149","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"loftagerokkelspau","last":"Loftager Okkels","name":"Loftager Okkels, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ditte Rokkjær","key":"dybdalpau","last":"Dybdal","name":"Dybdal, Ditte Rokkjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rie Johanne","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Rie Johanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Tobias Wirenfeldt","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","name":"Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annemarie","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"00ead20c-eb76-4590-b8b3-2a40e479f463","name":"Olsen, Annemarie","orcid":"0000-0002-8335-0588","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Marie","key":"beckpau","last":"Beck","locid":"2d5ae4e8-4bcf-4aed-be6c-31b24effb820","name":"Beck, Anne Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-1210-0167","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne","key":"bügelpau","last":"Bügel","locid":"3e1ceb52-77be-48d7-8fff-5029d6a54a37","name":"Bügel, Susanne Gjedsted","name_org":"Bügel, Susanne","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-0500","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34024505"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnesp.2021.02.002","issn":["24054577"],"issue":"June","journal":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","pages":"137-147","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition ESPEN","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102451944"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","unilabs a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-e692e116-7f2b-466c-a43a-9663bf3c0992","ku-da4d70de-65f2-402c-817b-27375884bf5f"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A culinary twist of a two-course meals-on-wheels menu in a cluster-randomized controlled trial influencing health-related quality of life in nursing home residents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.19-039547","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Titanium nitride (TiN) has emerged as one of the most promising refractory materials for plasmonic and photonic applications at high temperatures due to its prominent optical properties along with mechanical and thermal stability. From a high temperature standpoint, TiN is a substitution for Au and Ag in the visible to near-infrared wavelength range, with potential applications including thermophotovoltaics, thermoplasmonics, hot-electron and high temperature reflective coatings. However, the optical properties and thermal stability of TiN films strongly depend on the growth conditions, such as temperature, partial pressure of the reactive ion gas, ion energy, and substrate orientation. In this work, epitaxial TiN films are grown at 835 °C on an Al2O3 substrate using a radio frequency sputtering method. The oxidization behavior of TiN is investigated at 1000 °C under a medium vacuum condition of 2 × 10–3 mbar, which is relevant for practical technical applications, and the thermal stability at 1400 °C under a high vacuum condition of 2 × 10–6 mbar. The TiN film structure shows an unprecedented structural stability at 1000 °C for a minimum duration of 2 h under a medium vacuum condition, and an exceptional thermal stability at 1400 °C, for 8 h under a high vacuum condition, without any protective coating layer. The work reveals, for the first time to the authors’ knowledge, that the TiN film structure with columnar grains exhibits remarkable thermal stability at 1400 °C due to low-index interfaces and twin boundaries. These findings unlock the fundamental understanding of the TiN material at extreme temperatures and demonstrate a key step towards fabricating thermally stable photonic/plasmonic devices for harsh environments.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Krekeler, Tobias","S. Rout, Surya","V. Krishnamurthy, Gnanavel","Störmer, Michael","Arya, Mahima","Ganguly, Ankita","S. Sutherland, Duncan","i. Bozhevolnyi, Sergey","Ritter, Martin","Pedersen, Kjeld","Yu Petrov, Alexander","Eich, Manfred","Chirumamilla, Manohar"],"cuid":["S03-097.53-011864"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Chirumamilla, Manohar"],"country":["Germany","Russia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hamburg University of Technology","Helmholtz Association of German Research Centres","Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","Institute for Coastal Research, GKSS Research Centre","St. Petersburg National Research University of Information Technologies, Mechanics and Optics (ITMO)"],"keyword":["High temperature stability","Photonics","Plasmonics","Thin films","Titanium nitride"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unprecedented thermal stability of plasmonic titanium nitride films up to 000000001400 c","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/adom.202100323","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors gratefully acknowledge financial support from the German Research Foundation (DFG) via SFB 986 “Tailor‐Made Multi‐Scale Materials Systems: M3,” Project‐ID 192346071, and projects C1, C7, and Z3."],"id":"S03-097.53-011864","identifier":[{"id":"85106739401","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f861d373-d7b2-473b-bb6c-a4ff5d85a03e","au-599914c9-3779-4cff-9b4d-1b927ee2c837","sdu-6034c441-d81e-4227-9653-30367c7c58b3"],"keyword":["high-temperature stability","photonics","plasmonics","thin films","titanium nitride"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-23906987187A7