rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"störmerpau","last":"Störmer","name":"Störmer, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahima","key":"aryapau","last":"Arya","name":"Arya, Mahima","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ankita","key":"gangulypau","last":"Ganguly","name":"Ganguly, Ankita","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Duncan S.","key":"sutherlandpau","last":"Sutherland","locid":"5c5c563f-ca05-4219-b60d-8a3d6303ff2f","name":"Sutherland, Duncan S","name_org":"Sutherland, Duncan S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sergey I.","key":"bozhevolnyipau","last":"Bozhevolnyi","locid":"9df17db0-2e69-41ff-8a38-8738093f0385","name":"Bozhevolnyi, Sergey I.","orcid":"0000-0002-0393-4859","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"ritterpau","last":"Ritter","name":"Ritter, Martin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kjeld","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff5fc0ab-1fa1-47a2-916c-8b7556f2f938","name":"Pedersen, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0002-6835-1566","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"yupetrovpau","last":"Yu Petrov","name":"Yu Petrov, Alexander","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 8 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Yu","key":"petrovpau","last":"Petrov","name":"Petrov, Alexander Yu","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Manfred","key":"eichpau","last":"Eich","name":"Eich, Manfred","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manohar","key":"chirumamillapau","last":"Chirumamilla","name":"Chirumamilla, Manohar","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/adom.202100323","issn":["21951071"],"issue":"16","journal":"Advanced Optical Materials","paperid":"2100323","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Advanced Optical Materials","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106739401"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f861d373-d7b2-473b-bb6c-a4ff5d85a03e","au-599914c9-3779-4cff-9b4d-1b927ee2c837","sdu-6034c441-d81e-4227-9653-30367c7c58b3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Unprecedented Thermal Stability of Plasmonic Titanium Nitride Films up to 1400 °C","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.53-011864","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We investigated the intratumoral source of PD-L1 expression and the infiltration of tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) in large B-cell lymphomas (LBCLs) with or without MYC-translocation, as well as possible correlations to BCL2-and BCL6-translocations and cell of origin (COO). One-hundred and twenty-six patient samples were studied in a cohort enriched for MYC-translocated tumors with 34 samples carrying this translocation. Demonstration of intratumoral distribution and cellular source of PD-L1 was enabled by immunohistochemical (IHC) dual staining specifically highlighting PD-L1 expression in lymphoma B-cells with antibodies against PD-L1 and PAX5. Additional IHC with antibodies against CD68 and CD163 identified TAMs. We found that CD68-positive TAMs were the main source of PD-L1 protein expression in contrast to lymphoma B cells which rarely expressed PD-L1. Semiquantitative IHC demonstrated a significant correlation between CD68 and PD-L1 protein expression. Unsupervised hierarchical analysis of PD-L1, CD68, and CD163 IHC data subsequently demonstrated three potential clusters defined by expression of the three biomarkers. Cluster A consisted of patient samples with significantly lower expression of PD-L1, CD68, and CD163, but also significantly higher prevalence of BCL2-translocation and MYC-BCL2-double-hit (DH) compared to the other two clusters. In cluster C we found a significant accumulation of BCL6 translocated tumors. This cluster in contrast had the highest protein expression of PD-L1, CD68, and CD163. Cluster B tumors had an intermediate expression of the three biomarkers, but no accumulation of the specific genetic translocations. Our data, which were based on morphological analysis, immunophenotyping and genotyping by fluorescence in situ hybridization were in line with new concepts of LBCL taxonomy integrating genetic, phenotypical, and immunological characteristics with identification of new subgroups where MYC translocation and MYC-BCL2 DH may identify a noninflamed subtype. These findings may furthermore hold significant predictive value especially regarding immune checkpoint blockade therapy, but further molecular characterization should be done to substantiate this hypothesis.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Breinholt, Marie F.","Oliveira, Douglas V.N.P.","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","Gang, Anne Ortved","Schejbel, Lone","Pedersen, Mette Ølgod","Elbæk, Mette V.","Clasen-Linde, Erik","Nielsen, Signe Ledou","Knudsen, Helle","Høgdall, Estrid","Larsen, Peter N"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459070"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["MYC","Programmed death ligand 1","Tumor associated macrophages","double hit lymphoma","large B cell lymphoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high grade b cell lymphomas with myc and bcl000000000002 translocations lack tumor associated macrophages and pd l000000000001 expression a possible noninflamed subgroup","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-459070","identifier":[{"id":"85100579383","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33480087","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6de6ccf1-6bf5-40c3-bf1f-0ff18dbc8fa2"],"keyword":["MYC","double-hit lymphoma","immune checkpoint blockade therapy","large B-cell lymphoma","programmed death ligand 1","tumor-associated macrophages"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D2DAD8C5A144086F264B41DB2677E53"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie F.","key":"breinholtpau","last":"Breinholt","name":"Breinholt, Marie F.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Douglas V.N.P.","key":"oliveirapau","last":"Oliveira","name":"Oliveira, Douglas V.N.P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias W.","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","locid":"94ba8398-4108-4dc5-86df-a5a2101e9f97","name":"Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","name_org":"Klausen, Tobias W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne O.","key":"gangpau","last":"Gang","locid":"d6439cff-57cd-406d-b6be-940a96f64f8f","name":"Gang, Anne Ortved","name_org":"Gang, Anne O.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone","key":"schejbelpau","last":"Schejbel","name":"Schejbel, Lone","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"14af7027-aca3-4062-b56e-36867263bc32","name":"Pedersen, Mette Ølgod","name_org":"Pedersen, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette V.","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","name":"Elbæk, Mette V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"clasenlindepau","last":"Clasen-Linde","name":"Clasen-Linde, Erik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe L.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"48a7d837-0860-4ccc-9fc3-0bd30339bfe6","name":"Nielsen, Signe Ledou","name_org":"Nielsen, Signe L.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"26a35a1c-beee-43d8-b46d-ae0089076bb1","name":"Knudsen, Helle","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6d-4a52-a3f3-deb515bdd48f","name":"Høgdall, Estrid","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"443a21ab-2266-47a3-9db7-6757ca35147e","name":"Larsen, Peter N","name_org":"Nørgaard, Peter","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33480087"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/hon.2839","issn":["02780232","10991069"],"issn_org":["02780232"],"issue":"3","journal":"Hematological Oncology","pages":"284-292","status":"p","title":"Hematological Oncology","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100579383"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6de6ccf1-6bf5-40c3-bf1f-0ff18dbc8fa2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-grade B-cell lymphomas with MYC and BCL2 translocations lack tumor-associated macrophages and PD-L1 expression : A possible noninflamed subgroup","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-459070","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: Quinones represent an important group of highly structurally diverse, mainly polyketide-derived secondary metabolites widely distributed among filamentous fungi. Many quinones have been reported to have important biological functions such as inhibition of bacteria or repression of the immune response in insects. Other quinones, such as ubiquinones are known to be essential molecules in cellular respiration, and many quinones are known to protect their producing organisms from exposure to sunlight. Most recently, quinones have also attracted a lot of industrial interest since their electron-donating and -accepting properties make them good candidates as electrolytes in redox flow batteries, like their often highly conjugated double bond systems make them attractive as pigments. On an industrial level, quinones are mainly synthesized from raw components in coal tar. However, the possibility of producing quinones by fungal cultivation has great prospects since fungi can often be grown in industrially scaled bioreactors, producing valuable metabolites on cheap substrates. In order to give a better overview of the secondary metabolite quinones produced by and shared between various fungi, mainly belonging to the genera Aspergillus, Penicillium, Talaromyces, Fusarium, and Arthrinium, this review categorizes quinones into families such as emodins, fumigatins, sorbicillinoids, yanuthones, and xanthomegnins, depending on structural similarities and information about the biosynthetic pathway from which they are derived, whenever applicable. The production of these quinone families is compared between the different genera, based on recently revised taxonomy. Key points: • Quinones represent an important group of secondary metabolites widely distributed in important fungal genera such as Aspergillus, Penicillium, Talaromyces, Fusarium, and Arthrinium. • Quinones are of industrial interest and can be used in pharmacology, as colorants and pigments, and as electrolytes in redox flow batteries. • Quinones are grouped into families and compared between genera according to the revised taxonomy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christiansen, J. V.","Isbrandt, T.","Petersen, Celine","Sondergaard, Teis Esben","Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Sørensen, Jens Laurids","Larsen, T. O.","Frisvad, J. C."],"cuid":["S02-097.86-007484"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Frisvad, J. C.","Frisvad, Jens Christian"],"keyword":["Anthraquinones","Arthrinium","Aspergillus","Benzoquinones","Fusarium","Naphtoquinones","Penicillium","Quinones","Talaromyces"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fungal quinones diversity producers and applications of quinones from i aspergillus penicillium talaromyces fusarium i and i arthrinium i","src":["aau","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/258507681/QUINONE_review_v11.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project was funded by Novo Nordic Foundation (grant no. NNF 18OC0034952)."],"id":"S02-097.86-007484","identifier":[{"id":"34625822","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85116839405","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9a1665f5-d030-4cb1-8db2-665732d6526d","dtu-ad980f36-d29c-45f3-9131-766d156ac18b"],"keyword":["Anthraquinones","Arthrinium","Aspergillus","Benzoquinones","Fusarium","Naphtoquinones","Penicillium","Quinones","Talaromyces"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1E5ED8E92EA8A19F28301D9C817542BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/file