{"abstract":"Purpose: The impact of endogenous androgen levels on the risk of type 2 diabetes in women remains uncertain. The objective was to investigate associations between endogenous androgen levels and risk of type 2 diabetes in young women without established comorbidity. Methods: In this retrospective cohort study, women aged 18 to 50 years who underwent measurement of plasma testosterone, dehydroepiandrosterone-sulfate (DHEA-S), dihydrotestosterone (DHT), and sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) for the first time from January 2007 to December 2015 were included. Androgens were analyzed using tandem liquid chromatography mass spectrometry. Women with established comorbidity were excluded, using Danish healthcare registries. We calculated incidence rate ratios (IRRs, 95% confidence intervals) of type 2 diabetes according to quartiles of plasma androgens using multivariate Poisson regression models. Results: A total of 8876 women, with a mean ± SD age of 38.5 ± 4.6 years and a median (interquartile range [IQR]) follow-up duration of 8.1 (6.6-9.4) years, were eligible for analyses. During 69 728 person-years, 69 women were diagnosed with type 2 diabetes. Women in the highest quartile of plasma total testosterone and calculated free testosterone displayed increased risk of type 2 diabetes compared with the lowest quartile: IRR 1.97 (1.01; 3.85), P = .048 and IRR 7.32 (2.84; 18.83), P < .001. SHBG was inversely associated with type 2 diabetes, Q4 versus Q1; IRR 0.06 (0.02; 0.21), P < .001. Plasma DHEA-S and DHT were not associated with incident type 2 diabetes. Conclusions: Higher levels of plasma total and free testosterone were associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes among women.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jon J","Selmer, Christian","Frøssing, Signe","Schou, Morten","Faber, Jens","Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","Gislason, Gunnar","Køber, Lars","Hougaard, David M","Cohen, Arieh S","Kistorp, Caroline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-478432"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"endogenous testosterone levels are associated with risk of type 000000000002 diabetes in women without established comorbidity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/jendso/bvaa050","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-478432","identifier":[{"id":"85090599304","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32537541","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7278278","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-8e2561fa-367f-4e42-ad46-fda40de115cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-45109746F7591C090A27676343FC7856"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1210/jendso/bvaa050","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250552401/Endogenous_Testosterone_Levels_Are.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jon J","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jon J","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"selmerpau","last":"Selmer","name":"Selmer, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"frøssingpau","last":"Frøssing","name":"Frøssing, Signe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"48fa6ec9-1941-4566-b931-14b0cc8cbae3","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Tobias","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gunnar H","key":"gislasonpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","name_org":"Gislason, Gunnar H","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"køberpau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David M","key":"hougaardpau","last":"Hougaard","name":"Hougaard, David M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Arieh S","key":"cohenpau","last":"Cohen","name":"Cohen, Arieh S","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"kistorppau","last":"Kistorp","locid":"42328645-d772-4f53-9f70-438ff40291b9","name":"Kistorp, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0002-3019-6775","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32537541"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jendso/bvaa050","issn":["07435800","15324206"],"issn_org":["07435800"],"issue":"6","journal":"Endocrine Research","paperid":"bvaa050","status":"p","title":"Endocrine Research","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090599304"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8e2561fa-367f-4e42-ad46-fda40de115cd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Endogenous Testosterone Levels Are Associated with Risk of Type 2 Diabetes in Women without Established Comorbidity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-478432","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this article the results of a survey of the Razavar Valley (north of Kermanshah province) undertaken jointly by the University of Copenhagen and Razi University in the framework of the project \"Tracking Cultural and Environmental Change: Epipaleolithic and Neolithic in Central Zagros\". This part of the Central Zagros has produced some of the earliest evidence of the ‘Neolithic Revolution’ in the eastern Fertile Crescent (e.g. at Asiab, Ganj Dareh, and Sheikhi-Abad), as well as important Middle and Upper Paleolithic remains, but our understanding of the wider landscape context of these sites remains incomplete. We surveyed a part of the Kermanshah plain, otherwise probably the best known area of the Central Zagros that has not yet been systematically explored; the basin of the Razavar River, a tributary of the Qara Su to the north of Kermanshah city. The area is a long but rather wide intermountain with old terraces from the Pleistocene. The abundance of water resources, raw material resources, and fertile agricultural lands has provided the ideal conditions for the formation of human settlements, especially during the Neolithic period. Our aim was to perform a high-coverage, targeted survey with a focus on identifying sites with potential for excavation. We used a tablet-based, “paperless” recording system to map, photograph and document sites,as well as salient natural features such as springs. The survey team was also equipped with GPS tracking watches, to maintain a precise record of which areas were surveyed. In total we identified 59 sites Preliminarily, 19 of these are of potential early prehistoric date, although many are only small surface scatters. 6 of sites belong to the Neolithic including huge Tell sites from PPN period, Teppeh Ghalah B (RZVR67) and Teppeh Salaar Abad (RZVR68), situated in the central part of the valley. A summary of our Neolithic findings at these sites in the Razavar Valley are presented in this article.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Khosravi, Shouku","Pedersen, Patrick Nørskov","Alibaigi, Sajjad","Roe, Joe","Heidary Dastenaei, Mohsen","Miladi, Behzad","Darabi, Hojjat","Richter, Tobias","Mortensen, Peder"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-539306"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Iran"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Razi University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"archaeological landscape of razavar valley in the neolithic period the survey of the 000000000008th 000000000006th millennium b c in the north of kermanshah province","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22084/NBSH.2020.21133.2094","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-539306","ids":["ku-f4622b87-c8e4-4636-a1a6-405bb36df96c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0F034424D83F3C3C9DCF6312D9810080"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258179010/NB_Volume_10_Issue_26_Pages_7_32.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22084/NBSH.2020.21133.2094","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ir","key":"razi university","loc":["Iran","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"Razi University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Cross-Cultural and Regional Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Shouku","key":"khosravipau","last":"Khosravi","name":"Khosravi, Shouku","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Patrick Nørskov","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"3bc10786-6db0-43a3-a028-9de1697afb13","name":"Pedersen, Patrick Nørskov","orcid":"0000-0001-9843-0858","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sajjad","key":"alibaigipau","last":"Alibaigi","name":"Alibaigi, Sajjad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Joe","key":"roepau","last":"Roe","locid":"ac17f6a4-a93a-46b3-871a-ab6072641e76","name":"Roe, Joe","orcid":"0000-0002-1011-1244","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohsen","key":"heidarydastenaeipau","last":"Heidary Dastenaei","name":"Heidary Dastenaei, Mohsen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Behzad","key":"miladipau","last":"Miladi","name":"Miladi, Behzad","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hojjat","key":"darabipau","last":"Darabi","name":"Darabi, Hojjat","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tobias","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","locid":"eacd6ca8-b280-46dd-bd5c-7405e386b59b","name":"Richter, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0001-9902-8852","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peder","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"609de9d4-a88e-4029-873b-557c267adf9d","name":"Mortensen, Peder","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22084/nbsh.2020.21133.2094","issn":["23455225","23455500"],"issn_org":["23455225"],"journal":"Bastanshenasi Iran","pages":"7-32","status":"p","title":"Bastanshenasi Iran","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f4622b87-c8e4-4636-a1a6-405bb36df96c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Archaeological Landscape of Razavar Valley in the Neolithic Period, The survey of the 8th - 6th millennium B.C in the North of Kermanshah Province","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-539306","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Pedersen, Tobias Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063466"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jeg har udviklet en metode til at analysere corona prøver","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-063466","ids":["aau-2e3d99f4-9fcc-4cd5-8391-4e85746298a6"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E12127AD5A11ECF86BE173E7DD021024"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Functional Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Bruun","key":"pedersenppu","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc73daa2-870d-4de9-bf18-bd8a23efc501","name":"Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","rank":1,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Engineer the Future","publisher_org":"Engineer The Future","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2e3d99f4-9fcc-4cd5-8391-4e85746298a6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Jeg har udviklet en metode til at analysere Corona-prøver","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063466","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The productivity of fish populations varies naturally over time, dependent on integrated effects of abundance, ecological factors, and environmental conditions. These changes can be expressed as gradual or abrupt shifts in productivity as well as fluctuations on any time scale from seasonal oscillations to long-term changes. This study considers three extensions to biomass dynamic models that accommodate time-variant productivity in fish populations. Simulation results reveal that neglecting seasonal changes in productivity can bias derived stock sustainability reference levels and, thus, fisheries management advice. Results highlight the importance of biannual biomass indices and their timing relative to the peaks of the seasonal processes (i.e. recruitment, growth, mortality) for the estimation of seasonally time-variant productivity. The application to real-world data of the eastern Baltic cod (Gadus morhua) stock shows that the model is able to disentangle differences in seasonal fishing mortality as well as seasonal and long-term changes in productivity. The combined model with long-term and seasonally varying productivity performs significantly better than models that neglect time-variant productivity. The model extensions proposed here allow to account for time-variant productivity of fish populations leading to increased reliability of derived reference levels.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mildenberger, Tobias","Berg, Casper Willestofte","Pedersen, Martin Wæver","Kokkalis, Alexandros","Nielsen, J. Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319047"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mildenberger, Tobias"],"keyword":["Fish stock assessment","Fisheries management","Maximum sustainable yield","Population dynamics","SPiCT","Seasonality","Surplus production model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"time variant productivity in biomass dynamic models on seasonal and long term scales","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265048299/tvp_maintext.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319047","identifier":[{"id":"85082032050","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-30a52f3e-b8c5-4745-adf1-442de22c4d15"],"keyword":["Eastern Baltic cod (Gadus morhua)","Fish stock assessment","Fisheries management","Maximum sustainable yield","Population dynamics","SPiCT","Seasonality","Surplus production model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-96373259122AF4BB187ED846DFD37B16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265048299/tvp_maintext.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"mildenbergerpau","last":"Mildenberger","locid":"563a243d-0a7b-401c-a1a7-fcc5a5495e93","name":"Mildenberger, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-6631-7524","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Casper Willestofte","key":"bergpau",