{"abstract":"The discovery of drivers of cancer has traditionally focused on protein-coding genes1–4. Here we present analyses of driver point mutations and structural variants in non-coding regions across 2,658 genomes from the Pan-Cancer Analysis of Whole Genomes (PCAWG) Consortium5 of the International Cancer Genome Consortium (ICGC) and The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA). For point mutations, we developed a statistically rigorous strategy for combining significance levels from multiple methods of driver discovery that overcomes the limitations of individual methods. For structural variants, we present two methods of driver discovery, and identify regions that are significantly affected by recurrent breakpoints and recurrent somatic juxtapositions. Our analyses confirm previously reported drivers6,7, raise doubts about others and identify novel candidates, including point mutations in the 5′ region of TP53, in the 3′ untranslated regions of NFKBIZ and TOB1, focal deletions in BRD4 and rearrangements in the loci of AKR1C genes. We show that although point mutations and structural variants that drive cancer are less frequent in non-coding genes and regulatory sequences than in protein-coding genes, additional examples of these drivers will be found as more cancer genomes become available.","author_count":52,"contributors":["Rheinbay, Esther","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Abascal, Federico","Wala, Jeremiah A","Shapira, Ofer","Tiao, Grace","Hornshøj, Henrik","Hess, Julian M","Juul, Randi Istrup","Lin, Ziao","Feuerbach, Lars","Sabarinathan, Radhakrishnan","Madsen, Tobias","Kim, Jaegil","Mularoni, Loris","Shuai, Shimin","Lanzós, Andrés","Herrmann, Carl","Maruvka, Yosef E","Shen, Ciyue","Amin, Samirkumar B","Bandopadhayay, Pratiti","Bertl, Johanna","Boroevich, Keith A","Busanovich, John","Carlevaro-Fita, Joana","Chakravarty, Dimple","Chan, Calvin Wing Yiu","Craft, David","Dhingra, Priyanka","Diamanti, Klev","Fonseca, Nuno A","Gonzalez-Perez, Abel","Guo, Qianyun","Hamilton, Mark P","Haradhvala, Nicholas J","Hong, Chen","Isaev, Keren","Johnson, Todd A","Juul, Malene","Kahles, Andre","Kahraman, Abdullah","Kim, Youngwook","Komorowski, Jan","Kumar, Kiran","Kumar, Sushant","Lee, Donghoon","Sidiropoulos, Nikos","Weischenfeldt, Joachim","Pedersen, Jakob Skou"],"cuid":["S02-096.58-022813"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["PCAWG Consortium","PCAWG Drivers and Functional Interpretation Working Group"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Japan","Poland","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Baylor College of Medicine","Broad Institute","Cornell University","Dana-Farber Cancer Institute","European Bioinformatics Institute","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","Harvard University","Heidelberg University ","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Institute for Research in Biomedicine","Institute of Computer Science of the Polish Academy of Sciences","Ontario Institute for Cancer Research","Pompeu Fabra University","RIKEN Center for Life Science Technologies","University of Bern","University of Cambridge","University of Lausanne","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","Uppsala University","Weill Cornell Medical College","Wellcome Sanger Institute","Yale University"],"keyword":["Annotation","Discovery","Expression","GENES","Landscape","REGULATORY MUTATIONS","Recurrent","Selection","TARGET","TERT PROMOTER MUTATIONS"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Informatics and Biocomputing Platform, Ontario Institute for Cancer Research, Toronto, Ontario, Canada."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyses of non coding somatic drivers in 000000000002 000000000658 cancer whole genomes","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-1965-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.58-022813","identifier":[{"id":"85079047263","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000529097800009","type":"wos"},{"id":"32025015","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7054214","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-8b3918ce-bf15-46dc-bd2a-ddf64a39fada","ku-a9364ec5-9bfe-4c5c-9712-690b3d0fb5ac"],"keyword":["ANNOTATION","DISCOVERY","EXPRESSION","GENES","LANDSCAPE","RECURRENT","REGULATORY MUTATIONS","SELECTION","TARGET","TERT PROMOTER MUTATIONS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-41101DAD4EFFBEE2539D70250E422AE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-020-1965-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236174565/s41586_020_1965_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/220346031/s41586_020_1965_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"broad institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Broad Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clin