en","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"gimsingpeterpau","last":"Gimsing","name":"Gimsing, Peter","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"frederiksenhenrikpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Henrik","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardnielspau","last":"Abildgaard","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1182/blood-2019-128074","issn":["00064971","15280020"],"issn_org":["00064971"],"issue":"Suppl 1","journal":"Blood","paperid":"1849","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Blood","volume":"134"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d8438e60-e3fc-4402-acbc-17a8832e656e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Validation of a new clinical prediction model for outcome in newly diagnosed multiple myeloma patients not eligible for autologous stem-cell transplantation; A population-based study from the Danish National Multiple Myeloma Registy","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-252810","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Diffuse gliomas are the most common primary malignant brain tumor. Although extracranial metastases are rarely observed, recent studies have shown the presence of circulating tumor cells (CTCs) in the blood of glioma patients, confirming that a subset of tumor cells are capable of entering the circulation. The isolation and characterization of CTCs could provide a non-invasive method for repeated analysis of the mutational and phenotypic state of the tumor during the course of disease. However, the efficient detection of glioma CTCs has proven to be challenging due to the lack of consistently expressed tumor markers and high inter- and intra-tumor heterogeneity. Thus, for this field to progress, an omnipresent but specific marker of glioma CTCs is required. In this article, we demonstrate how the recombinant malaria VAR2CSA protein (rVAR2) can be used for the capture and detection of glioma cell lines that are spiked into blood through binding to a cancer-specific oncofetal chondroitin sulfate (ofCS). When using rVAR2 pull-down from glioma cells, we identified a panel of proteoglycans, known to be essential for glioma progression. Finally, the clinical feasibility of this work is supported by the rVAR2-based isolation and detection of CTCs from glioma patient blood samples, which highlights ofCS as a potential clinical target for CTC isolation.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Bang-Christensen, Sara R","Pedersen, Rasmus S","Ayres Pereira, Marina","Clausen, Thomas Mandel","Løppke, Caroline","Sand, Nicolai T","Ahrens, Theresa D","Jørgensen, Amalie M","Lim, Yi Chieh","Goksøyr, Louise","Choudhary, Swati","Gustavsson, Tobias","Dagil, Robert","Daugaard, Mads","Sander, Adam F.","Torp, Mathias H","Søgaard, Max","Theander, Thor G","Østrup, Olga","Lassen, Ulrik","Hamerlik, Petra","Salanti, Ali","Agerbæk, Mette Ø"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-536429"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"capture and detection of circulating glioma cells using the recombinant var000000000002csa malaria protein","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8090998","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-536429","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6769911","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"31466397","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083694995","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-efa0d0ff-f274-4873-a191-6b94e481bd19"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F23161B56DD754E1914A94C60D247AB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8090998","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/238529871/cells_08_00998_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, CMP"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_