{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: In patients with large B-cell lymphoma (LBCL) according to WHO, the prognostic significance of MYC translocation is still not sufficiently clarified. We therefore aimed to investigate whether prognostication could be improved in patients with MYC translocation positive LBCL by additional stratification according to MYC and BCL2 protein expression levels or MYC translocation partner gene as well as concurrent BCL2 and/or BCL6 translocation (DH). METHODS: From an unselected consecutive cohort of >600 patients with LBCL investigated with fluorescent in situ hybridization (FISH), 64 patients were diagnosed with MYC translocation positive LBCL and included in the study. They were further investigated for supplemental translocations with FISH and MYC and BCL2 protein expression with immunohistochemistry (IHC). RESULTS: MYC expression >75% was associated with both reduced progression-free survival (PFS) and overall survival (OS) (PFS: HR 6.8 (95% CI 1.5-31), P = 0.004. OS: HR 4.3 (95% CI 0.9-21), P = 0.05). Immunoglobulin (IG) MYC translocation partner gene was related to high MYC protein expression (P = 0.047) but was not prognostic for PFS (P = 0.8) or OS (P = 0.6). DH did not confer a worse outcome compared to MYC single hit (SH). These findings were confirmed in a comparable, independent validation cohort of 28 patients with MYC translocation positive LBCL. All patients included in the survival analyses were treated with R-CHOP (rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, vincristine, and prednisone) or R-CHOEP (R-CHOP + etoposide). CONCLUSION: These findings suggest that in patients with LBCL stratification by MYC protein expression level significantly improves the prognostic impact associated with MYC translocation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Pedersen, Mette Ølgod","Gang, Anne Ortved","Clasen-Linde, Erik","Breinholt, Marie Fredslund","Knudsen, Helle","Nielsen, Signe Ledou","Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","Høgdall, Estrid","Nørgaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-540770"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols adverse effects","Biomarkers Tumor","Female","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Neoplasm Staging","Oncogene Proteins Fusion genetics","Prognosis","Proto Oncogene Proteins c myc genetics","Translocation Genetic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stratification by myc expression has prognostic impact in myc translocated b cell lymphoma identifies a subgroup of patients with poor outcome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-540770","identifier":[{"id":"85062550038","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30737994","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f6cde3a0-cbce-4668-8eec-08b449207969"],"keyword":["Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols/adverse effects","Biomarkers, Tumor","Female","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Lymphoma, B-Cell/diagnosis","Male","Neoplasm Staging","Oncogene Proteins, Fusion/genetics","Prognosis","Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-myc/genetics","Translocation, Genetic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-348A7A2D8CEC08ABD82B6305DD72FB13"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Ølgod","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"14af7027-aca3-4062-b56e-36867263bc32","name":"Pedersen, Mette Ølgod","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Ortved","key":"gangpau","last":"Gang","locid":"d6439cff-57cd-406d-b6be-940a96f64f8f","name":"Gang, Anne Ortved","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik","key":"clasenlindepau","last":"Clasen-Linde","name":"Clasen-Linde, Erik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie Fredslund","key":"breinholtpau","last":"Breinholt","name":"Breinholt, Marie Fredslund","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Helle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe Ledou","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Signe Ledou","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tim Svenstrup","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Tim Svenstrup","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias Wirenfeldt","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","name":"Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Estrid","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"a48f77b8-ee6d-4a52-a3f3-deb515bdd48f","name":"Høgdall, Estrid","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Peter","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30737994"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejh.13219","issn":["09024441","09024506"],"issn_org":["09024441"],"issue":"5","journal":"European Journal of Haematology","pages":"395-406","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Haematology","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85062550038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f6cde3a0-cbce-4668-8eec-08b449207969"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stratification by MYC expression has prognostic impact in MYC translocated B-cell lymphoma-Identifies a subgroup of patients with poor outcome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-540770","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, the availability of reduced representation library (RRL) methods has catalysed an expansion of genome-scale studies to characterize both model and non-model organisms. Most of these methods rely on the use of restriction enzymes to obtain DNA sequences at a genome-wide level. These approaches have been widely used to sequence thousands of markers across individuals for many organisms at a reasonable cost, revolutionizing the field of population genomics. However, there are still some limitations associated with these methods, in particular, the high molecular weight DNA required as starting material, the reduced number of common loci among investigated samples, and the short length of the sequenced site-associated DNA. Here, we present MobiSeq, a RRL protocol exploiting simple laboratory techniques, that generates genomic data based on PCR targeted-enrichment of transposable elements and the sequencing of the associated flanking region. We validate its performance across 103 DNA extracts derived from three mammalian species: grey wolf (Canis lupus), red deer complex (Cervus sp.), and brown rat (Rattus norvegicus). MobiSeq enables the sequencing of hundreds of thousands loci across the genome, and performs SNP discovery with relatively low rates of clonality. Given the ease and flexibility of MobiSeq protocol, the method has the potential to be implemented for marker discovery and population genomics across a wide range of organisms - enabling the exploration of diverse evolutionary and conservation questions. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Rey-Iglesia, Alba","Gopalakrishan, Shyam","Carøe, Christian","Alquezar-Planas, David E.","Nielsen, Anne Ahlmann","Röder, Timo","Bruhn Pedersen, Lene","Naesborg-Nielsen, Christina","Sinding, Mikkel-Holger S.","Fredensborg Rath, Martin","Li, Zhipeng","Petersen, Bent","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Bunce, Michael","Mourier, Tobias","Hansen, Anders Johannes"],"cuid":["S02-083.88-035963"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Anders Johannes"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Curtin University"],"keyword":["Genotyping","Population genomics","Reduced representation library","SNP discovery","Te","Transposable elements"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobiseq de novo snp discovery in model and non model species through sequencing the flanking region of transposable elements","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250426691/Rey_Iglesia_et_al_2019_Molecular_Ecology_Resources_MobiSeq_De_novo_SNP_discovery_in_model_and_non_model_species_through_sequencing_the_flanking_region_of_transposable_elements_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful to all the people and institutions that have provided samples for this study, specifically Department of Environment Nunavut, Environment and Natural Resources Northwest Territories, and Lindsey Carmichael and David Coltman at University of Alberta (wolf samples); Frank Zachos (Natural History Museum in Vienna); Meirav Meiri (Tel Aviv University); Adrian Lister, Ian Barnes and Richard Sabin (Natural History Museum of London); Kristian Murphy Gregersen (Natural History Museum of Denmark); Rolf Langvatn (University Centre in Svalbard); and Gennady Baryshnikov (Russian Academy of Sciences, Moscow) (deer material). We also thank Lasse Vinner for experimental methodology discussions; Maria Asplund for discussion on data analysis in the early stages of the project; and The Danish National Advanced Technology Foundation. S.G. was funded by EU Marie Skłodowska‐Curie Grant 655732 (Wherewolf)."],"id":"S02-083.88-035963","identifier":[{"id":"000459815200017","type":"wos"},{"id":"85061303011","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30575257","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-939ba213-105c-4c6e-b3f1-e6ca764b5818","ku-1e01080c-1f16-42ae-b2bc-500dec0dd781"],"keyword":["Genotyping","Population genomics","Reduced representation library","SNP discovery","TE","Transposable elements"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6B5919A16E20B76FBE5B29E478928C87"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164225625/Rey_Iglesia_et_al_2018_Molecular_Ecology_Resources.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250426691/Rey_Iglesia_et_al_2019_Molecular_Ecology_Resources_MobiSeq_De_novo_SNP_discovery_in_model_and_non_model_species_through_sequencing_the_flanking_region_of_transposable_elements_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"curtin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Curtin University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alba","key":"reyiglesiapau","last":"Rey-Iglesia","locid":"3762f335-5f40-4693-9e84-353e78a02999","name":"Rey-Iglesia, Alba","orcid":"0000-0002-3768-9185","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shyam","key":"gopalakrishanpau","last":"Gopalakrishan","locid":"916fe6ce-9552-4c02-821d-a3daf516e32b","name":"Gopalakrishan, Shyam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"carøepau","last":"Carøe","locid":"ac9e0369-c0ab-4484-a7d3-08d2600928e0","name":"Carøe, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"David E.","key":"alquezarplanaspau","last":"Alquezar-Planas","locid":"6d751051-1a76-4887-b5b6-1b65ee529788","name":"Alquezar Planas, David Eugenio","name_org":"Alquezar-Planas, David E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Ahlmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6a334744-bbe2-4f8f-9f5a-de93253b0d71","name":"Nielsen, Anne Ahlmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Timo","key":"röderpau","last":"Röder","name":"Röder, Timo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Bruhn","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2aaa32e9-09e5-49b8-9c59-67cdaef43a21","name":"Pedersen, Lene Bruhn","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christina","key":"næsborgnielsenpau","last":"Næsborg-Nielsen","name":"Næsborg-Nielsen, Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel-Holger S.","key":"sindingpau","last":"Sinding","locid":"d441872e-7274-486b-b9b2-0c0ee8bb3545","name":"Sinding, Mikkel Holger S.","name_org":"Sinding, Mikkel-Holger S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1371-219X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Fredensborg","key":"rathpau","last":"Rath","locid":"17e1980e-e336-4c55-ad3e-9e680dcd8364","name":"Rath, Martin Fredensborg","orcid":"0000-0002-4047-6324","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhipeng","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Zhipeng","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bent","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"483a94e4-a22f-4192-aa04-100588c07904","name":"Petersen, Bent","orcid":"0000-0002-2472-8317","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M Thomas P","key":"gilbertpau","last":"Gilbert","locid":"58c97189-c7e9-4486-afb1-e7669608599e","name":"Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","name_org":"Gilbert, M Thomas P","orcid":"0000-0002-5805-7195","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"buncepau","last":"Bunce","name":"Bunce, Michael","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"mourierpau","last":"Mourier","locid":"a25925b1-60da-485a-8ad5-9b6025d3cba8","name":"Mourier, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-2727-1903","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Johannes","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"846e4329-bfc5-4ddb-968c-445cdb16825a","name":"Hansen, Anders Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-1890-2702","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30575257"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1755-0998.12984","issn":["1365294X","1755098X"],"issn_org":["1755098X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Molecular Ecology Resources","pages":"512-525","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Molecular Ecology Resources","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061303011"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-939ba213-105c-4c6e-b3f1-e6ca764b5818","ku-1e01080c-1f16-42ae-b2bc-500dec0dd781"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MobiSeq: De Novo SNP discovery in model and non-model species through sequencing the flanking region of transposable elements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.88-035963","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To determine the diagnostic accuracy of 68gallium prostate-specific membrane antigen (PSMA)-based positron emission tomography/computed tomography (PET/CT) in comparison with 18F-fluoride-based PET/CT (NaF-PET/CT) and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging (WB-MRI) for the detection of bone metastases in patients with prostate cancer. METHODS: Sixty patients with prostate cancer were included in the period May 2016 to June 2017. The participants underwent three scans (index tests) within 30 days: a NaF-PET/CT, a WB-MRI and a PSMA-PET/CT. Experienced specialists assessed the scans. In the absence of a histological reference standard, the final diagnosis was determined as a panel diagnosis. Measures of the diagnostic performances of the index tests were calculated from patient-based dichotomous outcomes (0 or ≥ 1 bone metastasis) and pairwise compared (McNemar test). For each index test, the agreement with the final diagnosis with regard to the number of bone metastases detected (0, 1-5, > 5) and the inter-reader agreement was calculated (kappa coefficients). RESULTS: Fifty-five patients constituted the final study population; 20 patients (36%) were classified as having bone metastatic disease as their final diagnosis. The patient-based diagnostic performances were (sensitivity, specificity, overall accuracy) PSMA-PET/CT (100%, 100%, 100%), NaF-PET/CT (95%, 97%, 96%) and WB-MRI (80%, 83%, 82%). The overall accuracy of PSMA-PET/CT was significantly more favourable compared to WB-MRI (p = 0.004), but not to NaF-PET/CT (p = 0.48). PSMA-PET/CT classified the number of bone metastases reliably compared to the final diagnosis (kappa coefficient 0.97) and with an \"almost perfect\" inter-reader agreement (kappa coefficient 0.93). CONCLUSIONS: The overall accuracy of PSMA-PET/CT was significantly more advantageous compared to WB-MRI, but not to NaF-PET/CT. KEY POINTS: • PSMA-PET/CT assessed the presence of bone metastases correctly in all 55 patients • PSMA-PET/CT was more advantageous compared to WB-MRI • No difference was found between PSMA-PET/CT and NaF-PET/CT.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Dyrberg, Eva","Hendel, Helle W","Huynh, Tri Hien Viet","Klausen, Tobias Wirenfeldt","Løgager, Vibeke B","Madsen, Claus","Pedersen, Erik Morre","Pedersen, Maria","Thomsen, Henrik S"],"cuid":["S02-099.81-022064"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms diagnosis","Bone and Bones","Humans","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Magnetic Resonance Imaging methods","Male","Metastasis","Middle Aged","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography","Positron Emission Tomography Computed Tomography methods","Prospective Studies","Prostatic Neoplasms","Prostatic Neoplasms pathology","Reproducibility of Results","Whole Body Imaging methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sup 000000000068 sup ga psma pet ct in comparison with sup 000000000018 sup f fluoride pet ct and whole body mri for the detection of bone metastases in patients with prostate cancer a prospective diagnostic accuracy study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85052604103","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.81-022064","identifier":[{"id":"30132104","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85052604103","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-80bee78a-a380-4666-bb11-748cd1a969f0","ku-40988c70-f24c-4383-959f-09b7cd898622"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Antigens, Surface/pharmacology","Bone Neoplasms/diagnosis","Bone and bones","Gallium Radioisotopes/pharmacology","G