{"abstract":"Fusarium pseudograminearum is a significant pathogen of cereals in arid regions worldwide and has the ability to produce numerous bioactive secondary metabolites. The genome sequences of seven F. pseudograminearum strains have been published and in one of these strains, C5834, we identified an intact gene cluster responsible for biosynthesis of the cyclic lipopeptide fusaristatin A. The high level of sequence identity of the fusaristatin cluster remnant in strains that do not produce fusaristatin suggests that the absence of the cluster evolved once, and subsequently the resulting locus with the cluster fragments became widely dispersed among strains of F. pseudograminearum in Australia. We examined a selection of 99 Australian F. pseudograminearum isolates to determine how widespread the ability to produce fusaristatin A is in F. pseudograminearum. We identified 15 fusaristatin producing strains, all originating from Western Australia. Phylogenetic analyses could not support a division of F. pseudograminearum into fusaristatin producing and nonproducing populations, which could indicate the loss has occurred relatively recent.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wollenberg, Rasmus","Sondergaard, Teis Esben","Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Knutsson, Simon","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Westphal, Klaus Ringsborg","Wimmer, Reinhard","Gardiner, Donald Max","Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093449"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CSIRO"],"keyword":["Evolution","Fusarium crown rot","Non ribosomal peptides","Polyketides","Secondary metabolites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"there it is i fusarium pseudograminearum i did not lose the fusaristatin gene cluster after all","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/305772430/There_it_is_Fusarium_pseudograminearum_did_not_lose_the_fusa_2018_Fungal_Bi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was funded by the Danish Research Council, Technology and Production (grant no. 4005-00204B ) and the Novo Nordisk Foundation ( NNF15OC0016028 and NNF15OC0016186 ). The collection of isolates used in this study was funded in various projects by the Australian Grain Research and Development and Research Corporation and CSIRO. Isolate RBG5266 was a kind gift from the Royal Botanic Gardens of Sydney. The authors wish to thank laboratory trainees Belinda Sandvang Jensen and Karoline Andersen for extracting DNA and Camilla Juel Høj for extracting secondary metabolites from F. pseudograminearum . The NMR laboratory at Aalborg University is supported by the Obel, SparNord and Carlsberg Foundations. Appendix A"],"id":"S01-000.00-093449","identifier":[{"id":"85056165316","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-95985954-1274-4fed-a49e-c196d444d515"],"keyword":["Evolution","Fusarium crown rot","Non-ribosomal peptides","Polyketides","Secondary metabolites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B74ED965A6B47F305FD4E9CFB10925A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/305772430/There_it_is_Fusarium_pseudograminearum_did_not_lose_the_fusa_2018_Fungal_Bi.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"csiro","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"CSIRO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Dam","key":"wollenbergpau","last":"Wollenberg","locid":"fa21c1a2-3d8f-47c4-b52d-ecf1acc9535e","name":"Wollenberg, Rasmus","name_org":"Wollenberg, Rasmus Dam","orcid":"0000-0002-8320-2497","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Teis Esben","key":"sondergaardpau","last":"Sondergaard","locid":"c4550265-7489-4e7e-a723-b7cfef89912e","name":"Sondergaard, Teis Esben","orcid":"0000-0002-4455-7498","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Rank","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1f966c21-5cb9-4909-9f4c-d694ffd9becc","name":"Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","orcid":"0000-0003-2408-9444","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon","key":"knutssonpau","last":"Knutsson","locid":"a520f6bf-af8b-4a84-9c27-f750638a6699","name":"Knutsson, Simon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Bruun","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bc73daa2-870d-4de9-bf18-bd8a23efc501","name":"Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klaus Ringsborg","key":"westphalpau","last":"Westphal","locid":"c21eaaaf-2ceb-4130-b15e-2cd64b5b0a6c","name":"Westphal, Klaus Ringsborg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","