{"abstract":"Background: Viruses and other infectious agents cause more than 15% of human cancer cases. High-throughput sequencing-based studies of virus-cancer associations have mainly focused on cancer transcriptome data. Methods: In this study, we applied a diverse selection of presequencing enrichment methods targeting all major viral groups, to characterize the viruses present in 197 samples from 18 sample types of cancerous origin. Using high-throughput sequencing, we generated 710 datasets constituting 57 billion sequencing reads. Results: Detailed in silico investigation of the viral content, including exclusion of viral artefacts, from de novo assembled contigs and individual sequencing reads yielded a map of the viruses detected. Our data reveal a virome dominated by papillomaviruses, anelloviruses, herpesviruses, and parvoviruses. More than half of the included samples contained 1 or more viruses; however, no link between specific viruses and cancer types were found. Conclusions: Our study sheds light on viral presence in cancers and provides highly relevant virome data for future reference.","author_count":46,"contributors":["Mollerup, Sarah","Asplund, Maria","Friis-Nielsen, Jens","Kjartansdóttir, Kristín Rós","Fridholm, Helena","Hansen, Thomas Arn","Herrera, José Alejandro Romero","Barnes, Christopher James","Jensen, Randi Holm","Richter, Stine Raith","Nielsen, Ida Broman","Pietroni, Carlotta","Alquezar-Planas, David E","Rey-Iglesia, Alba","Olsen, Pernille V S","De Meyts, Ewa Rajpert-","Groth-Pedersen, Line","von Buchwald, Christian","Jensen, David H","Gniadecki, Robert","Høgdall, Estrid","Langhoff, Jill Levin","Pete, Imre","Vereczkey, Ildikó","Baranyai, Zsolt","Dybkær, Karen","Johnsen, Hans Erik","Steiniche, Torben","Hokland, Peter","Rosenberg, Jacob","Baandrup, Ulrik","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Willerslev, Eske","Brunak, Søren","Lund, Ole","Mourier, Tobias","Vinner, Lasse","Izarzugaza, Jose M G","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Hansen, Anders Johannes"],"cuid":["S04-097.41-008153"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mollerup, Sarah"],"country":["Hungary"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Institute of Oncology","Semmelweis University"],"keyword":["Artefacts","CELL","Cancer","Enrichment","High throughput sequencing","Human","Human papillomavirus","Infection","Next generation sequencing","Samples","Vaccine","Virome","Virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Centre for GeoGenetics, Natural History Museum of Denmark, University of Copenhagen, DK Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high throughput sequencing based investigation of viruses in human cancers by multi enrichment approach","src":["aau","au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/infdis/jiz318","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-097.41-008153","identifier":[{"id":"31253993","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000490988000011","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC6743825","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85072234028","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a8b6be0c-34de-4fcf-b6ef-ab0d8ac39650","au-56ee3a2b-589e-42fe-907d-07784bffb461","dtu-a07fb38a-547c-400b-9696-2b2ddcb68b6d","ku-c48f709f-f48a-4edd-80be-e3e4e62ff20d"],"keyword":["Artefacts","CELL","HUMAN-PAPILLOMAVIRUS","INFECTION","In-depth analysis","Next generation sequencing","SAMPLES","VACCINE","Virus","cancer","enrichment","high-throughput sequencing