,"url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-000127","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: Motif analysis methods have long been central for studying biological function of nucleotide sequences. Functional genomics experiments extend their potential. They typically generate sequence lists ranked by an experimentally acquired functional property such as gene expression or protein binding affinity. Current motif discovery tools suffer from limitations in searching large motif spaces, and thus more complex motifs may not be included. There is thus a need for motif analysis methods that are tailored for analyzing specific complex motifs motivated by biological questions and hypotheses rather than acting as a screen based motif finding tool. Methods: We present Regmex (REGular expression Motif EXplorer), which offers several methods to identify overrepresented motifs in ranked lists of sequences. Regmex uses regular expressions to define motifs or families of motifs and embedded Markov models to calculate exact p-values for motif observations in sequences. Biases in motif distributions across ranked sequence lists are evaluated using random walks, Brownian bridges, or modified rank based statistics. A modular setup and fast analytic p value evaluations make Regmex applicable to diverse and potentially large-scale motif analysis problems. Results: We demonstrate use cases of combined motifs on simulated data and on expression data from micro RNA transfection experiments. We confirm previously obtained results and demonstrate the usability of Regmex to test a specific hypothesis about the relative location of microRNA seed sites and U-rich motifs. We further compare the tool with an existing motif discovery tool and show increased sensitivity. Conclusions: Regmex is a useful and flexible tool to analyze motif hypotheses that relates to large data sets in functional genomics. The method is available as an R package (https://github.com/muhligs/regmex).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Tataru, Paula","Madsen, Tobias","Hobolth, Asger","Pedersen, Jakob Skou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-229357"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Morten Muhlig"],"keyword":["Binding","Signatures"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regmex a statistical tool for exploring motifs in ranked sequence lists from genomics experiments","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13015-018-0135-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-229357","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6286601","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85058122502","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000452704400001","type":"wos"},{"id":"30555524","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-af5a472d-a2f5-4ead-b231-8391fbdc25cc"],"keyword":["BINDING","OCCURRENCES","SIGNATURES"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EDB23CA935FEA521A8CE9B261579C20"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/139017515/s13015_018_0135_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13015-018-0135-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Muhlig","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ce46d54c-d3eb-48f7-91ab-3439edeeb46a","name":"Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"tatarupau","last":"Tataru","locid":"4969ba5c-0416-4aac-aa18-2c348ef6819c","name":"Tataru, Paula","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"357e5996-0e47-4e89-9ed6-42b1b76660ae","name":"Madsen, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger","key":"hobolthpau","last":"Hobolth","locid":"8d387f4e-86e9-4405-a50d-1e5a6efd97d8","name":"Hobolth, Asger","orcid":"0000-0003-4056-1286","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Skou","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9c14e87f-2dc3-4c08-a074-146337aff8a0","name":"Pedersen, Jakob Skou","orcid":"0000-0002-7236-4001","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30555524"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13015-018-0135-2","issn":["17487188"],"issue":"1","journal":"Algorithms for Molecular Biology","paperid":"17","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Algorithms for Molecular Biology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058122502"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-af5a472d-a2f5-4ead-b231-8391fbdc25cc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Regmex : A statistical tool for exploring motifs in ranked sequence lists from genomics experiments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-229357","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We demonstrate a gigahertz source of verifiable quantum random numbers based on homodyne detection of the vacuum state. Using a whitening filter, we generate iid samples with a potential randomness rate of 20Gbit/s.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kordts, Arne","Lupo, Cosmo","Nikolic, Dino Solar","Pedersen, Thomas Bachau","Gehring, Tobias","Andersen, Ulrik Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-341233"],"event":{"end":"2018-05-18","place":"San Jose, us","start":"2018-05-13","title":"2018 Conference on Lasers and Electro-Optics (CLEO)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of York"],"keyword":["Correlation","Cryptography","Digital signal processing","Generators","Physics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security verification for vacuum fluctuation based quantum random number generator","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-341233","ids":["dtu-7adb67a7-6221-440f-80a1-515620e83928"],"keyword":["Correlation","Cryptography","Digital signal processing","Elementary particle vacuum","Generators","Physics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-D15016E33A6344106A675FD94079EAFB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Quantum Physics and Information Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Cryptomathic A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arne","key":"kordtspau","last":"Kordts","locid":"550438fd-b272-4a79-8249-d4b0dcb4fba2","name":"Kordts, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-5826-2319","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cosmo","key":"lupopau","last":"Lupo","name":"Lupo, Cosmo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dino S.","key":"nikolicpau","last":"Nikolic","locid":"88c57926-8459-42b8-b3d9-2f6e189dac90","name":"Nikolic, Dino Solar","name_org":"Nikolic, Dino S.","orcid":"0000-0003-1653-4018","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Bachau","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Thomas Bachau","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"gehringpau","last":"Gehring","locid":"9d770890-d39e-4a90-b4bf-345098e747c9","name":"Gehring, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4311-2593","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d1c6f584-4c31-410d-8879-7669229593fb","name":"Andersen, Ulrik Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-1990-7687","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781943580422"],"isbn":["9781538657331"],"pages":"1-2","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 Conference on Lasers and Electro-Optics (CLEO)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85049141386","2-s2.0-85052564951"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","cryptomathic a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7adb67a7-6221-440f-80a1-515620e83928"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Security verification for vacuum fluctuation based quantum random number generator","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-341233","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Most Fusarium species produce bikaverin and aurofusarin for mycelium pigmentation and fusarubins for perithecial pigmentation [1]. However, Fusarium solani produces fusarubins during mycelial growth and another unknown pigment during sexual reproduction. This unknown pigment is predicted to be biosynthesized by a non-reducing polyketide synthase (PKS35 = PKSN [2]). PKS35 encodes a 2106 aa protein and share 52% identity to PhnA from P. herquei, which catalyzes the first step of the herqueinone biosynthetic pathway [3]. Genetic analyses of the PKS35 gene cluster suggests that it contains eleven genes, of which four are present in the herqueinone cluster. Herqueinone contains tricyclic phenalenone core ring structure cyclized by a FAD-dependent monooxygenase. To unravel the biosynthetic products in the PKS35 pathway the intron stripped PKS was cloned and put under control of a galactose inducible promoter in a 2µ vector, which was transformed into a Saccharomyces cerevisiae strain co-expressing a Sfp-Type 4′-Phosphopantetheinyl Transferase (Ppt1). The transformed yeast strain was cultivated under induced conditions in liquid cultures for five days and before production of secondary metabolites was analyzed by high-resolution mass spectrometry (HRMS). The results showed that the yeast strain was able to produce prephenalenone, which is also the first step of the herqueinone pathway. We also detected dehydroxyprephenalenone, which is formed through spontaneous dehydration [3]. Through heterologous expression of the other genes in the cluster, we will follow the biosynthetic route and ultimately unravel the entire pathway of the perithecial pigment of F. solani. [1] Studt L, Wiemann P, Kleigrewe K et al (2012): Appl Environ Microbiol, 78: 4468-4480. [2] Graziani S, Vasnier C, Daboussi MJ (2004): Appl Environ Microbiol, 70: 2984-2988. [3] Gao SS, Duan A, Xu W et al (2016): J Am Chem Soc, 138: 4249-4259.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","Pedersen, Tobias Bruun","Wollenberg, Rasmus","Sondergaard, Teis Esben","Sørensen, Jens Laurids"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093566"],"event":{"end":"2018-04-11","place":"Tulln, at","start":"2018-04-08","title":"European Fusarium Seminar 14","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of the first steps in phenalenone pigment biosynthesis in fusarium solani","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/334500014/PKS35_tulln3_MRN.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093566","ids":["aau-960a0deb-d4a2-4c7f-b9bb-25f647b33ea4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-60260612A08C43F9F18CC9EB95E5EBD1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/334500014/PKS35_tulln3_MRN.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Chemical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Rank","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1f966c21-5cb9-4909-9f4c-d694ffd9becc","name":"Nielsen, Mikkel Rank","orcid":"0000-0003-2408-