ps://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-000378","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Non-coding mutations may drive cancer development. Statistical detection of non- coding driver regions is challenged by a varying mutation rate and uncertainty of functional impact. Here, we develop a statistically founded non-coding driver-detection method, ncdDetect, which includes sample-specific mutational signatures, long-range mutation rate variation, and position-specific impact measures. Using ncdDetect, we screened non-coding regulatory regions of protein-coding genes across a pan-cancer set of whole-genomes (n = 505), which top-ranked known drivers and identified new candidates. For individual candidates, presence of non-coding mutations associates with altered expression or decreased patient survival across an independent pan-cancer sample set (n = 5454). This includes an antigen-presenting gene (CD1A), where 5’UTR mutations correlate significantly with decreased survival in melanoma. Additionally, mutations in a base-excision-repair gene (SMUG1) correlate with a C-to-T mutational-signature. Overall, we find that a rich model of mutational heterogeneity facilitates non-coding driver identification and integrative analysis points to candidates of potential clinical relevance.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Juul, Malene","Bertl, Johanna","Guo, Qianyun","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Świtnicki, Michał P","Hornshøj, Henrik","Madsen, Tobias","Hobolth, Asger","Pedersen, Jakob Skou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-232604"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non coding cancer driver candidates identified with a sample and position specific model of the somatic mutation rate","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.21778","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-232604","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5440169","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85019709734","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28362259","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-b5001113-ca71-4157-b01c-939d56f9e163"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4C74FF277155B33AFFA4089559DC49EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.21778","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e3719ff-26a4-4a1f-bec2-ebe32b44f24b","name":"Juul, Malene","name_org":"Rasmussen, Malene Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanna","key":"bertlpau","last":"Bertl","locid":"c95ddcbf-3f64-4581-b47c-7a7b3e212be8","name":"Bertl, Johanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qianyun","key":"guopau","last":"Guo","locid":"53ae21c8-c72f-40a0-aba1-eb804771e278","name":"Guo, Qianyun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Muhlig","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ce46d54c-d3eb-48f7-91ab-3439edeeb46a","name":"Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michał","key":"świtnickipau","last":"Świtni