{"abstract":"In this article a framework for robust design and variation management is proposed by combining central models to Robust Design, namely, the Quality Loss Function, the Transfer Function, and the Domains of Axiomatic Design. The Variation Management Framework (VMF) shows how variation can be mapped from production variation right through to the quality loss perceived by the customer for a single characteristic chain. Seven levers which can be activated to increase product quality are described and positioned on the VMF and variation metrics are proposed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Howard, Thomas J.","Eifler, Tobias","Pedersen, Søren Nygaard","Göhler, Simon Moritz","Boorla, Srinivasa Murthy","Christensen, M. E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356371"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Howard, Thomas J."],"keyword":["Quality Loss","Reliability engineering","Robust design","Variation management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-NOVO","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the variation management framework vmf a unifying graphical representation of robust design","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/163090146/A_Framework_for_Robust_Design_and_Variation_Management.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356371","identifier":[{"id":"85015247003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ad71dfab-9bd3-4d70-a214-5464748e3593"],"keyword":["Quality engineering","Quality loss","Reliability engineering","Robust design","VMF","Variation management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6E32BA2246CFE4C1E790F21A86F5DC2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/163090146/A_Framework_for_Robust_Design_and_Variation_Management.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Engineering Design and Product Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-NOVO","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk Foundation","namevar":["Novo Nordisk Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas J.","key":"howardpau","last":"Howard","locid":"f0a461fa-62fc-48c1-890a-8f3b07b23d80","name":"Howard, Thomas J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2927-1897","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"eiflerpau","last":"Eifler","locid":"2c991ed4-93e0-405f-a1bf-5d28bb1d2771","name":"Eifler, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1293-3313","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5c662409-baa1-4b33-a456-63ec089b1f88","name":"Pedersen, Søren Nygaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Moritz","key":"göhlerpau","last":"Göhler","locid":"2adc2220-dc12-4fbe-9b9e-2cc8b0db0db1","name":"Göhler, Simon Moritz","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Srinivasa Murthy","key":"boorlapau","last":"Boorla","locid":"ea7a49ca-346b-4bef-bc80-1704875207b5","name":"Boorla, Srinivasa Murthy","orcid":"0000-0001-7793-2832","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. E.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, M. E.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08982112.2016.1272121","issn":["08982112","15324222"],"issn_org":["08982112"],"issue":"4","journal":"Quality Engineering","pages":"563-572","publisher":"Taylor & Francis Inc.","status":"p","title":"Quality Engineering","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015247003"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ad71dfab-9bd3-4d70-a214-5464748e3593"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The variation management framework (VMF): A unifying graphical representation of robust design","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356371","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The era of ‘big data’ studies and computational social science has recently given rise to a number of realignments within and beyond the social sciences, where otherwise distinct data formats – digital, numerical, ethnographic, visual, etc. – rub off and emerge from one another in new ways. This article chronicles the collaboration between a team of anthropologists and sociologists, who worked together for one week in an experimental attempt to combine ‘big’ transactional and ‘small’ ethnographic data formats. Our collaboration is part of a larger cross-disciplinary project carried out at the Danish Technical University (DTU), where high-resolution transactional data from smartphones allows for recordings of social networks amongst a freshman class (N = 800). With a parallel deployment of ethnographic fieldwork among the DTU students, this research set-up raises a number of questions concerning how to assemble disparate ‘data-worlds’ and to what epistemological and political effects? To address these questions, a specific social event – a lively student party – was singled out from the broader DTU dataset. Our experimental collaboration used recordings of Bluetooth signals between students’ phones to visualize the ebb and flow of social intensities at the DTU party, juxtaposing these with ethnographic field-notes on shifting party atmospheres. Tracing and reflecting on the process of combining heterogeneous data, the article offers a concrete case of how a ‘stitching together’ of digital and ethnographic data-worlds might take place.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Blok, Anders","Carlsen, Hjalmar Alexander Bang","Jørgensen, Tobias Bornakke","Madsen, Mette My","Ralund, Snorre","Pedersen, Morten Axel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455557"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Big social data","Complementarity","Ethnography","Experiment","Faculty of Social Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stitching together the heterogenous party a complementary social data science experiment","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2053951717736337","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-455557","identifier":[{"id":"85068373258","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6805fc12-8715-447e-9d04-beef730a1220"],"keyword":["Big social data","Faculty of Social Sciences","complementarity","data-worlds","ethnography","experiment","party sociality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7797F7314FDFA1DC7F516A442B6C2537"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2053951717736337","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"blokpau","last":"Blok","locid":"303f5c18-72f5-4b2a-8a4c-dfbe18008345","name":"Blok, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-3403-698X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hjalmar Alexander Bang","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"e84f3312-176b-4855-ac39-72eb473ba6a0","name":"Carlsen, Hjalmar Alexander Bang","orcid":"0000-0002-2638-0932","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias Bornakke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9efae2ff-f7f9-48b7-a400-8033cc150c49","name":"Jørgensen, Tobias Bornakke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette My","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"af9d97f8-bb79-40b9-b0ff-227a10ffe369","name":"Madsen, Mette My","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Snorre","key":"ralundpau","last":"Ralund","locid":"06b1f049-f3d5-4e28-bcf6-587a75c11a16","name":"Ralund, Snorre","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Axel","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"36e8fb75-1af4-4030-b2c3-77255dc97fe7","name":"Pedersen, Morten Axel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/2053951717736337","issn":["20539517"],"journal":"Big Data & Society","pages":"1-15","status":"p","title":"Big Data & Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068373258"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6805fc12-8715-447e-9d04-beef730a1220"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stitching together the heterogenous party : A complementary social data science experiment","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455557","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Peberspray blev introduceret i dansk politi i 2008 med henblik på at reducere skader på borgere og betjente. Siden da er politiets brug af stav og skydevåben mindsket, men den samlede brug af magtmidler er tredoblet. Vi analyserer dette misforhold mellem hensigt og virkning ved at undersøge, hvordan danske politibetjente forholder sig til brugen af peberspray sammenlignet med andre magtmidler. Undersøgelsen bygger på interviews med ni politibetjente fra tre danske politikredse. Betjentene er overordnet meget positive over for peberspray, men beskriver også problemer med risiko for sekundær eksponering og falsk tryghedsfølelse. Vi identificerer yderligere tre gennemgående temaer i betjentenes forklaringer, som omhandler typiske situationer, afvejningen mellem spray eller stav og forholdet mellem smerte eller skade. Afslutningsvis diskuterer vi betjentenes perspektiver med afsæt i Sykes og Matzas (1957) teknikker til neutralisering af normoverskridende handlinger. Keywords: use of force, pepper spray, OC spray, neutralization","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Anne Juul","Nielsen, Josefine","Kammersgaard, Tobias","Hald, Christina Østergaard","Møller, Kim"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-011763"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"danske politibetjentes perspektiver på peberspray som magtmiddel","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18261/issn.1894-8693-2017-01-07","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-011763","ids":["aau-f61972c2-665a-432c-8c9a-625982045b16","au-ae49916e-0520-42ff-9931-6ea803688f79"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C404D013EDBCFE4595C9E019DF96808B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/119032592/danske_politibetjentes_perspektiver_paapeberspray_som_magtm.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18261/issn.1894-8693-2017-01-07","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.idunn.no/nordisk_politiforskning/2017/01/danske_politibetjentes_perspektiver_paapeberspray_som_magtm","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences","Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - Centre for Alcohol and Drug Research, Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Sociology and Social Work, CASTOR - Sociological and criminological research on social differentiation and social control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Juul","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anne Juul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Josefine","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Josefine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"kammersgaardpau","last":"Kammersgaard","locid":"1e01206b-4f87-4fe4-8783-2690a6cfb472","name":"Kammersgaard, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-4551-5131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Østergaard","key":"haldpau","last":"Hald","name":"Hald, Christina Østergaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"338e32f8-8b56-4e83-bb07-1487cc5e6b7e","name":"Møller, Kim","orcid":"0000-0002-4417-1253","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18261/issn.1894-8693-2017-01-07","issn":["18948693"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordisk Politiforskning","pages":"89-107","publisher":"Universitetsforlaget","status":"p","title":"Nordisk Politiforskning","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f61972c2-665a-432c-8c9a-625982045b16","au-ae49916e-0520-42ff-9931-6ea803688f79"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Danske politibetjentes perspektiver på peberspray som magtmiddel","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-011763","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Immunoparesis (hypogammaglobulinemia) is associated to an unfavorable prognosis in newly diagnosed Multiple myeloma (MM) patients. However, this finding has not been validated in an unselected population-based cohort. We analyzed 2558 newly diagnosed MM patients in the Danish Multiple Myeloma Registry representing the entire MM population in Denmark from 2005-2013. Two-thousand two hundred and fifty three patients (90%) presented with reduction below lower normal levels of at least one uninvolved immunoglobulin. Using multivariable Cox regression we found that high age, high ISS score, high LDH and IgA MM were associated to both shorter overall survival and progression free survival. Furthermore, bone marrow plasma cell % was associated to short progression free survival. Immunoparesis had no independent significant effect on OS (HR 0.9 (95%CI: 0.7;1.0; p = 0.12)). Likewise, the number of suppressed immunoglobulins or the relative degree of suppressed uninvolved immunoglobulins from lower normal level (quantitative immunoparesis) was not associated to OS in the multivariable analysis. However, quantitative immunoparesis with at least 25% reduction (from lower normal level) of uninvolved immunoglobulins was associated to shorter PFS for the entire population. The impact of quantitative immunoparesis on PFS was present irrespective of calendar periods 2005-2008 and 2009-2013. Our population-based study does not confirm that immunoparesis at diagnosis is an independent prognostic factor regarding OS. However, quantitative immunoparesis is associated to a shorter PFS.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Sørrig, Rasmus","Klausen, Tobias W","Salomo, Morten","Vangsted, Annette J","Frølund, Ulf Christian","Andersen, Kristian T","Klostergaard, Anja","Helleberg, Carsten","Pedersen, Robert S","Pedersen, Per T","Helm-Petersen, Sissel","Teodorescu, Elena Manuela","Preiss, Birgitte","Abildgaard, Niels","Gimsing, Peter","Svirskaite, Asta","Teodorescu, Elena Manuela","Johnsen, Hans Erik","Gregersen, Henrik","Gade, Inger Lise","Bødker, Julie Støve"],"cuid":["S04-089.79-004514"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corpau":["Danish Myeloma Study Group","Danish Myeloma Study Grp"],"corresponding_author":["Sorrig, Rasmus"],"keyword":["CELLS","Criteria","Journal Article","Mechanisms","Registry","Risk stratification","Suppression"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Hematological Research Laboratory, Herlev Hospital, Herlev, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunoparesis in newly diagnosed multiple myeloma patients effects on overall survival and progression free survival in the danish population","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0188988","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-089.79-004514","identifier":[{"id":"85037606674","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29216227","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5720701","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000417337800055","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-5ce8a483-549f-4f74-8fa5-8fe2bd95b7c4","au-b8306320-13f0-439b-b816-34ea7deddb45","ku-45c8e60f-aa8c-45dc-b9bd-f369ed271d87","sdu-a62e005e-2bd5-445b-a848-960c92f73f73"],"keyword":["CELLS","CRITERIA","Journal Article","MECHANISMS","REGISTRY","RISK STRATIFICATION","SUPPRESSION","UNINVOLVED IMMUNOGLOBULINS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-2176B57422DD14094AA8AC2CD4589F76"],"oa_link":