{"abstract":"A microwave sensing system for estimating deflection of a wind turbine blade is presented. The system measures distances at two ultrawideband (UWB) wireless links between one antenna at the tip and two antennas at the root of the blade, which allows for determination of the tip position by triangulation. An experimental setup with corner reflector antenna mounted at the tip and horn antennas at the root of a 37.3 m long blade is described. Analyzing the data from the experiment, special attention is given to the propagation aspects of the UWB links, with focus on the multipath effects caused by the blade. It is demonstrated that despite the adverse effects of the multipath propagation the ranging accuracy of the system amounts to 1.5 cm, leading to maximum error of deflection 4.5 %.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Franek, Ondrej","Zhang, Shuai","Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","Olesen, Kim","Byskov, Claus","Pedersen, Gert Frølund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-113992"],"event":{"acronym":"ICEAA","end":"2016-09-23","place":"Cairns, au","start":"2016-09-19","title":"2016 International Conference on Electromagnetics in Advanced Applications / IEEE-APS Topical Conference on Antennas and Propagation in Wireless Communications","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LM"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LM","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"wind turbine blade deflection sensing system based on uwb technology","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/245349347/deflection_sensing_openaccess.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-113992","identifier":[{"id":"85003874432","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dbfd62f4-bb8d-4463-8940-91a5a01b2798"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A81CA88536C526FE2F6FC0EB45E2807D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/245349347/deflection_sensing_openaccess.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lm wind power","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LM","l3nn":"LM Wind Power","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"LM Wind Power","namevar":["LM Wind Power"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ondrej","key":"franekpau","last":"Franek","locid":"abf85df6-62dd-4b00-8f4b-4d75a780b723","name":"Franek, Ondrej","orcid":"0000-0003-4928-2208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shuai","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"c97f8895-893d-4895-bc19-d7bf7d5fe6d9","name":"Zhang, Shuai","orcid":"0000-0002-9003-2879","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Lindstrøm","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a2e382fc-c4c6-4ff2-b7d2-8b012eb5160e","name":"Jensen, Tobias Lindstrøm","orcid":"0000-0003-4262-0577","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patrick Claus F.","key":"eggerspau","last":"Eggers","locid":"f054cb97-cef9-4540-a4db-37441facf026","name":"Eggers, Patrick Claus F.","orcid":"0000-0002-2359-9779","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"aa6eeabd-33cb-4ca5-bab9-16cdf79fde26","name":"Olesen, Kim","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"byskovpau","last":"Byskov","name":"Byskov, Claus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gert F.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a49c73ee-aed0-448c-8a92-792c9ee12a9e","name":"Pedersen, Gert Frølund","name_org":"Pedersen, Gert F.","orcid":"0000-0002-6570-7387","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/apwc.2016.7738172","edition":"6th","eisbn":["9781509004706"],"pages":"260-263","place":"Cairns, Australia","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"Antennas and Propagation in Wireless Communications (APWC), 2016 IEEE-APS Topical Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85003874432"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dbfd62f4-bb8d-4463-8940-91a5a01b2798"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Wind Turbine Blade Deflection Sensing System Based on UWB Technology","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113992","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Motivation: Cancer development and progression is driven by a complex pattern of genomic and epigenomic perturbations. Both types of perturbations can affect gene expression levels and disease outcome. Integrative analysis of cancer genomics data may therefore improve detection of perturbed genes and prediction of disease state. As different data types are usually dependent, analysis based on independence assumptions will make inefficient use of the data and potentially lead to false conclusions. Model: Here, we present PINCAGE (Probabilistic INtegration of CAncer GEnomics data), a method that uses probabilistic integration of cancer genomics data for combined evaluation of RNA-seq gene expression and 450k array DNA methylation measurements of promoters as well as gene bodies. It models the dependence between expression and methylation using modular graphical models, which also allows future inclusion of additional data types. Results: We apply our approach to a Breast Invasive Carcinoma dataset from The Cancer Genome Atlas consortium, which includes 82 adjacent normal and 730 cancer samples. We identify new biomarker candidates of breast cancer development (PTF1A, RABIF, RAG1AP1, TIMM17A, LOC148145) and progression (SERPINE3, ZNF706). PINCAGE discriminates better between normal and tumour tissue and between progressing and non-progressing tumours in comparison with established methods that assume independence between tested data types, especially when using evidence from multiple genes. Our method can be applied to any type of cancer or, more generally, to any genomic disease for which sufficient amount of molecular data is available.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Świtnicki, Michał P","Juul, Malene","Madsen, Tobias","Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard","Pedersen, Jakob Skou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-130637"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pincage probabilistic integration of cancer genomics data for perturbed gene identification and sample classification","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84966454922","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-130637","identifier":[{"id":"26740525","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84966454922","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-026e5491-9366-43db-8b40-fcead5767254"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-70C6997A3709F723EDC6D03CEECE2CAA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michał P","key":"świtnickipau","last":"Świtnicki","locid":"533adf28-7a85-4f12-b1bd-a5b5d69e83c3","name":"Świtnicki, Michał P","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e3719ff-26a4-4a1f-bec2-ebe32b44f24b","name":"Juul, Malene","name_org":"Rasmussen, Malene Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"357e5996-0e47-4e89-9ed6-42b1b76660ae","name":"Madsen, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karina D","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"41846f4d-63e9-4498-ac72-0a788c36e789","name":"Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard","name_org":"Sørensen, Karina D","orcid":"0000-0002-4902-5490","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob S","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9c14e87f-2dc3-4c08-a074-146337aff8a0","name":"Pedersen, Jakob Skou","name_org":"Pedersen, Jakob S","orcid":"0000-0002-7236-4001","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26740525"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btv758","issn":["13674803","13674811"],"issn_org":["13674803"],"issue":"9","journal":"Bioinformatics","pages":"1353-1365","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Bioinformatics","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84966454922"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-026e5491-9366-43db-8b40-fcead5767254"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"PINCAGE : Probabilistic integration of cancer genomics data for perturbed gene identification and sample classification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-130637","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Comparative anatomy and physiology are disciplines related to structures and mechanisms in three-dimensional (3D) space. For the past centuries, scientific reports in these fields have relied on written descriptions and two-dimensional (2D) illustrations, but in recent years 3D virtual modeling has entered the scene. However, comprehending complex anatomical structures is hampered by reproduction on flat inherently 2D screens. One way to circumvent this problem is in the production of 3D-printed scale models. We have applied computed tomography and magnetic resonance imaging to produce digital models of animal anatomy well suited to be printed on low-cost 3D printers. In this communication, we report how to apply such technology in comparative anatomy and physiology to aid discovery, description, comprehension and communication, and we seek to inspire fellow researchers in these fields to embrace this emerging technology.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lauridsen, Henrik","Hansen, Kasper","Nørgård, Mathias Ørum","Wang, Tobias","Pedersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-216700"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Additive manufacturing","Comparative anatomy","Comparative physiology","Imaging","Three dimensional printing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from tissue to silicon to plastic 000000000003d printing in comparative anatomy and physiology","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.150643","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-216700","identifier":[{"id":"84960382110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-99558bdf-7aa3-456b-864c-82d797d0913b"],"keyword":["Additive manufacturing","Comparative anatomy","Comparative physiology","Imaging","Three-dimensional printing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4659D9F548739DF53629219DF846D0EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4821264/pdf/rsos150643.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.150643","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Comparative Medicine Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aarhus school of architecture","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-AAA","l3nn":"Aarhus School of Architecture","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aarhus School of Architecture","namevar":["Arkitektskolen Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-AAA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"e9b42d0f-74e8-4835-92a3-18ce72bfafa6","name":"Lauridsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8833-4456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"38a9d794-f230-4f50-9327-a06057880fff","name":"Hansen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8669-8897","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Ørum","key":"nørgårdpau","last":"Nørgård","name":"Nørgård, Mathias Ørum","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"871199c4-33bb-4fac-95ef-9a2266f30695","name":"Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1146-0382","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1098/rsos.150643","issn":["20545703"],"issue":"3","journal":"Royal Society Open Science","paperid":"150643","publisher":"ROYAL SOC","status":"p","title":"Royal Society Open Science","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960382110"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-99558bdf-7aa3-456b-864c-82d797d0913b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"From tissue to silicon to plastic: 3D printing in comparative anatomy and physiology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-216700","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Motif analysis has long been an important method to characterize biological functionality and the current growth of sequencing-based genomics experiments further extends its potential. These diverse experiments often generate sequence lists ranked by some functional property. There is therefore a growing need for motif analysis methods that can exploit this coupled data structure and be tailored for specific biological questions. Here, we present an exploratory motif analysis tool, Regmex (REGular expression Motif EXplorer), which offers several methods to evaluate the correlation of motifs with sequence rank. Regmex uses regular expressions to define motifs or families of motifs and embedded Markov models to calculate exact probabilities for motif observations in sequences. Motif enrichment is optionally calculated using random walk, Brownian bridge, or modified rank based statistics. These features make Regmex well suited for a range of biological sequence analysis problems related to motif discovery, exemplified by microRNA seed enrichment, but also including enrichment problems involving complex motifs and combinations of motifs. We demonstrate a number of usage scenarios that take advantage of the regular expression feature, including enrichments for combinations of different microRNA seed sites. The method is implemented and made publicly available as an R package and supports high parallelization on multi-core machinery.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Tataru, Paula","Madsen, Tobias","Hobolth, Asger","Pedersen, Jakob Skou"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-245568"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motif discovery in ranked lists of sequences","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/suppl/2016/01/11/035956.DC2/035956-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-245568","ids":["au-cb6d322d-cad7-459e-90e3-4ea6a9513649"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-271C2F7E5CE0155079A64BCDB99F3839"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/suppl/2016/01/11/035956.DC2/035956-1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Muhlig","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"ce46d54c-d3eb-48f7-91ab-3439edeeb46a","name":"Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"tatarupau","last":"Tataru","locid":"4969ba5c-0416-4aac-aa18-2c348ef6819c","name":"Tataru, Paula","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"357e5996-0e47-4e89-9ed6-42b1b76660ae","name":"Madsen, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Asger","key":"hobolthpau","last":"Hobolth","locid":"8d387f4e-86e9-4405-a50d-1e5a6efd97d8","name":"Hobolth, Asger","orcid":"0000-0003-4056-1286","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Skou","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9c14e87f-2dc3-4c08-a074-146337aff8a0","name":"Pedersen, Jakob Skou","orcid":"0000-0002-7236-4001","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"4","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cb6d322d-cad7-459e-90e3-4ea6a9513649"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Motif discovery in ranked lists of sequences","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-245568","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
