{"abstract":"The first epigenomes from archaic hominins (AH) and ancient anatomically modern humans (AMH) have recently been characterized, based, however, on a limited number of samples. The extent to which ancient genome-wide epigenetic landscapes can be reconstructed thus remains contentious. Here, we present epiPALEOMIX, an open-source and user-friendly pipeline that exploits post-mortem DNA degradation patterns to reconstruct ancient methylomes and nucleosome maps from shotgun and/or capture-enrichment data. Applying epiPALEOMIX to the sequence data underlying 35 ancient genomes including AMH, AH, equids and aurochs, we investigate the temporal, geographical and preservation range of ancient epigenetic signatures. We first assess the quality of inferred ancient epigenetic signatures within well-characterized genomic regions. We find that tissue-specific methylation signatures can be obtained across a wider range of DNA preparation types than previously thought, including when no particular experimental procedures have been used to remove deaminated cytosines prior to sequencing. We identify a large subset of samples for which DNA associated with nucleosomes is protected from post-mortem degradation, and nucleosome positioning patterns can be reconstructed. Finally, we describe parameters and conditions such as DNA damage levels and sequencing depth that limit the preservation of epigenetic signatures in ancient samples. When such conditions are met, we propose that epigenetic profiles of CTCF binding regions can be used to help data authentication. Our work, including epiPALEOMIX, opens for further investigations of ancient epigenomes through time especially aimed at tracking possible epigenetic changes during major evolutionary, environmental, socioeconomic, and cultural shifts.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hanghøj, Kristian","Seguin, Andaine","Schubert, Mikkel","Madsen, Tobias","Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Willerslev, Eske","Orlando, Ludovic"],"cuid":["S02-098.37-020917"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Ancient DNA","DNA methylation","Epigenome","Nucleosome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast accurate and automatic ancient nucleosome and methylation maps with epipaleomix","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msw184","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.37-020917","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5100044","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27624717","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85016227802","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-70a29b13-be38-4795-b671-6615a9875e92","ku-07023f13-623a-423b-ba92-599a619b8e75"],"keyword":["Ancient DNA","DNA methylation","Epigenome","Nucleosome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5B90823AF05AF0C4A633898EC95B2F00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msw184","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/173092410/Hangh_j_2016_Fast_accurate_and_automatic.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)","Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Bioinformatics Research Centre (BiRC)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Ebbesen","key":"hanghøjpau","last":"Hanghøj","locid":"a17e9d55-e472-4c3b-b988-a1e924c30337","name":"Hanghøj, Kristian","name_org":"Hanghøj, Kristian Ebbesen","orcid":"0000-0003-1941-5495","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andaine","key":"seguinorlandopau","last":"Seguin-Orlando","locid":"4881f1ae-15f4-4a5a-bb7e-5852a69dd784","name":"Seguin-Orlando, Andaine","orcid":"0000-0002-8265-3229","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"schubertpau","last":"Schubert","locid":"3368f298-8b81-4bf8-b6a6-35e76446fb75","name":"Schubert, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0003-2401-9921","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"357e5996-0e47-4e89-9ed6-42b1b76660ae","name":"Madsen, Tobias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Skou","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9c14e87f-2dc3-4c08-a074-146337aff8a0","name":"Pedersen, Jakob Skou","orcid":"0000-0002-7236-4001","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eske","key":"willerslevpau","last":"Willerslev","locid":"21d2e042-0513-44fe-8acd-56b0d00a603e","name":"Willerslev, Eske","orcid":"0000-0002-7081-6748","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ludovic Antoine Alexandre","key":"orlandopau","last":"Orlando","locid":"87f03604-118c-4ae2-8f1c-a692b08ab5fd","name":"Orlando, Ludovic Antoine Alexandre","orcid":"0000-0003-3936-1850","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27624717"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/molbev/msw184","issn":["07374038","15371719"],"issn_org":["07374038"],"issue":"12","journal":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","pages":"3284-3298","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Molecular Biology and Evolution","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016227802"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-70a29b13-be38-4795-b671-6615a9875e92","ku-07023f13-623a-423b-ba92-599a619b8e75"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fast, accurate and automatic ancient nucleosome and methylation maps with epiPALEOMIX","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.37-020917","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer (NMIBC) is a heterogeneous disease with widely different outcomes. We performed a comprehensive transcriptional analysis of 460 early-stage urothelial carcinomas and showed that NMIBC can be subgrouped into three major classes with basal- and luminal-like characteristics and different clinical outcomes. Large differences in biological processes such as the cell cycle, epithelial-mesenchymal transition, and differentiation were observed. Analysis of transcript variants revealed frequent mutations in genes encoding proteins involved in chromatin organization and cytoskeletal functions. Furthermore, mutations in well-known cancer driver genes (e.g., TP53 and ERBB2) were primarily found in high-risk tumors, together with APOBEC-related mutational signatures. The identification of subclasses in NMIBC may offer better prognostication and treatment selection based on subclass assignment.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Hedegaard, Jakob","Lamy, Philippe","Nordentoft, Iver","Algaba, Ferran","Høyer, Søren","Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","Vang, Søren","Reinert, Thomas","Hermann, Gregers G","Mogensen, Karin","Thomsen, Mathilde Borg Houlberg","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Marquez, Mirari","Segersten, Ulrika","Aine, Mattias","Höglund, Mattias","Birkenkamp-Demtröder, Karin","Fristrup, Niels","Borre, Michael","Hartmann, Arndt","Stöhr, Robert","Wach, Sven","Keck, Bastian","Seitz, Anna Katharina","Nawroth, Roman","Maurer, Tobias","Tulic, Cane","Simic, Tatjana","Junker, Kerstin","Horstmann, Marcus","Harving, Niels","Petersen, Astrid Christine","Calle, M Luz","Steyerberg, Ewout W","Beukers, Willemien","van Kessel, Kim E M","Jensen, Jørgen Bjerggaard","Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Malmström, Per-Uno","Malats, Núria","Real, Francisco X","Zwarthoff, Ellen C","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Dyrskjøt, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002247"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"con