{"abstract":"BackgroundNineteen clinically normal snakes: six ball pythons (Python regius), six Burmese pythons (Python bivittatus), one Children¿s python (Antaresia childreni), four Amazon tree boas (Corallus hortulanus), and two Malagasy ground boas (Acrantophis madagascariensis) were subjected to ultrasound imaging with 21 MHz (ball python) and 50 MHz (ball python, Burmese python, Children¿s python, Amazon tree boa, Malagasy ground boa) transducers in order to measure the different structures of the anterior segment in clinically normal snake eyes with the aim to review baseline values for clinically important ophthalmic structures. The ultrasonographic measurements included horizontal spectacle diameter, spectacle thickness, depth of sub-spectacular space and corneal thickness. For comparative purposes, a formalin-fixed head of a Burmese python was subjected to micro computed tomography.ResultsIn all snakes, the spectacle was thinner than the cornea. There was significant difference in spectacle diameter, and spectacle and corneal thickness between the Amazon tree boa and the Burmese and ball pythons. There was no difference in the depth of the sub-spectacular space. The results obtained in the Burmese python with the 50 MHz transducer were similar to the results obtained with micro computed tomography. Images acquired with the 21 MHz transducer included artifacts which may be misinterpreted as ocular structures.ConclusionsOur measurements of the structures in the anterior segment of the eye can serve as orientative values for snakes examined for ocular diseases. In addition, we demonstrated that using a high frequency transducer minimizes the risk of misinterpreting artifacts as ocular structures.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lauridsen, Henrik","Da Silva, Mari-Ann O","Hansen, Kasper","Jensen, Heidi Meldgaard","Warming, Mads Kristian","Wang, Tobias","Pedersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-169080"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ultrasound imaging of the anterior section of the eye of five different snake species","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12917-014-0313-5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-169080","identifier":[{"id":"84965189298","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4302111","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25547871","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-45a60aeb-da05-4403-bf7d-51a7568a6834"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2768E5D4DAE04009FC50D5E39682EEE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12917-014-0313-5","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Comparative Medicine Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"e9b42d0f-74e8-4835-92a3-18ce72bfafa6","name":"Lauridsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8833-4456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mari-Ann O","key":"dasilvapau","last":"Da Silva","name":"Da Silva, Mari-Ann O","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"38a9d794-f230-4f50-9327-a06057880fff","name":"Hansen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8669-8897","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Heidi M","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b731eb82-16d8-4b6b-93e4-28b18bb13cf5","name":"Jensen, Heidi Meldgaard","name_org":"Jensen, Heidi M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Kristian","key":"warmingpau","last":"Warming","locid":"e63ec5a0-1c8c-4951-bc07-4f67da85f9ab","name":"Warming, Mads Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2d30a18d-7b6a-42f0-858b-f2672008d8f3","name":"Pedersen, Michael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25547871"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12917-014-0313-5","issn":["17466148"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Veterinary Research","pages":"959","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Veterinary Research","title_org":"B M C Veterinary Research","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84965189298"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-45a60aeb-da05-4403-bf7d-51a7568a6834"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Ultrasound imaging of the anterior section of the eye of five different snake species","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-169080","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Robust Design is an approach to reduce the effects of variation. There are numerous tools,methods and models associated with robust design, however, there is both a lack of a processmodel formalising the step of a robust design process and a framework tying the models together.In this paper we propose a framework for robust design and variation management bycombining central models to Robust Design, namely, the Quality Loss Function, the TransferFunction and the Domains of Axiomatic Design. The framework shows how variation can bemapped from production right through to quality loss in the market place and identifies areaswhere action can be taken against variation. An additional benefit of the framework is that itmakes the link between visual/sensory/perceptual robustness, product robustness, and productionvariation (Six Sigma).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Howard, Thomas J.","Christensen, Martin Ebro","Eifler, Tobias","Pedersen, S.","Göhler, Simon Moritz","Christiansen, A.","Rafn, A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352872"],"event":{"end":"2014-08-15","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2014-08-14","title":"1st International Symposium on Robust Design","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Quality Loss","Reliability engineering","Robust design","Variation management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the variation management framework vmf for robust design","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/102244037/171_175_ISoRD14_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352872","ids":["dtu-a1dcc9bd-1d73-4175-b2d2-b431821ade08"],"keyword":["Quality Loss","Reliability Engineering","Robust Design","Variation Management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2A35013A7577BFB01B7F343339D35209"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4122/dtu:2104","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/102244037/171_175_ISoRD14_Proceedings.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Engineering Design and Product Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas J.","key":"howardpau","last":"Howard","locid":"f0a461fa-62fc-48c1-890a-8f3b07b23d80","name":"Howard, Thomas J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2927-1897","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"ebropau","last":"Ebro","locid":"bf7c78bf-f49a-48e2-a4c1-130ae8e7a510","name":"Christensen, Martin Ebro","name_org":"Ebro, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"eiflerpau","last":"Eifler","locid":"2c991ed4-93e0-405f-a1bf-5d28bb1d2771","name":"Eifler, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-1293-3313","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Moritz","key":"göhlerpau","last":"Göhler","locid":"2adc2220-dc12-4fbe-9b9e-2cc8b0db0db1","name":"Göhler, Simon Moritz","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, A.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"rafnpau","last":"Rafn","name":"Rafn, A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas J.","key":"howardpedh","last":"Howard","name":"Howard, Thomas J.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"eiflerpedh","last":"Eifler","name":"Eifler, Tobias","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4122/dtu:2104","eisbn":["9788774753810"],"pages":"171-175","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the First Internatinal Symposium of Robust Design 2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a1dcc9bd-1d73-4175-b2d2-b431821ade08"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Variation Management Framework (VMF) for Robust Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352872","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Type 2 diabetes is characterized by increased insulin resistance and impaired insulin secretion. Type 2 diabetes is also associated with low-grade inflammation and increased levels of proinflammatory cytokines such as TNF-α. TNF-α has been shown to impair peripheral insulin signaling in vitro and in vivo. However, it is unclear whether TNF-α may also affect endogenous glucose production (EGP) during fasting and glucose-stimulated insulin secretion (GSIS) in vivo. We hypothesized that low-dose TNF- α would increase EGP and attenuate GSIS. Recombinant human TNF-α or placebo was infused in healthy, nondiabetic young men (n = 10) during a 4-hour basal period followed by an intravenous glucose tolerance test (IVGTT). TNF-α lowered insulin levels by 12% during the basal period (P < 0.05). In response to the IVGTT, insulin levels increased markedly in both trials, but there was no difference between trials. Compared to placebo, TNF-α did not affect EGP during the basal period. Our results indicate that TNF-α acutely lowers basal plasma insulin levels but does not impair GSIS. The mechanisms behind this are unknown but we suggest that it may be due to TNF-α increasing clearance of insulin from plasma without impairing beta-cell function or hepatic insulin sensitivity.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ibfelt, Tobias","Fischer, Christian Philip","Plomgaard, Peter","van Hall, Gerrit","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-463294"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Double Blind Method","Glucose","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin","Insulin Secreting Cells","Male","Recombinant Proteins","Signal Transduction","Tumor Necrosis Factor alpha","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the acute effects of low dose tnf α on glucose metabolism and β cell function in humans","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2014/295478","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-463294","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3945645","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84896278072","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24692847","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-74d59772-a2c6-4334-897b-217d6ca5515c"],"keyword":["Adult","Blood Glucose","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Double-Blind Method","Glucose","Glucose Tolerance Test","Humans","Insulin","Insulin-Secreting Cells","Male","Recombinant Proteins","Signal Transduction","Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BEE131DE106062939189F9066A75EF38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1155/2014/295478","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Endocrinology and Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"ibfeltpau","last":"Ibfelt","name":"Ibfelt, Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian Philip","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a17260a4-4ec1-41e8-85be-97659b87b98d","name":"Fischer, Christian Philip","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"plomgaardpau","last":"Plomgaard","name":"Plomgaard, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gerrit","key":"vanhallpau","last":"van Hall","locid":"55a9b111-6dbb-4a42-a9ab-d5f3785fbdae","name":"van Hall, Gerrit","orcid":"0000-0002-2519-8127","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente Klarlund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5d38d54e-e0d1-4397-98ca-6d8c9b78606d","name":"Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24692847"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1155/2014/295478","issn":["09629351","14661861"],"issn_org":["09629351"],"journal":"Mediators of Inflammation","pages":"1-7","paperid":"295478","status":"p","title":"Mediators of Inflammation","volume":"2014"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84896278072"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74d59772-a2c6-4334-897b-217d6ca5515c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Acute Effects of Low-Dose TNF-α on Glucose Metabolism and β-Cell Function in Humans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-463294","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In large B-cell lymphoma (LBCL) MYC- and MYC/BCL2 double-hit (DH) translocations have been associated with inferior survival. We hypothesised that the negative prognostic impact of MYC translocation was determined by an immunoglobulin MYC translocation partner gene (IG-MYC), as opposed to a non-immunoglobulin partner gene (nonIG-MYC). In a prospective, unselected cohort of 237 LBCL patients MYC and BCL2 translocations were identified by fluorescent in situ hybridisation (FISH) with split probes. MYC translocation partner gene was identified by IGH/MYC fusion probes and/or kappa/lambda split probes. Clinical data were collected from patient files. MYC translocation was identified in 28/225 patients. IG-MYC translocation partner gene was identified in 12/24 patients. DH translocation was identified in 23/228 patients. IG-MYC translocation partner gene was identified in 9/19 DH patients. Neither MYC-nor DH translocation showed correlation with survival. However, MYC translocation with IG-MYC translocation partner gene was associated with worse OS compared with both MYC translocation with nonIG-MYC translocation partner gene (P = 0.02) as well as absence of MYC translocation (P = 0.03). In patients with DH a similar, however, stronger correlation was seen (P = 0.003 and P = 0.0004 respectively). MYC - or DH translocation with nonIG-MYC translocation partner gene was not associated with worse overall survival (P = 0.2 and P = 0.3 respectively). Most patients received Rituximab (86%) and CHOP/CHOP-like chemotherapy regimes (81%). We suggest that prognostic stratification of LBCL patients by MYC and/or DH translocations should include identification of MYC translocation partner gene because approximately half of the cases harbour nonIG-MYC translocation partner genes with no or minor influence on survival.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Mette Ø","Gang, Anne O","Poulsen, Tim S","Knudsen, Helle","Lauritzen, Anne F","Nielsen, Signe Lykke","Klausen, Tobias W","Nørgaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-481969"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Genes bcl 2","Genes myc","Humans","Lymphoma Large B Cell Diffuse","Male","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Translocation Genetic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"myc translocation partner gene determines survival of patients with large b cell lymphoma with myc or double hit myc bcl000000000002 translocations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.12212","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-481969","identifier":[{"id":"84890161748","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24118498","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-943028f8-faf4-450f-88d5-3912fbfb1d6f"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Genes, bcl-2","Genes, myc","Humans","Lymphoma, Large B-Cell, Diffuse","Male","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Translocation, Genetic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-174E4D6395AE6DF788D7700DB42D0889"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ejh.12212","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Miljø- og Arbejdsmedicin"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Ø","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ff29766f-2c8a-4c13-bae1-eefe31c6f55b","name":"Pedersen, Mette Ø","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne O","key":"gangpau","last":"Gang","name":"Gang, Anne O","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tim S","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Tim S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Helle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne F","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","name":"Lauritzen, Anne F","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe L","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c44b31e3-2dfd-4051-9bba-6a2540e889eb","name":"Nielsen, Signe Lykke","name_org":"Nielsen, Signe L","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias W","key":"klausenpau","last":"Klausen","name":"Klausen, Tobias W","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24118498"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejh.12212","issn":["09024441","09024506"],"issn_org":["09024441"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Journal of Haematology","pages":"42-48","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Haematology","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84890161748"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-943028f8-faf4-450f-88d5-3912fbfb1d6f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MYC translocation partner gene determines survival of patients with large B-cell lymphoma with MYC- or double-hit MYC/BCL2 translocations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-481969","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The synthesis of all eight rare, but biologically important L-hexoses as the according thioglycosyl donors was achieved through a procedure involving the C-H activation of their corresponding 6-deoxy-L-hexoses. The key steps of the procedure were the silylation of the OH group at C4 followed by an intramolecular C-H activation of the methyl group in g-position; both steps were catalyzed by iridium. The following Fleming-Tamao oxidation and acetylation gave the suitably protected L-hexoses. This is the first general method for the preparation of all eight L-hexoses as their thioglycosyl donors ready for glycosylation and the first example of an iridium-catalyzed C(sp3)-H activation on sulfide-containing compounds.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Frihed, Tobias","Pedersen, Christian Marcus","Bols, Mikael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-508158"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["C H activation","Iridium catalysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synthesis of all eight l glycopyranosyl donors using c h activation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.201408209","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-508158","identifier":[{"id":"84919392302","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25303081","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c0423df9-4c4c-4cfa-8a7a-b5f17d9b6fba"],"keyword":["C-H activation","Fleming-Tamao oxidation","Glycosyl donors","Iridium catalysis","L-hexoses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-323968732386505BDE1D836EE155FD5A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/anie.201408209","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84919392302&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"frihedpau","last":"Frihed","locid":"0227f6b1-da49-463d-9c60-ae7a07fc1729","name":"Frihed, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0001-7647-1894","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Marcus","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"994945e4-c86b-4440-b9bd-8117822c77db","name":"Pedersen, Christian Marcus","orcid":"0000-0003-4661-4895","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael","key":"bolspau","last":"Bols","locid":"23a8a20e-b9f1-4bf5-ae25-3377249ae440","name":"Bols, Mikael","orcid":"0000-0002-6561-6952","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25303081"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/anie.201408209","issn":["14337851","15213773"],"issn_org":["14337851"],"issue":"50","journal":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","pages":"13889-13893","status":"p","title":"Angewandte Chemie International Edition","title_org":"Angewandte Chemie - International Edition","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84919392302"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c0423df9-4c4c-4cfa-8a7a-b5f17d9b6fba"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Synthesis of all eight L-glycopyranosyl donors using C-H activation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-508158","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"High-spatial and energy resolution electron energy-loss spectroscopy (EELS) can be used for detailed characterization of localized and propagating surface-plasmon excitations in metal nanostructures, giving insight into fundamental physical phenomena and various plasmonic effects. Here, applying EELS to ultra-sharp convex grooves in gold, we directly probe extremely confined gap surface-plasmon (GSP) modes excited by swift electrons in nanometre-wide gaps. We reveal the resonance behaviour associated with the excitation of the antisymmetric GSP mode for extremely small gap widths, down to ~5 nm. We argue that excitation of this mode, featuring very strong absorption, has a crucial role in experimental realizations of non-resonant light absorption by ultra-sharp convex grooves with fabrication-induced asymmetry. The occurrence of the antisymmetric GSP mode along with the fundamental GSP mode exploited in plasmonic waveguides with extreme light confinement is a very important factor that should be taken into account in the design of nanoplasmonic circuits and devices.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Raza, Søren","Stenger, Nicolas","Pors, Anders","Stær, Tobias Holmgaard","Kadkhodazadeh, Shima","Wagner, Jakob B.","Pedersen, Kjeld","Wubs, Martijn","Bozhevolnyi, Sergey I.","Mortensen, Niels Asger"],"cuid":["S03-097.17-000914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["cond mat mes hall physics optics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extremely confined gap surface plasmon modes excited by electrons","src":["aau","dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms5125","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The Center for Nanostructured Graphene is sponsored by the Danish National Research Foundation, Project DNRF58. The A. P. Møller and Chastine Mc-Kinney Møller Foundation is gratefully acknowledged for the contribution towards the establishment of the Center for Electron Nanoscopy. N.S. acknowledges financial support by a Lundbeck Foundation grant no. R95-A10663; A.P., T.H., K.P. and S.I.B. acknowledge financial support from the Danish Council for Independent Research (FTP contract no. 09-072949 ANAP)."],"id":"S03-097.17-000914","identifier":[{"id":"84902817968","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000338838400002","type":"wos"},{"id":"24939641","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-118728ee-2c26-42a2-bac7-b9a0146a541e","dtu-8d266303-2dfc-4abb-b9d6-c2c511cb3887","sdu-a756ce99-98c7-4520-b5b3-5ecd79bf86d6"],"keyword":["cond-mat.mes-hall physics.optics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-6A3EC8E252810346028DEF485D4C0825"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms5125","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Structured Electromagnetic Materials"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Physics and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"razapau","last":"Raza","locid":"3ea5ad9a-67fb-45c2-b196-631066e1af1d","name":"Raza, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-0296-7202","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolas","key":"stengerpau","last":"Stenger","locid":"b458470c-3f7f-4b44-a269-eb6e3007c2fe","name":"Stenger, Nicolas","orcid":"0000-0002-6808-9211","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Lambertus","key":"porspau","last":"Pors","locid":"0610a48c-d233-4ffb-93c6-38f66a5f7cc9","name":"Pors, Anders Lambertus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Holmgaard","key":"stærpau","last":"Stær","locid":"f9c73bfe-cf15-440a-9aca-290bb9e2f2a5","name":"Stær, Tobias Holmgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Shima","key":"kadkhodazadehpau","last":"Kadkhodazadeh","locid":"531c5d5a-4