null,"first":"Jesper","key":"lindhardsenpau","last":"Lindhardsen","name":"Lindhardsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Søren Lund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"0ee9531c-28fa-41bc-8eb4-64d8ae7f0fb1","name":"Iversen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1816-4508","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"lastheinpau","last":"Lasthein","locid":"7c73043a-541f-45df-b9aa-7a932f8e3fa3","name":"Lasthein, Stine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"gniadeckipau","last":"Gniadecki","name":"Gniadecki, Robert","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomas Norman","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"6ad0c653-50e3-4ffa-9ba5-b42d6d22a186","name":"Dam, T N","name_org":"Dam, Tomas Norman","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Tobias","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Riis","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Peter Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-9056-535X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22558442"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0036342","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84860431562"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dfc89acd-0556-4c61-b1ea-296acb752763","ku-3e76bcb0-967a-431b-bdb2-bf7f6f63ea92","sdu-04149a57-669d-448d-acb5-4be7bfb28322"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Pharmacological undertreatment of coronary risk factors in patients with psoriasis : observational study of the Danish nationwide registries","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.44-028904","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Many freshwater turtles are extremely tolerant to the lack of oxygen and can survive the winter submerged in anoxic mud in ice-covered lakes. The pronounced anoxia-tolerance resides with a considerable depression of cellular metabolism and the ability to use the shell to buffer the acidosis arising from anaerobic metabolism (1). Infusion of microspheres has shown that the shell receives almost half of the cardiac output in turtles made anoxic at low temperatures (2). However, the vasculature of the turtle shell remains to be described. To visualise the vasculature within the carapace and plastron of the turtle Trachemys scripta, we perfused terminally anaesthetised turtles with different contrast enhancing agents (Microfil [lead n/a]), barium sulphate [250 mg/kg], and iodine [15-250 mg/kg]), and the animals were then scanned by both single source as well as dual energy Computed Tomographic systems, to create three dimensional representations. Dual energy Computed Tomography provided good visual contrast between blood vessels and bony tissue inside the turtle shell due to differences in energy level from the two simultaneously acquired x-ray sources. However, inadequate resolution of the clinical scanners prevented visualisation of the smaller vessels with a diameter below approximately 600 μm. Thus, our technique clearly revealed the larger intracortical vessel embedded in the carapace and plastron of Trachemys, and future studies should seek to determine whether this vascularisation is altered during prolonged anoxia. 1. Jackson, DC. (2011). Life in a shell: a physiologist´s view of a turtle. Harvard University Press, USA. 2. Stecyk, JAW., Overgaard, J., Farrell, AP., Wang, T. (2004). α-Adrenergic regulation of systemic peripheral resistance and blood flow distribution in the turtle Trachemys scripta during anoxia submergence at 5˚C and 21˚C. J. Exp. Biol. 207, 269-283.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Kasper","Thygesen, Jesper","Wang, Tobias","Ullerup, Rita","Pedersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-156335"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-04","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2011-07-01","title":"Society for Experimental Biology, SEB Annual Meeting 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the shell vasculature of trachemys turtles investigated by modern 000000000003d imaging techniques","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebiology.org/meetings/Past_Meetings/Glasgow_2011/Glasgow.html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-156335","ids":["au-2f38f913-946a-4507-ae6e-e5921c46745d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4309233640DE598BF038F8DCFDC89748"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebiology.org/meetings/Past_Meetings/Glasgow_2011/Glasgow.html","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"38a9d794-f230-4f50-9327-a06057880fff","name":"Hansen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8669-8897","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","name":"Thygesen, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias Wang","key":"nielsenpa