{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Pedersen, Ove K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-281592"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"højskolerne den loyale opposition","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-281592","ids":["cbs-41565e02-1798-4c72-b47e-fc745499422d"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0F28FC0E1A8107476BBE62A1D6D5BAD2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Business and Politics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ove K.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a19bd29a-f723-485d-be3b-3d14c852b0bd","name":"Pedersen, Ove K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tobias","key":"beckpedh","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Tobias","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771291360"],"pages":"39-54","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Klim","status":"p","subtitle":"Højskolen til debat 2012","title":"Hvorfor skal hverdagen ligne en slutspurt?"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-41565e02-1798-4c72-b47e-fc745499422d"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Højskolerne - den loyale opposition","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-281592","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"While the overall autonomic regulation of the heart and vasculature of anurans has been studied in some detail, little is known about the role of the adreno- and cholinoreceptors in smooth muscle when looking at resistance in the pulmonary and systemic vessels. Vascular smooth muscle is the primary site of regulation of resistance and therefore holds the capacity to control blood flow and pressure. This vascular control allows amphibians to regulate their shunt, i.e. partially bypassing either the pulmonary or systemic circuit. Shunting in amphibians has been studied due to their multiple respiratory modalities and their ontogeny including fundamental morphological changes during metamorphosis. Here we use wire myography to evaluate how the vascular tone of isolated blood vessels from the pulmocutaneous, pulmonary, cutaneous and systemic segments respond to sympathetic and parasympathetic stimulation. Hence, myography on vessels ranging from 0.2 to 2.0 mm allow for the investigation of isometric response to agonists and antagonists of smooth muscle with no autonomic tone. This provides the possibility of mapping the function of adreno- and cholinoreceptor in vascular regulation in anurans.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pedersen, Pil Birkefeldt Møller","Wang, Tobias","Brøndum, Emil Toft"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-188430"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-04","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2011-07-01","title":"Annual meeting of Society of Experimental Biology, SEB, 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mechanisms of adreno and cholinoreceptors in isolated pulmonary and systemic vasculature of the cane toad rhinella marina","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebiology.org/meetings/Past_Meetings/Glasgow_2011/docs/Abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-188430","ids":["au-677d2e2c-c85a-4dde-a3f3-6bce762302d2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5598244AFA9C15579B23BC68AB512348"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebiology.org/meetings/Past_Meetings/Glasgow_2011/docs/Abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Ecoinformatics and Biodiversity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pil Birkefeldt Møller","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bf10d8f7-5087-4afa-84b7-b252ff9d7357","name":"Pedersen, Pil Birkefeldt Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-8378-4677","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil Toft","key":"brøndumpau","last":"Brøndum","locid":"c6d52a57-ff18-468b-8640-793f97d108e2","name":"Brøndum, Emil Toft","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-677d2e2c-c85a-4dde-a3f3-6bce762302d2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Mechanisms of adreno- and cholinoreceptors in isolated pulmonary and systemic vasculature of the cane toad (Rhinella marina)","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-188430","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Dronedarone restores sinus rhythm and reduces hospitalization or death in intermittent atrial fibrillation. It also lowers heart rate and blood pressure and has antiadrenergic and potential ventricular antiarrhythmic effects. We hypothesized that dronedarone would reduce major vascular events in high-risk permanent atrial fibrillation.","author_count":52,"contributors":["Connolly, Stuart J","Camm, A John","Halperin, Jonathan L","Joyner, Campbell","Alings, Marco","Amerena, John","Atar, Dan","Avezum, Álvaro","Blomström, Per","Borggrefe, Martin","Budaj, Andrzej","Chen, Shih-Ann","Ching, Chi Keong","Commerford, Patrick","Dans, Antonio","Davy, Jean-Marc","Delacrétaz, Etienne","Di Pasquale, Giuseppe","Diaz, Rafael","Dorian, Paul","Flaker, Greg","Golitsyn, Sergey","Gonzalez-Hermosillo, Antonio","Granger, Christopher B","Heidbüchel, Hein","Kautzner, Josef","Kim, June Soo","Lanas, Fernando","Lewis, Basil S","Merino, Jose L","Morillo, Carlos","Murin, Jan","Narasimhan, Calambur","Paolasso, Ernesto","Parkhomenko, Alexander","Peters, Nicholas S","Sim, Kui-Hian","Stiles, Martin K","Tanomsup, Supachai","Toivonen, Lauri","Tomcsányi, János","Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","Tse, Hung-Fat","Vardas, Panos","Vinereanu, Dragos","Xavier, Denis","Zhu, Wei Jun","Zhu, Jun-Ren","Baret-Cormel, Lydie","Husted, Steen"],"cuid":["S02-085.58-026036"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["PALLAS Investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Amiodarone","Anti Arrhythmia Agents","Atrial fibrillation","Atrial flutter","Cardiovascular Diseases","Chronic Disease","Digoxin","Double Blind Method","Drug Therapy Combination","Female","Follow Up Studies","Heart Rate","Heart failure","Hospitalization","Humans","Male","Risk Factors","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Fluid Mechanic