","locid":"9568fb5e-c3f7-4045-ac14-13b8493fcd46","name":"Jeppesen, Jørgen","name_org":"Jeppesen, Jørgen Lykke","rank":50,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22082198"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmoa1109867","issn":["00284793","15334406"],"issn_org":["00284793"],"issue":"24","journal":"The New England Journal of Medicine","pages":"2268-76","status":"p","title":"The New England Journal of Medicine","title_org":"New England Journal of Medicine","volume":"365"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855163167"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b7babad0-090b-4970-9134-73fb9a182fc0","ku-c83d0bd1-e1bb-43b4-ba62-df2d661056a6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dronedarone in high-risk permanent atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.58-026036","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Animal anatomy has traditionally relied on detailed dissections to produce anatomical illustrations, but modern imaging modalities, such as MRI and CT, now represent an enormous resource that allows for fast non-invasive visualizations of animal anatomy in living animals. These modalities also allow for creation of three-dimensional representations that can be of considerable value in the dissemination of anatomical studies. In this methodological review, we present our experiences using MRI, CT and mCT to create advanced representation of animal anatomy, including bones, inner organs and blood vessels in a variety of animals, including fish, amphibians, reptiles, mammals, and spiders. The images have a similar quality to most traditional anatomical drawings and are presented together with interactive movies of the anatomical structures, where the object can be viewed from different angles. Given that clinical scanners found in the majority of larger hospitals are fully suitable for these purposes, we encourage biologists to take advantage of these imaging techniques in creation of three-dimensional graphical representations of internal structures","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lauridsen, Henrik","Hansen, Kasper","Wang, Tobias","Agger, Peter","Andersen, Jonas Lembcke","Knudsen, Peter Skødt","Rasmussen, Anne Staub","Uhrenholt, Lars","Pedersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228225"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inside out modern imaging techniques to reveal animal anatomy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/48531251/journal.pone.0017879_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-228225","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3062562","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"79952982778","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21445356","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ad72c81f-72a7-483e-ba8e-20905b695460"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E419F771BFD09F995E3C3CB3723D2632"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/48531251/journal.pone.0017879_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0017879","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Science, Department of Biological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"e9b42d0f-74e8-4835-92a3-18ce72bfafa6","name":"Lauridsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-8833-4456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"38a9d794-f230-4f50-9327-a06057880fff","name":"Hansen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8669-8897","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tobias","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"7a3d91ab-5dbf-46e4-bc6e-634e16bd8d80","name":"Wang, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0002-4350-3682","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"aggerpau","last":"Agger","locid":"d2d20d5f-a4c1-484c-980c-0fc1b52bad0c","name":"Agger, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-7338-6624","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Lembcke","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8690d766-d820-4275-b927-57aec6851dc4","name":"Andersen, Jonas Lembcke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Skødt","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"56334ee4-82c8-4d7d-a22c-4bd7d8a44f52","name":"Knudsen, Peter Skødt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Staub","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"da63e6b3-5ecd-4c95-9bae-3b1727f4aea6","name":"Rasmussen, Anne Staub","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"uhrenholtpau","last":"Uhrenholt","locid":"3fdbbf4d-7b71-451b-b15e-928ae109fcab","name":"Uhrenholt, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2823-3995","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"871199c4-33bb-4fac-95ef-9a2266f30695","name":"Pedersen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1146-0382","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21445356"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0017879","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"3","journal":"PLOS ONE","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952982778"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ad72c81f-72a7-483e-ba8e-20905b695460"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Inside Out: Modern Imaging Techniques to Reveal Animal Anatomy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228225","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"center dot General use of hormone replacement therapy (HRT) dropped drastically after 2002 when pivotal randomized trials showed increased risk of coronary artery disease and other complications with HRT. center dot HRT is not recommended for primary or secondary prevention of coronary heart disease and guidelines recommend discontinuation of HRT after myocardial infarction (MI). center dot It is unknown whether women actually discontinue HRT after MI. WHAT THIS STUDY ADDS center dot Women who use HRT when they experience their MI generally continue using HRT. center dot We found a remarkably low increase in discontinuation after 2002, in contrast to the general drop in use of HRT. AIM To characterize the pattern of use and discontinuation of postmenopausal hormone replacement therapy (HRT) in women with myocardial infarction (MI) before and after 2002, where the general use of HRT dropped drastically subsequent to the results of the Women's Health Initiative trial. METHODS All Danish women aged >= 40 years hospitalized with MI in the period 1997 to 2005 and their use of HRT were identified by individual-level-linkage of nationwide registers of hospitalization and drug dispensing from pharmacies. Characteristics associated with HRT use at time of MI and subsequent HRT discontinuation were analysed by multivariable logistic regression. RESULTS In the study period, 34 778 women were discharged after MI. Of these, 3979 (11.4%) received HRT at the time of MI and their most used categories of HRT were vaginal oestrogen and oral oestrogen alone (46.6% and 28.7%, respectively). The percentage of women who continued HRT during the first year after discharge was 85.0% in the period 2000-2002 and had decreased to 79.6% in the period 2003-2005. Vaginal oestrogen use was associated with overall discontinuation of HRT (odds ratio [OR] 1.37, 95% confidence interval [CI] 1.10, 1.72), whereas use of oral oestrogen alone and use of oral cyclic combined oestrogen/progestogen were associated with change of HRT after MI (OR 2.33, 95% CI 1.10, 4.93 and OR 2.94, 95% CI 1.35, 6.39, respectively). CONCLUSION The majority of women experiencing an MI during ongoing HRT continued HRT after discharge and this pattern of HRT use did not change markedly after 2002.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bretler, Ditte-Marie","Hansen, P. R.","Abildstrom, S. Z.","Jorgensen, C. H.","Sorensen, R.","Hansen, M. L.","Schramm, Tina Ken","Lokkegaard, E.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","Gislason, Gunnar Hilmar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765997"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use and discontinuation of hormone replacement therapy in women with myocardial infarction a nationwide study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2010.03790.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765997","identifier":[{"id":"78650055203","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3969cd07-776c-45c1-8742-9543eb75bba1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-973D6251B8A537AA30A0251DA323E9A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2010.03790.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Register/Ulykker/Hjerter"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte-Marie","key":"bretlerdittemariepau","last":"Bretler","name":"Bretler, Ditte-Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"P. R.","key":"hansenprpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, P. R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S. Z.","key":"abildstromszpau","last":"Abildstrom","locid":"8c578136-f71b-4f74-8f79-c0adef021924","name":"Abildstrom, S. Z.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"C. H.","key":"jorgensenchpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, C. H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"sorensenrpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M. L.","key":"hansenmlpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, M. L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina Ken","key":"schrammtinakenpau","last":"Schramm","name":"Schramm, Tina Ken","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"lokkegaardepau","last":"Lokkegaard","name":"Lokkegaard, E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Tobias","key":"torppedersenchristiantobiaspau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian Tobias","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar Hilmar","key":"gislasongunnarhilmarpau","last":"Gislason","name":"Gislason, Gunnar Hilmar","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1365-2125.2010.03790.x","issn":["02643774","03065251"],"issn_org":["03065251"],"issue":"1","journal":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","pages":"105-115","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-78650055203"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3969cd07-776c-45c1-8742-9543eb75bba1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Use and discontinuation of hormone replacement therapy in women with myocardial infarction: a nationwide study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765997","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"An MR-electrophysiology (EP) catheter is presented that provides full diagnostic EP functionality and a high level of radiofrequency safety achieved by custom-designed transmission lines. Highly resistive wires transmit intracardiac electrograms and currents for intracardiac pacing. A transformer cable transmits the localization signal of a tip coil. Specific absorption rate simulations and temperature measurements at 1.5 T demonstrate that a wire resistance > 3 kΩ/m limits dielectric heating to a physiologically irrelevant level. Additional wires do not increase tip specific absorption rate significantly, which is important because some clinical catheters require up to 20 electrodes. It is further demonstrated that radiofrequency-induced and pacing-induced resistive heating of the wires is negligible under clinical conditions. The MR-EP catheters provided uncompromised recording of electrograms and cardiac pacing in combination with a standard EP recorder in MR-guided in vivo EP studies, and the tip coil enabled fast and robust catheter localization. In vivo temperature measurements during such a study did not detect any device-related heating, which confirms the high level of safety of the catheter, whereas unacceptable heating was found with a standard EP catheter. The presented concept for the first time enables catheters with full diagnostic EP functionality and active tracking and at the same time a sufficient level of radiofrequency safety for MRI without specific absorption rate-related limitations.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Weiss, Steffen","Wirtz, Daniel","David, Bernd","Krueger, Sascha","Lips, Oliver","Caulfield, Dennis","Pedersen, Steen Fjord","Bostock, Julian","Razavi, Reza","Schaeffter, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-249924"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London"],"keyword":["Animals","Burns Electric","Catheter ablation","Electrophysiologic Techniques Cardiac","Equipment Design","Equipment Failure Analysis","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Radio Waves","Swine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in vivo evaluation and proof of radiofrequency safety of a novel diagnostic mr electrophysiology catheter","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.22669","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-249924","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3715087","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"79951836656","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21337409","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d3249e07-ac44-451e-b980-b73ab7d694d5"],"keyword":["Animals","Burns, Electric","Catheter Ablation","Electrophysiologic Techniques, Cardiac","Equipment Design","Equipment Failure Analysis","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Radio Waves","Swine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FC3F3F66389E4296906B3409FB4A55F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mrm.22669","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"king s college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","